Three Ministries Understand and Discuss Addressing Challenges of Rural People to Promote Rural Development
(Phnom Penh): Three Ministries, including the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and the Ministry of Rural Development, held the first tripartite meeting to study and understand common issues to discuss and address people's challenges. In rural areas, most of which depend on agriculture.
The first meeting was held at the Ministry of Agriculture this morning, May 6, 2024, with the participation of the three Ministers, including Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Tho Chetha. Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology and Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development.
Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Dith Tina said in this meeting that this is the first meeting but not the last, as the three ministries will hold a series of meetings every three months. It is necessary to take turns in each ministry to make the cooperation between the three ministries better and more effective for the benefit of the rural people.
He added that cooperation between the three ministries is very important because the rural development sector has a lot to do with agriculture because most of the rural economy depends on agriculture. And agriculture also depends on water resources. Therefore, the three ministries should have a joint plan to put together the means and resources to promote development in rural areas.
