Weeks ago! Police arrest more than 400 people in connection with crimes
(Phnom Penh): The operation to crack down on drug trafficking and use, criminal offenses, gangs and gambling is actively carried out by the National Police Force throughout the country. In fact, in the past week from April 29 to May 5, 2024, authorities within the Ministry of Interior arrested a total of 467 crime suspects across the country.
Mr. Touch Sok (Sok), Deputy Spokesman of the Ministry of Interior, said that among the total number of suspects arrested by the National Police from the General Commission to the Commune / Sangkat Administration Post, 259 were involved in 107 drug crimes. 93 people were involved in 57 general criminal offenses, 85 were involved in gang cases and 30 were involved in illegal gambling offenses.
Cracking down on drug trafficking and use is one of the six priority tasks that Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior Abhisit Bandit Sar Sokha announced to increase attention from the beginning of the seventh legislature of the National Assembly. The government has also been actively implementing anti-drug campaigns across the country.
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathi Hun Manet, on the afternoon of May 6, 2024, announced the provision of military service to the relatives of the 20 soldiers who were killed in the bombing incident in the 3rd Military Zone. Kampong Speu.
Samdech Thipdey's announcement after Samdech saw the message of a young man named Chea Samnang Raksmey Satya, the son of Major General Chea Samnang, a soldier who was killed in a bombing incident who wanted to join the army from his father They.
Prime Minister Hun Manet posted the message: "I saw the message of Chea Samnang Raksmey Satya, the son of Lieutenant Colonel Chea Samnang, a soldier who was killed in the bombing incident in the 3rd Army Zone. In the ranks of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to succeed his father. I agree with the request of my nephew Reaksmey Satya.
Please be informed that the bombing incident in the 3rd Army Zone in Kampong Speu Province on Saturday afternoon, April 27, 2024 caused 20 soldiers to be killed and some soldiers were injured.
(Kampong Speu): Good news! The TARAL garment factory in Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province, along National Road 3 km 46, needs more than 6,000 workers, now more than 3,000. This was confirmed by the factory owner in front of Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, as he led the officials to visit and find out about the production chain at this factory on the morning of May 6, 2024.
During a face-to-face inspection inside the factory, Mr. Vy Samnang confirmed that the factory was comfortable to sew in air conditioners. If the area has a large number of workers gathered, the factory will deliver directly, but no travel expenses will be deducted.
According to the provincial governor of Kampong Speu, the factory exports garments to the European Union and the United States, and daily exports are unhindered, with only insufficient production to meet demand.
The plant was operational in November 2023.
