Thirty families in Svay Chrum district grow all kinds of vegetables to supply the local market and sell in Phnom Penh
(Svay Rieng): Residents of Trabek and Khmat villages, Svay Chrum commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province, grow a variety of natural vegetables for sale at Svay Chrum market and other markets, earning extra income from farming and having a better life. Before.
Farmer Prohm Saran, who grows vegetables for sale, said that his family, as well as other villagers, turned to growing mixed vegetables in almost every house and cut vegetables to sell to the market, including builders. Then there are those who sell their own vegetables.
Ms. Bun Pheap stated that in this vegetable business, her family's life has been improved to a certain extent, and not only that, she can raise fish in a pond that grows vines. As for farming, his family still works normally, just adding vegetables to the farm work, because the land around the house is empty, only growing vegetables to eat and sell for some money.
Regarding growing vegetables from farmers in Svay Chrum district, Mr. Touch Sek, director of the Svay Chrum district agriculture office, said that there are 30 families growing mixed vegetables in Trabek and Khmat villages, and they sell them at Svay Chrum market. Also a reseller community.
He added that because of this vegetable growing technique, they have learned techniques from agriculture to apply to their cultivation work because of the current challenges due to climate change, that is, the extreme heat makes people Farmers do not get good yields, the sky is very hot and their vegetables need water.
In addition, farmers also asked the authorities as well as the competent authorities to help prevent as well as reduce the import of vegetables from abroad, which makes local vegetables sell cheaper and promote local vegetables so that farmers have the courage. In further cultivation. CRC Svay Rieng Branch Distributes Relief to 36 Families Affected by Windstorms
(Svay Rieng): At least 36 families in Svay Chrum, Kampong Ror and Chantrea districts of Svay Rieng province were affected by strong winds on May 5, 2024.
Seeing the hardships of such people, the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Svay Rieng province, led by Mrs. Duong Vanna, Honorary President and Mrs. Pov Sopheap, the treasurer, visited and brought humanitarian donations to distribute on time.
Ms. Duong Vanna sent a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the affected people, who are always concerned about the well-being of the people and urge to solve people's problems at all times. And everywhere.
At the same time, the Cambodian Red Cross and Red Cross Branch in Svay Rieng Province expressed their regret for the damage to property and houses caused by this unexpected natural disaster.
She also instructed the local authorities to cooperate in helping to rehabilitate the houses of the affected people as a shelter for them to stay, and to be very careful about personal and family safety by turning off the television. Find a safe place when it is raining, which can be dangerous due to lightning or strong winds.
