Police Arrest 5 Robbers and 7 Beneficiaries in Kambol District
(Phnom Penh): The police force of Kambol district, in cooperation with the police of Po Sen Chey district, arrested 5 suspects out of a total of 7 motorcycle robbers. After a motorcycle robbery incident occurred on April 23, 2024 at around 22:00 pm in front of Meprey, National Road 4, Snguon Pich Village, Sangkat Kantouk, Khan Kampol, Phnom Penh.
The seven suspects include:
Kambol district police said that on April 23, 2024, at around 5:30 pm, the victim was riding a motorbike back from visiting his daughter's house in Ang Snoul district, Kandal province. When they arrived at Meprey point, Snguon Pich village, Sangkat Kantouk, Khan Kambol, suddenly 4 suspects riding 2 black Honda C125 motorcycles with license plates and license plates came close and then kicked the victim's motorcycle. Caused to fall and lift the victim's motorcycle to escape.
The victim then went to file a complaint at the Kantouk Administrative Police Station. On April 24, 2024, at about 1 o'clock, the victim searched the motorcycle on the GPS and saw it jumping around the village of Po Prak Cheung, Sangkat Kakap I. He then reported to the administrative police station to arrest a suspect named Duong Vichet and the victim's motorcycle there and then took him to the Kantouk administrative police station for questioning.
Police said that when questioned, the suspect, Thun, admitted that he had sold a motorcycle to No for only $ 700, for which he had paid $ 90 to two people named Sna. The force then proceeded to arrest the other remaining faction member, Phoun Chamroeun alias No, who was standing on the sidewalk in Borey Andong village, Sangkat Tropeam Krasaing, Khan Por Sen Chey.
When questioned, the suspect, Phoun Chamroeun, confessed that he and his accomplices, Son Panha, Cheat and Nuth, actually stole one of the motorcycles.
