Ministry of Water Resources announces weather conditions in Cambodia for May 6, 2024
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia for May 6, 2024.
Low pressure over the Gulf of Thailand, the Kingdom of Cambodia, the central Mekong Basin and the South China Sea.
1. Lowland area: * Minimum temperature 25 ° C and maximum temperature 36 ° C. Winds from the southeast and southwest average 2.5 meters per second. Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap, Battambang, Pursat, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Cham, Svay Rieng, Prey Veng, Kandal and Phnom Penh are likely to experience rain with thundershowers and gusts covering 20% of the area.
2. Upland areas: * Minimum temperature 24 ° C and maximum temperature 37 ° C. Winds from the west and southwest have an average speed of 3.5 m / s. Oddar Meanchey, Pailin, Preah Vihear, Stung Treng, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Tbong Khmum, Kratie and Cardamom mountain areas may receive rain with thunder and gust covering 25% of the area.
