Vanda Institute Holds Graduation Ceremony for More Than 5,000 Students
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Sunday, May 5, 2024, Vanda Institute organized a graduation ceremony for more than 5,000 of its students after they successfully graduated.
The graduation ceremony was presided over by Dr. Heng Vanda, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Vanda Institute and Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Higher Education Association.
The total number of graduates is 5,214, 4,762 of whom are female. The graduates graduated in the 2021-2023 academic year at Phnom Penh, Siem Reap and Battambang. There are 38 undergraduate students of Dr. Heng Vanda, 32 females.
Dr. Heng Vanda expressed his pleasure and congratulations to all students who have worked hard to study, absorb knowledge until success. Dr. also joined in the congratulations with the students' families and highly appreciated the parents and families of all students who persevered and provided all the possibilities for their children's education until successful graduation.
Dr. considered the graduation of this student as a great success in life mission and also an achievement born of the struggle of the individual and strong support from parents and family.
On that occasion, Dr. Heng Vanda also reminded all the winning students about the values of peace. He said that the peace achieved by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate and former Prime Minister, is the most important element, giving people the opportunity to live in peace and for all students to absorb knowledge as capital. For life.
In this regard, Dr. Heng Vanda calls on all students to know how to maintain this peace. Keeping peace is like taking care of yourself.
In addition to highlighting the values of peace, Dr. Heng Vanda also mentioned the Funan Techo canal project. In front of more than 5,000 students, he highlighted that the canal project is important for Cambodia's national economy and trade. In particular, the transportation of goods from the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port to the sea and continue to international markets.
On behalf of the professors and students of Vanda Institute, Dr. Heng Vanda announced his strong support for the construction of the Funan Techo canal project. Dr. Proclamation strongly opposes any evil ideas that attempt to disrupt this project.
Please note that Vanda Institute is a private higher education institution that currently has 3 locations in operation, one in Phnom Penh and two in Siem Reap and Battambang.
Based on this, in order to strengthen the sustainability, efficiency and quality of education services, Vanda Institute has implemented and has a clear vision to continue to improve the quality of the internal management system, strengthen the quality of professors, strengthen the discipline of students in order to implement better in line. By current standards of training and the job market.
