Senior officials of the Ministry of Rural Development solve the problem of water shortage and daily drinking water in 2 districts of Kandal province
(Kandal): The people of Kandal Stung and Saang districts affected by the lack of water for daily consumption during the dry season were immediately requested by Mrs. Chi Thavy, Director of the Department of Rural Development, to the Ministry for emergency assistance. Immediately after receiving the request, Ms. Lim Muy Leng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, this weekend addressed the issue immediately.
The locations inspected were Trapeang Chak village, Thmey village, Thmey commune, Rong Ko village, Trea commune, Kandal Steung district and Kampong Trea village, Saang Phnom commune, Prek Reang (A) village, Teuk Vil commune and Andong village, Kraing Yov commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
On that occasion, Ms. Lim Muy Leng continued to meet with the people and inspect the condition of water sources that have dried up, lack of drinking water and drinking water due to climate change factors, including: wells, sewers and O-We community water production station ( OV) and inspect the work of digging water wells.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Rural Development said that the current inspection of water supply sources is in response to the current situation that the world is experiencing a crisis of climate change, as well as in Cambodia this year, the weather. The drought is heating up, which is worrying about experiencing severe drought, which could leave rural people short of water.
The Secretary of State advised the technical working group of the Department to continue to pay close attention to solving and finding water sources to distribute to the people urgently in situations where people lack water for daily use. Received water on time and thanked the leaders of the Ministry, provincial leaders and technical team who came to help them in time.
(Phnom Penh): 142 students have successfully completed their bachelor's and master's degrees from the American University of Phnom Penh (AUPP), one of the top universities in Cambodia, offering two degree programs.
The graduation ceremony was held on May 4, 2024 under the high presidency of HE Dr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, as well as more than 500 participants, professors, parents and guardians.
All 142 students have completed Bachelor's and Master's degrees in both undergraduate and advanced degree programs in various fields such as architecture, business, engineering, civil engineering, global affairs, information technology management, tourism law, telecommunications and information technology, and master's degrees. . Among them are six foreign students from the United States, Korea, France, China and Russia.
Prof. Dr. Raymond Leos, Rector of Academic Affairs and Student Affairs, shared his personal experience and encouraged graduates to overcome all subsequent obstacles to success and contribute to positive change in society, especially to continue to focus on their goals. Be yourself and enjoy the achievements every day to have a better and happier life.
Prof. Dr. Leos said, "All the successful students have successfully completed the United States curriculum based on the culture and civilization of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Southeast Asia." "Success today is about your dreams and your determination."
On that solemn occasion, HE Dr. Chea Vandeth gave some key recommendations to the graduating students and considered them as the future pillars of Cambodia. He added that more and more young Cambodians are voting. Domestically and internationally, there are many AUPP graduates.
AUPP offers undergraduate and advanced degree programs in Architecture, Business, Civil Engineering, Civil Affairs, Global Affairs, Information Technology Management, Tourism Law, Telecommunications and Information Technology.
