(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ung Kongkea led a delegation from the charity Quantum to donate $ 20,000 to Kantha Bopha Hospital to support the hospital's activities, which examine and treat more than 1 million children every year.
The handover ceremony took place on the morning of May 3, 2024 at Kantha Bopha II Hospital in the presence of Dr. Denis Laurent, Director General of Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Ung Kongkea, President of Quentum Charitable Organization, said, "On behalf of Quentum Charity, we would like to express our deep respect to the doctors and nurses of Kantha Bopha Hospital who have taken all their physical and mental treatment." Lots of pediatric patients every year.
Mr. Ung Kongkea said that in the past we have seen many enterprises and institutions donate money to help Kantha Bopha Hospital. We would like to contribute to support this noble humanitarian activity.
He said that since the Quantum Charitable Organization was recently established and its resources were limited, he would like to make the first donation of 20,000 US dollars to Kantha Bopha Hospital. Although this amount is not much, it shows our enthusiasm and support for Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Please, Director General of Kantha Bopha Hospital, please accept these funds to be used in the hospital's mission to save more patients' lives.
Dr. Denis Laurent, Director General of Kantha Bopha Hospital, thanked the delegates of the Quantum Charity for donating funds to support the hospital's activities.
At present, Kantha Bopha Hospital has 5 branches located in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap province. The hospital has a total of 2,680 staff and doctors who see and treat more than 2,000 children a day. The examination and treatment are free and of the same standard as the hospitals in Singapore, China.
He said that Kantha Bopha Hospital spends $ 42 million a year, receiving more than 20,000 pediatric patients a year. In total, more than 1 million children are examined and treated each year.
He hopes that the donation of Quantum Charity today will be a good example for companies, enterprises and other philanthropists to donate money to support Kantha Bopha Hospital.
He added that Kantha Bopha Hospital treats pediatric patients without discrimination. Foreign children in Cambodia can also come to Kantha Bopha Hospital for treatment with the same quality, but the hospital does not have beds. No VIPs are equal. Spokesman for the Ministry of Interior: 70 people were arrested for criminal and drug offenses on May 4 yesterday
