(Phnom Penh): Senior officials of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries have encouraged farmers with small plots of land who want to engage in commercial farming to be united as a community, use the land as a common production, and come together to find a common management system to encourage Their farming is as lucrative as those with large plots of land.
Khim Finang, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Agriculture, said that currently there are about 2 million Cambodian farmers with about 1 hectare of agricultural land per family. If a farmer per family owns only one hectare of land and wants to farm commercially for a higher profit, it will be difficult and difficult to compete in the market because of high production costs.
However, he said that these small groups of farmers would be able to farm at lower costs and be able to make as much profit as those with large tracts of land commercially through community cohesion. Agriculture. That is why the Ministry encourages farmers with small families to unite as a modern farming community.
He further explained that small farmers would simply move from family farming to mobilization, and their costs would fall.
