The Minister of Health urges all doctors in the public sector and especially the private sector to pay more attention to taking responsibility for the lives of the people.
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, requested all doctors in the public sector and especially the private sector to pay more attention to taking responsibility for people's lives and to strengthen the provision of Health services with professional ethics in accordance with health norms.
This statement was made by Professor Chheang Ra on the occasion of presiding over the opening ceremony of the 3rd workshop of the Association of Newborn Doctors under the theme "START4NEWBORN-Rescue of Newborns" and the awarding ceremony of medals to the leadership. Health officials who have completed their work organized by Calmette Hospital on May 4, 2024.
The purpose of this workshop is to train and share new experiences with doctors, midwives and nurses related to rescuing newborns in a timely and efficient manner, as well as sending sick babies to the hospital. Properly safe. Capital, healthy people, high quality of life are the nation's most valuable assets.
According to the Cambodian Demographic and Health Survey, the infant mortality rate in Cambodia has dropped significantly from 37 per 1,000 live births in 2000 to just eight. Out of 1,000 births live in 2021-2022. This is a great achievement of the Ministry of Health as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Taking this special opportunity, the Minister gave the following recommendations to contribute to reducing infant mortality in Cambodia:
Referral of a baby with a problem to another hospital should have the baby in stable condition before referral and must be contacted to that hospital and enclosed in a referral filled out. Every corner.
* Participants in today's workshop are trainers to apply this knowledge in their workplace and to share it with their colleagues.
* The public sector, and especially the private sector working in obstetrics, must also pay attention to training its doctors and staff to understand the rescue of the baby.
Finally, the Minister strongly hopes that this workshop will contribute to the development of the health sector, especially the well-being of the baby in Cambodia to improve from year to year and wish the workshop success. High.
On that occasion, Professor Minister presented 38 medals to the leaders, civil servants and health workers of Calmette Hospital and members of the Cambodian Pediatric Association to encourage outstanding health officials. Work, dedicate time, physical and mental energy with a high sense of responsibility in the past.
