(Tbong Khmum): The Cambodian cleaning campaign has encouraged participants to come out and collect plastic waste properly at the local level, especially to strengthen the movement to reduce the use of plastic.
Mr. Try Pov, Chief of Preah Theat Commune, said that the joint activities now after the people, especially students and teachers and people participated in the campaign to reduce the use of plastic initiated by the Ministry of Environment. Past. Local authorities are committed to keeping homes clean and littering.
Please note that the Cambodian clean-up mechanism is the next step of the Ministry of Environment's campaign to reduce the use of plastics, which is set in line with the environmental chakra strategy, focusing on three strategic angles: cleanliness, greenness and sustainability. The Cambodian Clean Campaign is a cross between cell cleanliness, cleanliness, cleanliness and cleanliness in Cambodia, focusing on three priority activities:
First. Villagers set out to clean up the environment at the same time to make schools, streets, public areas, community areas, tourist places clean and free of plastic bags and plastic pollution.
Second. Participants collected and stored plastic waste properly at the designated places for the authorities to send to the collection service to be transported to the field, and in particular reduced the amount of waste to be dumped at the field to some extent.
And third. We collect the waste and recycle it in the next step. No, it is the foundation for Cambodia, for the beauty of Cambodia.
The Minister said that the reason why the campaign to reduce the use of plastic from school students is to promote a change in the inner mindset of our students. If he starts reducing the use of plastic bags now, in the future, when he grows up, has a wife, children and grandchildren, they will stop using plastic bags forever.
