(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia for May 5, 2024.
Low pressure covers the Gulf of Thailand, the Kingdom of Cambodia, the central Mekong Basin and the South China Sea, the ministry said. This situation will make: From 5 to 7 May 2024:
1. Lowland area: * Minimum temperature 26 ° C and maximum temperature 38 ° C. Winds from the southeast and southwest average 2.5 meters per second. The southeastern part of Svay Rieng, Prey Veng, Kandal and Kampong Cham provinces will receive rain with thunder, lightning and gust covering 15% of the area.
2. Upland areas: * Minimum temperature 26 ° C and maximum temperature 39 ° C. Winds from the west and southwest average 2.5 meters per second. The northern part of Preah Vihear, Stung Treng and northeastern provinces of Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri and Kratie are likely to receive rain with thundershowers and gusts over 25%.
