This lecture was made to disseminate information related to the Funan Techo canal project to the Cambodian people, as well as to dispel corrupt information inspired by Vietnamese scholars as well as opposition politicians led by Sam Rainsy.
As the beginning of the lecture, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol highlighted the mission of the new Royal Government of Samdech Hun Sen Manet to turn the country into a high-income country by 2050. In order to stimulate the national economy to achieve this goal, attracting foreign investors is an important task.
Mr. Sun Chanthol claimed that Samdech President Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, always visits the country to highlight the potential of investment in Cambodia. For Sun Chanthol, the potential that Cambodia has always highlighted is a peaceful, stable macroeconomic situation, a young workforce, a transport network with a flexible policy and favorable business practices.
Regarding this investment, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, Chief of Staff of Samdech Hun Manet on Investment Affairs, highlighted that Cambodia currently has roads, railways and roads, but Cambodian waterways are not yet interconnected, especially the lack of waterways connecting Rivers and seas, which are why trade and competition remain difficult.
According to Mr. Sun Chanthol, seeing such problems, only in 2021, when Samdech Techo Hun Sen, when he was the Prime Minister, led the Royal Government, he ordered a study to open a water transport network connecting rivers and seas in Cambodia.
After receiving the order, Mr. Sun Chanthol, then Minister of Public Works and Transport, conducted a detailed 26-month study with a total of 48 national and international technicians.
In that lecture, Mr. Sun Chanthol explained in detail the technical characteristics, environmental impact and economic benefits. Mr. Sun Chanthol claimed that this Funan Techo canal was a canal that existed in the Funan period to serve transportation at that time. However, due to the evolving situation of territorial administration as well as conflicts from one generation to the next, especially in the Chenla water and Chenla period, this canal was abandoned until today.
According to Mr. Sun Chanthol, this canal does not cause the river to flow into the sea or the sea water flows into the river due to the construction of the dam up to 3 stages and the flow of the river from the Bassac River is very small. Currently, the Mekong River flows into the sea through Vietnam at its highest level.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also explained that the river did not affect the biodiversity or water regime of the river, but instead increased the fish production along the canal for the benefit of the people. The canal will also be a place for tourism.
More specifically, this Funan Techo canal makes the transportation of goods from Phnom Penh Autonomous Port to the Khmer Sea faster than transporting by Vietnam up to more than 100 km, reducing the cost of transportation and operations by nearly $ 200 per container. Will ship via Vietnam. By reducing costs, Cambodia increases its competitive advantage.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol has confirmed that he will work to push for the project to be officially opened by the end of 2024.
After explaining the technology and benefits that will be gained from the canal for more than an hour, the Deputy Prime Minister also opened the opportunity for participants to ask a lot of questions.
After listening to this explanation, the participating civil servants, professors and students became more aware of the benefits of the Prek Chik Funan Techo project. They applauded and strongly supported the project to connect the necessary waterways for this national economy.
Please note that Prek Fun-Techo project is a project to connect waterways between rivers to the sea of Cambodia, passing through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep, about 180 kilometers long. The project is expected to cost about $ 1.7 billion and has been studied in detail for about 26 months. The project has a water depth of only 5.4 meters.
Prek Chik Funan-Techo was highlighted by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of Cambodia, with at least four interests, including:
Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet has confirmed that the project will begin construction in late 2024 or early 2025. Military sends two Thais to court after arresting drug traffickers in Poipet
(Banteay Meanchey): The Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie Base Force, led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, the Municipal Gendarmerie Local Commander, conducted two separate drug busts and arrested two suspects in Poipet City.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro, Commander of the Municipal Gendarmerie Base, said that at 4 o'clock on May 3, 2024, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie received information from security that there was a case of drug trafficking in front of the building. O'Promden is located in O'Chrov Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City.
Immediately, the force arrived at the scene and arrested a suspect named Pich Khum Doeun, 38 years old, a Thai national, currently living in a rented house in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province. Exhibits include 2 bags of red round tablets (WY).
Then, at 2 o'clock, the Municipal Gendarmerie received information from security that there was a case of storing and using drugs in front of MEX CLUB Club in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City.
After being arrested and interrogated, the suspect, Pich Khum Doeun, alias Pie, admitted that he had actually bought drugs to sell and used for himself. The suspect, Prasit Chhamnan Moeung, alias Fert, admitted that he had actually stored and used illegal drugs.
Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the local force of the Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure. Colonel Chea Dara, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of anti-drug work, said that the crackdown was ordered by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie and coordinated the procedure from him. Born Vannareth, a prosecutor with the provincial court.
Currently, the suspect was sent by the Provincial Anti-Drug Office of the Royal Gendarmerie to the Provincial Court this morning, Saturday, May 4, 2024 to follow the procedure.
