Thailand targets 1% cross-border trade growth this year
BANGKOK: The Thai Ministry of Commerce has set a target of 1% cross-border trade growth this year due to political instability in neighboring countries, including armed conflict in Myanmar. According to the Bangkok Post.
Mr Ronnarong said: "Despite the decline in cross-border trade due to challenges such as high inflation, a slowdown in the exchange rate in Laos and the conflict in Myanmar, as well as additional protectionist measures. "As neighboring countries reduce imports and prevent trade deficits, cross-border trade will increase in both total value and exports by 2024."
Armed conflict in Myanmar is raising concerns about further declines in cross-border trade between Thailand and Myanmar. He said the dispute could affect transportation and logistics.
