General Kheng Someth Opens the 8th Generation Border Police Training Course for Border Police Force and Intervention Force in 2024
(Preah Vihear): General Kheng Someth, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police and Commander of the National Police in the 3rd, 4th and 5th Zones on the afternoon of May 2, 2024, attended the opening ceremony of the Border Police Training Course for the Police Force. Land Border Protection and 8th Generation Intervention 2024 at Preah Vihear Provincial Border Police Training School.
General Kheng Someth said that the training was aimed at raising awareness of the inland border police force and intervening in the implementation of highly effective border protection skills.
This training course includes the National Police Discipline Program No. 873 PRK of the Ministry of Interior and Regulation No. 001 PRK of the General Commission of the National Police and the internal regulations of the training course to ensure the effectiveness and efficiency of the training.
The Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police also addressed the officers and police during the training course on the Prek Chik Funan-Techo project, which is a project that serves the great national interest, especially in the socio-economic field in Cambodia.
General Kheng Someth confirmed that the Funan-Techo canal connects the river between the river to the Cambodian sea, passing through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep provinces with a length of 180 kilometers. Funan-Techo canal provides great benefits to Cambodia. Especially in the transportation sector, so we must fully declare our full support for this Funan-Techo canal project to run smoothly and successfully.
At the same time, General Kheng Someth also told all border guards and police officers to be ready to intervene to transport water to the needy people if the drought continues. .
