Istanbul: Turkey said on Friday it would not continue trading with Israel until a ceasefire was reached and humanitarian aid was guaranteed in the Gaza Strip. According to Reuters.
The $ 7 billion-a-year trade suspension is the first by a major Israeli trading partner due to the Israeli-Palestinian conflict in the Gaza Strip.
Turkish Trade Minister Omer Bolat was quoted by Reuters as saying that Israel's "uncoordinated attitude" and the worsening situation in Rafah in the southern Gaza Strip, which Israel has threatened to launch a new offensive, urged. Let Turkey stop all exports and imports.
"We have decided to suspend exports and imports to and from Israel until a permanent ceasefire (in Gaza) is reached and humanitarian aid is allowed without restrictions," said Bolat. Annoying.
He added that Turkey is negotiating "with our Palestinian brothers on alternative arrangements to ensure that they are not affected by this decision."
Last month, Turkey blocked exports of steel, fertilizer and jet fuel from 54 products because Israel refused to allow Ankara to participate in a drone strike operation in the Gaza Strip.
All remaining trade, worth $ 5.4 billion in Turkish exports and $ 1.6 billion in imports from Israel last year, has now been suspended.
Turkish trade data showed that Turkey's major exports to Israel were steel, automobiles, plastics, electronics and machinery, while imports accounted for $ 634 million in fuel last year. According to Reuters.
