Hamas Health Authority: Gaza death toll rises to 34,622
The death toll from the ongoing Israeli offensive in the Gaza Strip has risen to 34,622, the Gaza Health Authority said in a statement on Friday. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on May 3, 2024.
In the past 24 hours, the Israeli army has killed 26 Palestinians and wounded 51 others, bringing the total to 34,622 dead and 77,867 wounded since the Palestinian-Israeli conflict. The current erupted in October last year.
Israel launched a large-scale offensive against Hamas in the Gaza Strip in retaliation for its October 7, 2023, cross-border offensive against southern Israel, when about 1,200 people were killed. Killed and more than 200 were taken hostage. Ministry of Environment: The transfer of power to the sub-national level is to promote the prevention of natural resource crime more effectively
(Phnom Penh): Map showing 73 protected areas of the Ministry of Environment covering an area of more than 7 million hectares in 21 provinces and 111 cities / districts distributed to 21 sub-national administrations During the handover ceremony of the protected area map to the sub-national administration at the Ministry of Environment on May 3, 2024.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, stated at the ceremony that the transfer of power to the sub-national level is to promote the prevention of natural resource crime more effectively in accordance with the four measures that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly. Introduced in the first phase:
First. Promote 100% law enforcement with no exceptions for natural resource crimes.
Third. Collaborate with the National Gendarmerie Command and the Anti-Corruption Unit in addition to previous cooperation with local authorities
And 4th. Promoting reforestation means planting more trees than cutting down to increase forest cover by 60% by 2050.
