Samdech Thep Hun Sen considers the Cambodia Daily's broadcast related to Mr. Kun Nhim as a kind of fake news! (Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, considered the Cambodia Daily's coverage of the allegations made by the President and Mr. Kun Nhim on bribery to delay his retirement until 2028 as false information.
His Excellency Hun Manet made the remarks when he met with about 5,000 journalists at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center to celebrate World Press Freedom Day on May 3, 2024.
"This evening, I was in a meeting when the Cambodia Daily reported that His Excellency Kun Nhim, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, had bribed me," said Hun Manet. "Through my wife, to extend my retirement until 2028, what is the intention?"
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech President Hun Manet meeting with about 5,000 journalists on the afternoon of May 3, 2024 at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center to celebrate World Press Freedom Day.
"The press is the fourth power that, if used properly, is very important for the development of the nation, for maintaining peace, stability and for empowering the people to make decisions, as well as for the Royal Government to set rules," he said. To be effective.
