He added that the three branches of government, the legislature, the executive and the judiciary, were formed to jointly protect the people and develop the nation, and the fourth branch also played an important role in ensuring that all powers Together with the responsibility to serve the people.
He emphasized that all citizens have the right to information, and that freedom of expression is guaranteed through the free giving and receiving of information. Every citizen also has the right to disseminate information, especially in this stage of digital development, one is the journalist, and so this fourth power is in greater demand.
He added that the Royal Government, ministries, institutions at the national and sub-national levels need real, timely and comprehensive information to put in place timely, targeted and effective measures and information from all walks of life.
