The Funan-Techo canal project, which connects the Mekong River to the sea, is a new historical project that will greatly benefit the motherland and the Cambodian people.
This project was approved by the Royal Government of Cambodia for the sixth term in 2023, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and also supported by the new Royal Government led by Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet. Both Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the current President of the Senate, and Samdech Manet, Hun Manet, have pledged their commitment to digging the Funan-Techo canal for economic benefits, especially the connection of Cambodia's rivers and seas. .
