The following is the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The embassies of 6 countries visited the Techo International Airport, as of the beginning of May, the construction was completed more than 72% at a cost of 1,052 million USD
The visit is aimed at highlighting the joint efforts and support of the embassies to be positive about Cambodia's infrastructure development and boost bilateral relations.
Representatives of the six embassies visited the Techo International Airport and the Air Traffic Control Building and praised the meticulous planning and green infrastructure included in the airport design.
Green infrastructure includes: the use of light bulbs in the design of the roof of the station to allow the use of natural light and the installation and use of solar energy.
During the visit, officials from their respective embassies also participated in constructive discussions with project stakeholders and praised the dedication and expertise of the team involved in implementing the project.
Dr. Lim Lina, Vice President of Canadia Group, mentioned the suppliers and contractors from the respective countries of the six embassies that Techo International Airport is participating in for the construction of the project worth a total of $ 133 million.
Dr. Lim Lina stated that CAIC, a joint venture between the Royal Government of Cambodia, welcomes investors from other countries to the Techo International Airport project, while the airport will be ready to welcome travelers from around the world in 2025.
About 17,000 staff and workers are currently working on the project, and construction is now 72.3% complete with a total investment of $ 1.052 billion, of which about $ 340 million through Purchase bonds from banking and financial institutions. Commentary: Cambodia-China uses murals as a bridge to cross-cultural and deepen cooperation
