His Excellency Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the paintings embody the historical and cultural significance of the two countries from the past to the present. His Excellency stated: "Painting has made both of our people aware of the cultural values, history, painting is a great decoration, look at the paintings, they can know the value of each nation. "Paintings do not speak, but can describe what we want of each person."
In conclusion, the selection of paintings by Cambodian and Chinese artists to present to the public to understand the meaning, content, meaning and beauty really reflects the high attention in connecting the hearts of the people of Cambodia and China more. More sticky. Chinese and Cambodian paintings are another new impetus to deepen the hearts and emotions between the people of our two countries.
Participants in the painting exhibition all said the same number of paintings, but more meaningful for the Cambodian-Chinese friendship.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol confirmed this at a press conference in order to explain and present information related to the Funan-Techo Prek Chik project on the morning of May 3, 2024.
On that occasion, the Deputy Prime Minister said that the Prek Chun Funan-Techo project will create jobs for at least 10,000 Cambodians, both in construction and other jobs, as well as technicians of some Cambodian ministries and institutions, and this is an opportunity. Participate in building great achievements in national history for them.
"Both construction and other jobs will employ about 10,000 workers, more than most Cambodians on the Chinese side, but technicians. China can not afford to transport tens of thousands of workers," he said. Travel costs a lot.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said that the project also needs a lot of Cambodian technical experts, as the Ministry of Public Works and Transport has experts in water transport, sea and port, so they will participate in the implementation of this historic project.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, the construction of the Funan-Techo canal project will take four years from 2024 or 2025.
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Keo Remy, Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee (CCHR), said that if the Cambodian authorities do not strictly enforce the law against those who violate Cambodian law, it will make society There is anarchy and do not try to drag in human rights abuses, law enforcement is a strong fence to keep Cambodia's stability.
This statement was made by Senior Minister Keo Remy at a press conference on "Human Rights Situation in Cambodia for 2024" this morning, May 3, 2024.
Senior Minister Keo Remy stressed that if everyone was on the law, it would make society anarchic and asked why the law was made. Therefore, the Cambodian authorities must strictly enforce the law against those who commit illegal acts, which is justified in order to maintain social stability.
In connection with the allegations that the government is persecuting anti-government activists, the chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee has questioned if the court would not have acted illegally. Punish them?
According to Senior Minister Keo Remy, the Royal Government of Cambodia has shown a strong commitment to the protection and promotion of human rights and international cooperation through the ratification and ratification of eight out of nine international human rights treaties. Cambodia has become a prominent and leading country in the region as a party to international human rights treaties.
In addition, he stated that Cambodia has fulfilled its obligations in accordance with the provisions of international human rights treaties and submitted a timely report on national human rights to the United Nations, with the Cambodian Human Rights Committee as its secretary. The Royal Government in the field of human rights to ensure that all citizens have the right to fully exercise their rights.
France estimates that about 150,000 Russian troops died in the war in Ukraine
Russian President Vladimir Putin has claimed in February this year that 180,000 Russian troops have been killed in the war, while the United Kingdom estimates that about 450,000 Russian soldiers have been killed or wounded in Ukraine. Russia invaded Ukraine on February 24, 2022, and it turned into a bloody protracted war in Europe and left Russia facing Western isolation.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron: Scout music is a scout education method that contributes to the development of children and youth to their full potential physically, intellectually and socially.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports and President of the Cambodian National Scouts, stated that Scout music is a method of scout education that contributes to the development of children and youth to their full physical potential. Social, mental and emotional intelligence to become responsible citizens and to become active local members living in the national and international community.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said this on the morning of May 3, 2024, when he presided over the opening ceremony of the first National Scout Band competition held under the theme "Music in Santepheap »with 8 scout groups from 6 capitals / provinces participating, including: 3 groups in Phnom Penh, 1 group in Kandal, 1 group in Siem Reap, 1 group in Oddar Meanchey, 1 group in Koh Kong and Ratanakkiri province has one group.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron continued that the selection of the theme of the first National Scout Band competition under the theme "Music in Peace" is now dedicated to peace, dedicated to spiritual leadership. Doctor of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister and current President of the Senate, who worked hard to unite the nation and bring peace to Cambodia.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister, also took this opportunity to dedicate this glorious achievement to Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An, former President of the Cambodian National Scouts, as well as all the scouts who have sacrificed their physical, mental, spiritual and self-sacrificing energy. In the cause of the Cambodian National Scout Movement and has formed a scout band of all forms and rich in the past.
