(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khim Finang, Undersecretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Agriculture, confirmed that the Ministry of Agriculture is ready to help farmers, especially smallholder families, so that they can be protected from risk. From lack of market, climate change, lack of capital and other challenges.
He emphasized that the recent major policies of the Royal Government, including the deployment of agricultural officials to the commune level, financing programs, price stability and modern farming communities, are to provide additional protection for smallholder farmers. Market capital risk and climate change risk.
He explained, "One of the solutions we can do is to help parents and siblings who are struggling to make ends meet. "First, consider organizing a community, and the Ministry of Agriculture is ready to help parents ensure that they are protected from the risk of lack of markets, climate change, lack of capital or other challenges."
