Responding to questions from the media regarding the comments from the US side, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said that he, on behalf of the Cambodian side, made a presentation to Mr. Wang Winthean, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia, Mr. Wang Yi, Minister of Foreign Affairs; Both Patrick Murphy, US Ambassador to Cambodia, to explain the Funan-Techo canal project in detail.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said that the Chinese side was also concerned about the project along the Mekong River, but when it came to seeing the map and the Cambodian side to explain, it clearly understood and supported this project, the Chinese side has no objection. Other Mekong countries, such as Laos, Thailand and Myanmar, did not object, seeing only the Vietnamese side.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also gave an interview with CNBC International TV and also informed that around the project of Prek Chik Funan-Techo, do not worry about environmental issues, the Cambodian side has studied and inspected for 26 months and completed. .
According to Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, the 1995 Mekong River Agreement states that until the construction project is completed, the signatory countries can come and inspect it directly, but before such construction, they have no right to come and negotiate for an extension or objection. No, because the Funan-Techo canal project is only done on the tributary, and the location along the project is also an old canal that has just been restored and expanded.
