Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun instructs the Anti-Drug Campaign Command to carry out its responsibilities responsibly to eradicate drugs
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, instructed the National and Sub-National Anti-Drug Campaign Command to carry out their duties and responsibilities responsibly in order to Achieve the Royal Government's plan to eradicate drugs, especially the lake clean-up plan, which refers to the purge of all officials not to be involved in drugs.
The introduction of Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun this morning, May 3, 2024, was co-chaired by Mr. Abhisand Bandith Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Deputy Director of the National Authority for Combating Drugs. Meeting to disseminate the action plan on the implementation of the 9th plan to fight against illegal drugs at the Ministry of Interior.
The Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs said, "The plan is to clean up our lake as much as possible, to build more fences and to expand it so that the lake is clean, which is the strategy of Samdech Manet." "Therefore, I hope that the command of the drug campaign will be carried out effectively and responsibly at both the national and sub-national levels in this plan."
In order to contribute to a successful anti-drug plan, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun made the following recommendations:
* First, to continue to implement the spirit of Regulation No. 01 BOP dated February 2, 2024 on strict measures in the fight against illegal drugs in ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations. The General Secretariat must continue to work with the seven commissions to continue discussions with the private sector so that the private sector, together with state institutions, can fight drugs.
* Second, to strengthen the capacity of the Unity Command and the relevant authorities along the border to prevent the transportation of drugs into Cambodia. In case of complex areas need to add specialized officers and equipment.
* Third: Continue to strengthen the management of chemical compounds by paying the utmost attention to any chemicals that can be used in drug processing. At this point, the relevant ministries that directly import the chemicals must be strengthened so that the chemicals do not fall into the hands of criminals.
* Fourth: The Capital-Provincial Unity Command must be committed to eradicating drug use in nightclubs, and this is an absolute position that must be implemented. This should be taken into account in the area around political institutions, economic institutions, tourism, religion and education, and in case of difficult or complicated areas, national intervention assistance should be reported.
* Fifth: Promote educational measures by updating and effective, as well as promoting MoUs with large organizations or associations to cooperate.
* Sixth: Regarding the treatment and rehabilitation work, chaired by Mr. Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, we must promote the establishment of treatment and rehabilitation centers with the participation of the private sector to establish this location. In addition, SOP standards need to be considered to establish the center, while the state must consider the same conditions for the private sector.
* 7th: The Unified Command must mobilize those who use drugs to show up for treatment, which is the best job. Engineering Command, Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Command donated 20 million Riels on the occasion of the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2024
