(Mondulkiri): An elephant went down to drink water from a stream in Phnom Prich Wildlife Sanctuary in Koh Nhek District, Mondulkiri Province and was trapped and could not get out, but was rescued by environmental experts and local authorities.
Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Mondulkiri Province, said on the morning of May 3, 2024 that after finding an elephant trapped in a pond, the environmental officer of the park, WWF, Royal Group and the district authorities cooperated to drag it. The victim elephant came out of the mud.
The provincial governor claimed that after being dragged out of the swamp, officials saw that the elephant had broken his left leg and was currently receiving medical treatment. Experts suspect that the elephant may have disappeared from the Keo Seima area a few days ago.
