After being elected as the President of the Cambodian Artists Association for the sixth mandate, Mrs. Neak Oknha Mao Chamnan, the wife of Oknha Kith Meng, announced her strong commitment to continue to lead the arts to grow strongly and join the Royal Government to Promote the arts and be able to penetrate into the international arena.
(France): Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, on May 2, 2024, attended the opening ceremony of the 2024 Ministerial Meeting of the OECD Council and met with some dignitaries in Paris, France.
In the morning, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn attended the opening ceremony of the 2024 Ministerial Meeting of the Council of Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD). On that occasion, the Secretary-General of ASEAN also delivered a speech to mark the 10th anniversary of the launch of the Southeast Asia Regional Program (SEARP).
In the afternoon of the same day, the ASEAN Secretary-General met with Mr. Taro Kono, Minister of Digital Development of Japan. On that occasion, the two sides exchanged views on strengthening digital cooperation between ASEAN and Japan, as well as other cooperation.
The ASEAN Secretary-General met with Indonesian Coordinating Minister for Economic Affairs Airlangga Hartarto. During the meeting, the two sides discussed the progress of the achievement of priority areas and achievable achievements of the ASEAN Economic Community and other issues.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn met with Mr. Young Tae Kim, Secretary General of the International Transport Forum. On that occasion, the two sides exchanged views on ways and means to strengthen transport links between ASEAN and the global market, as well as sustainable transport solutions and digital innovations in the transport sector.
In the afternoon of the same day, Mr. Kao Kim Hourn met with Ms. Sanhueza Riveros, Deputy Minister for International Economic Relations of the Chilean Ministry of Foreign Affairs. During the meeting, the two sides exchanged views on ways and means to further strengthen cooperation under the ASEAN-Chile Development Partnership, including trade and investment.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said that after the construction of Funan Techo canal, we will be able to avoid water from Stung Prek Tnaot into Prek Chik and will help Phnom Penh and Kandal province no longer flood by avoiding water to In the canal, if we do not need that water, we can open it to flow into the sea. This canal not only helped Cambodia not to sink, but also helped Vietnam not to sink as well due to the floods from Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said, "I have received information from His Excellency the Minister of Water Resources. He has already said that the flood in Phnom Penh is from Stung Prek Tnaot, and His Excellency has prepared a plan to avoid water from the river. Prek Tnaot enters this canal, Funan Techo, so Phnom Penh will no longer sink, Kandal will no longer sink.
Regarding the Funan Techo canal project, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said that the project will not affect Cambodia or Vietnam, instead it will help create new habitats for biodiversity of fish, birds and aquatic animals. Aquatic plants, reptiles and reptiles help sustain the environment, water flow, natural food, reduce floods and droughts, water is always full.
Please note that Prek Fun-Techo project is a project to connect waterways between rivers to the sea of Cambodia, passing through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep, about 180 kilometers long. The project is expected to cost about $ 1.7 billion and has been studied in detail for about 26 months. The project has a water depth of only 5.4 meters.
