(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, expressed his satisfaction with the inauguration of the Toyota Suzuki Group car factory yesterday and further encouraged the company that in addition to producing cars to supply the Cambodian market, it should be manufactured for Export to external markets as well.
Samdech Techo stated that this is the first time that Samdech has received the first delegation of foreign companies at the Senate. He said that this building was built by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk when he was the head. The state and this building will be preserved as history without any demolition or modernization.
Samdech continued that Samdech also watched the live broadcast of the inauguration of Toyota yesterday, Samdech considered that this is an achievement that Cambodia has achieved after the change of leadership from the old generation to the new generation that took place. Right and there is no turmoil or change, on the contrary, there is a process of political stability, economic growth is still going well, and the inauguration of the Toyota plant is proof.
Mr. ICHIRO vowed to work hard to follow the recommendations of the President of the Senate, as well as the Prime Minister yesterday, and to work together to run the plant successfully, he also informed the prince about the history of Toyota. Who came to Cambodia in 1991 in stages:
He also said that yesterday, the Prime Minister introduced the establishment of a human resource training school in Cambodia in the automotive sector.
Oknha Kong Nuon informed Samdech Techo that the inauguration of the factory to assemble this car is another source of pride for Cambodia, because this car is made in Cambodia, it will have a code on the car to confirm that "Made in Cambodia".
Samdech Techo, President of the Senate, recalled the famous history of Toyota, which is present in Cambodia and the Cambodian people have been very supportive for a long time, and when Samdech first arrived in Phnom Penh, there were no Toyota cars left, only tires left. The body of Pol Pot's car was turned into a water pump, leaving only the tires, and later a Japanese company procured the car's metal for processing.
At first, Cambodia used only Russian cars, such as Moscow Vichy Lada Volga, Samdech said that on the occasion of the 10th anniversary of the country's liberation from the Khmer Rouge regime, the government ordered the first 12 Toyota cars to receive. Foreign guests who came to commemorate the tenth anniversary of the liberation of Cambodia from the Khmer Rouge regime after the celebration, these 12 vehicles were distributed to the leaders of that generation to use.
Samdech Techo requested the company to help train human resources in car skills in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government to provide vocational training to 1.5 million young people without paying and provide additional funding.
Samdech Techo wants this factory in Cambodia to produce not only for the Cambodian market, but also to serve the Cambodian market and export to fill the external market.
He pledged to actively participate in implementing the recommendations of the Cambodian leadership, join the Royal Government to increase production and provide vehicle skills training to the people of Cambodia. Samdech Kittipritthbandit Delivers a Message of Thanks to His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia for Donating $ 3,000 to the Cambodian Red Cross in the Second Quarter of 2024
(Phnom Penh): On Friday, May 3, 2024, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, delivered a message of thanks to Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia. The Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross is the most revered person who has donated $ 3,000 to the Cambodian Red Cross for the second quarter of 2024.
