(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khim Finang, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Agriculture, said that the Ministry of Agriculture is currently trying to establish a modern agricultural community to mobilize farmers to work directly with the Ministry to provide farmers with general knowledge. Strong on production, competitive production for easy and comprehensive export.
He said that for the new government, we have a policy to deploy commune agriculture officers to 1,600 communes across the country, while last year we recruited 250 officers and this year to recruit 800 more. And next year will be full.
He added that the commune agriculture officer will help all commune people to work directly with farmers, provide information to farmers about new technical markets and bring back information from farmers such as challenges, farmers' requests to As a topic of direct dialogue between farmers and the Ministry, this is an important policy to push farmers.
He added that in addition, the Ministry of Agriculture plans to establish agricultural communities in the new mandate, which is a community of farmers to grow and hope that through this community, the Ministry will work directly with the community.
(Phnom Penh): Khim Finang, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Agriculture, said that the Minister of Agriculture does not want the agricultural sector to be Cambodia's burden, but wants to become a support for the country's gross domestic product. Cambodia (GDP).
"These are the factors that the Minister of Agriculture has said that the Ministry of Agriculture does not want the agricultural sector to be Cambodia's burden, but wants the agricultural sector to be a sector that directly contributes to Cambodia's GDP," he said. "The ministry strives to add value, efficiency of production, so that the livelihood of farmers can do just that."
He said that for this reason, all cultivation has an economic analysis to make it easier for people to engage in agriculture.
