(Phnom Penh): As the weather seems to be heating up significantly, Boeung Keng Kang district authorities continue to take care to use measures to prevent and prevent heat waves to ensure a positive effect on teachers' well-being Teachers, students who are studying.
Mr. Sok Sambath, Governor of Boeung Keng Kang District, led the civil servants around the Khan / Sangkat in cooperation with the officials of the Office of Prevention and Fire Truck of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to release two vehicles spraying water on the local school premises to reduce heat waves. Ensure positive results for the well-being of teachers, students who are currently studying.
Mr. Sok Sambath said that with the careful consideration of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, Boeung Keng Kang District Administration, together with Sangkat authorities, in cooperation with the Office of Prevention and Firefighting of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, released a water truck. Two water sprayers on campus to reduce heat waves so that teachers, students can teach and learn easily.
Mr. Sok Sambath said that the weather problem is warming up all over the country and other countries are also occurring, so the Boeung Keng Kang district administration pays close attention to this problem at the local level, especially in the nurseries and schools. Because if the weather is very hot, students do not go to school and teachers do not teach.
Due to the rising weather, it has really affected the students, and on behalf of the Boeung Keng Kang District Authority, he has been paying close attention to this work since before the New Year.
At the same time, the Governor of Boeung Keng Kang District advised teachers as well as all students, when coming to teach or come to study in very hot weather, to be connected with towels for soaking the head and body frequently, drinking plenty of water, doors and windows. Open wide to allow good ventilation. This is to protect the health of everyone.
