(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 3, 2024, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, invited ambassadors, ambassadors as well as officials representing embassies in Cambodia, including Vietnam, to explain. And present information related to the Funan-Techo Canal Project.
The Funan Techo Canal Project is a waterway project connecting the rivers and seas of Cambodia with great benefits related to Cambodian trade. This project has received great support from the Cambodian people.
Regarding the Funan-Techo canal project, Cambodia also informed the Mekong River Commission countries, including Thailand, Laos, Vietnam and Myanmar. Despite the news, Vietnam seems unhappy with the project and has tried to use negative media coverage to attack the project.
In order to counter Vietnam's corrupt strategy, Cambodia issued a series of statements by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, and Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister Hun Manet.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, as an official of the Royal Government and the manager of the Funan-Techo canal project, also launched a campaign to eradicate corruption in Vietnam. During Vietnam's anti-corruption campaign, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol gave interviews to international media, presented with students and so on.
The meeting with the Ambassadors and representatives of the Embassy in Cambodia, including representatives of the Vietnamese Embassy in the morning of May 3, 2024, is also an effort to make the representatives of friendly countries better understand and understand the Funan Canal project. Techo both the technical characteristics and the purpose of the construction of this canal.
During the meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister explained in detail the construction techniques of the river flow into the sea compared to the current water flow situation, legal aspects and the benefits gained from this canal.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, confirmed that the project will start construction in late 2024 or early 2025.
