The director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology said that the good irrigation system in Bak Anlong commune, Trapeang Prasat district is capable of irrigating 417 hectares of wet season rice, 165 hectares of dry season rice and 245 hectares of mixed crops. Hectares as well.
(Kampot): Dr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot Province, said that the provincial administration has already prepared a plan to rescue people affected by the drought in some areas in the province. In 15 days, the weather will still be hot and there will be no rain, and the authorities will launch a campaign to rescue people throughout the province.
Mr. Mao Thunin said that on behalf of the provincial authorities, leaders and authorities at all levels in the province are considering and preparing contingency plans to respond to natural disasters on some geographical locations in the province that are already vulnerable. And. Especially those areas that are vulnerable to flooding and those areas that are vulnerable to drought.
In the past, the provincial administration has submitted plans to local authorities, villages, communes, sangkats, districts, municipalities and experts based on the use of total force, total means to intervene in all these issues, because it can seriously affect the lives of people. And more than a year ago, the provincial administration has prepared to restore the Boeung Buor canal to store a large amount of water.
In connection with the above work, the provincial authorities carried out in strict accordance with the orders of the Royal Government and under the direct supervision of the Honorary General Dr. Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management and Secretary-General of the Former Association. Cambodian fighters.
