According to officials, the weather will continue to be hot until the end of May, when it will rain.
UN says resettlement in Gaza could take up to 80 years
(Gaza): Reconstruction in the Gaza Strip could last for centuries if current trends continue, the United Nations said on Thursday. This is according to the release by Reuters on April 2, 2024.
Nearly seven months after the Israeli bombing, the Gaza Strip has been devastated, causing billions of dollars in damage. The attack turned several high-rise concrete buildings there into rubble, with UN officials describing the landscape as "destructive to the moon".
According to Palestinian data, about 80,000 homes were destroyed in the conflict in the Gaza Strip as Israeli airstrikes killed tens of thousands of Palestinians.
A report from the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) says it will take about 80 years to restore all completely destroyed homes in Gaza.
The UNDP assessment predicts that based on the duration of the ongoing conflict, the suffering of the people of Gaza will last for decades to come. UNDP Administrator Achim Steiner warns of massive loss of life and destruction of infrastructure, as well as rising poverty. He stressed that such circumstances will lead to a serious development crisis that hinders the future of the next generation.
Kratie Provincial Department of Rural Development repairs 24 pump wells for people to use daily
(Kratie): The technical team of Kratie Provincial Department of Rural Development repaired 24 water wells in 3 districts in Kratie province.
Mr. Lim Chea Hav, Director of the Kratie Provincial Department of Rural Development, said that the water well that the team repaired was a community well shared. He said that during 1999 or 2000, about 25 families in the community, the Ministry provided water wells for common use, but now is to reduce the number of families if people live to 10 families than the Ministry and Provide a well for them to share.
The wells that the team repaired were owned by the Ministry of Rural Development and some by the commune fund or some partner organizations, and for most of those wells were dug deep, with unusable water sources. Dry.
In Snoul district, in Cheung Khle village, 2 wells were repaired by 34 families) and in Trapeang Sre village, 2 families were used by 2 families in 2 Thnou commune. * Krabey village enters 4 tunnels for 32 families, Kbal Trach village: 1 well for 11 families, Rahar village: 2 wells for use by 15 families, Clean village: 1 well for 7 families * Meanchey village: 1 well for 6 families in Sre Char commune .
At the same time, the Minister instructed all working groups to pay attention to the assignment to address local needs in a timely and efficient manner.
Sub-Committee on Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes Continues to Crack Down on Natural Resource Crimes in Bramoy Commune, Veal Veng District
(Pursat): Mr. Run Sary, Chairman of the 6th Group of the Sub-Committee on Natural Resource Crime, including the Pursat Provincial Unity Command, the National Police Force and the National Gendarmerie, cracked down on natural resource crimes in Chheuteal village. Chrum Bramoy Commune, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province.
It should be noted that for more than one month of the operation to suppress the crime of destroying natural resources in Phnom Kravanh and Veal Veng districts, the joint force conducted a hot operation to suppress the crime of natural resources in Pursat province, achieving 10 land confiscations. 821.65 hectares, found 50 suspects and sent cases to court in 18 cases. At the same time, the joint working group educated 92 people who helped grow crops for the perpetrators.
In addition, the coalition dismantled temporary huts on the site, encroached on a large amount of forest land in the protected area, and confiscated some materials as evidence.
Operation to suppress natural resource crime in Pursat province is large-scale and organized after the order of Samdech Moha Vortheid Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia to the Ministry of Environment, ministries, institutions and relevant authorities and law enforcement to strengthen the management of natural resources throughout the country and Strictly enforce the law on natural resource perpetrators.
In Pursat province, a joint force consisting of the National Gendarmerie, National Police Force, Provincial Unity Command, along with relevant local authorities and 789 park rangers, divided into 10 groups, has been operating hotly. Prevent the crime of logging, encroachment and burning of forest land in protected areas to be owned in Phnom Kravanh and Veal Veng districts, Pursat province.
In order to ensure the effective management of natural resources, the Minister of Environment has complied with the orders of Samdech Hun Sen and set out four measures, including promoting the implementation of the law 100%, there are no exceptions, and ending the culture of signing contracts and releasing them. Committing a crime.
