General Sao Sokha Announces the Inauguration of Brigadier General Meng Srun as Commander of Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie
(Kampong Speu): At the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie Command, this morning, Thursday, May 2, 2024, General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie, presided over the inauguration ceremony. The post of Commander of the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie was replaced by Brigadier General Meng Srun, replacing Brigadier General Chou Sarun.
General Sao Sokha stated that according to the Royal Government's political program on the reform of the armed forces and the five-year reform strategy of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the Royal Gendarmerie has accelerated the reforms towards (concentration, order, modernization and efficiency). .
For the current ceremony, the appointment, promotion, change of position in the armed forces, civil servants, as well as the private sector, that is, the rules of work, the organization of human resources for job growth and also the opportunity to change the environment. There are four key benefits to changing jobs (not to mention enforcing the law for veterans over the age of 60 and retiring):
* First: to protect the honor and dignity of officers * Second: to organize human resources in accordance with the ability, skills and temperament * Third: to provide opportunities for successors * Fourth: to change the work environment to share Good experience in order to make the organization grow at the same time. In addition, there are opportunities for learning to increase the ability to keep up with the latest developments in the situation.
For the commander to be appointed today, Brigadier General Meng Srun, should pay attention to three core tasks:
* First, the management of people must understand and implement 7 points, including food, clothing, accommodation, health, education, transportation, entertainment and problem solving, maintenance work, facilities and equipment, real estate management, work process. According to administrative procedures and army hierarchy.
* Second: Unit building work, work place (building, office and workplace), place of education, training, learning, place for the army to stay and eat in the unit.
* Third: The work of leading, managing, commanding the unit, the army is orderly, has good internal discipline, has unity, has the spirit, the will, the conscience, the honesty, the courage, the diligence, clearly understands the roles and responsibilities, respects the law, the discipline of the army, the professional ethics of the military police, and cooperates to accomplish tasks.
