Taiwan approves $ 878 million earthquake relief plan in early April
The Taiwanese government announced on Thursday that it had approved $ 878 million in aid after a major earthquake last month killed 17 people and damaged infrastructure. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Thursday, May 2, 2024.
Taiwan's cabinet has announced that it will do its utmost to rebuild homes as well as revitalize businesses with the $ 878 million budget. Under this project, part of the budget is for emergency repairs and reconstruction of public facilities, while the other part is used to assist in the resettlement and reconstruction of affected private homes. In addition, it will provide industry financing, insurance subsidies and employment assistance programs.
A magnitude 7.4 earthquake shook Taiwan on April 3, injuring 1,100 people, but a strong building defense system and disaster preparedness helped prevent the quake. The catastrophe is bigger. The quake caused landslides, blocked subways and roads, and damaged buildings, affecting business tourism in the eastern city of Hualien, Taiwan.
