Iran announces US, UK sanctions for supporting Israeli war in Gaza
Tehran: Iran on Thursday announced sanctions on individuals, as well as US and British entities, for supporting Israel's war against the Palestinian militant group Hamas in the Gaza Strip. . This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, May 2, 2024.
According to the Iranian Foreign Ministry, the sanctions include blocking accounts and conducting financial transactions in Iran's banking and financial system, freezing assets under Iranian jurisdiction and banning issuance. Visas and entry to Iran.
