This statement of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet was made on Thursday, May 2, 2024, on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the inauguration. Officially, Toyota car assembly plant with $ 37 million investment in Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone.
Samdech Hun Manet continued that Cambodia used to be an importer of all kinds, but now Cambodia can produce its own materials and products, in fact, Cambodia can produce cars to supply the market, although not a company of Cambodian children, but a foreign company. Products in Cambodia with high quality and affordable to the people of Cambodia, this is what the Royal Government wants.
"By improving the living standards of the people, not only increasing their salaries, but also keeping their expenses low, they can afford to buy more and have more money to do other things," said Hun Manet. "So keeping a percentage of the market in annual inflation is very important."
Samdech Manibodi Hun Manet added that if in one year the price of goods rises by 30 or 40 percent, it is difficult, so for salaries, the Royal Government always considers in the increase as possible and strive to provide products to the people.
Samdech President Hun Manet said that when it comes to development, it is not a one-way street to come together as a result for the people. In particular, the inauguration of Toyota's car assembly plant will bring many benefits to the Cambodian economy and people, mainly to increase productivity, enhance prestige and provide pride for the Cambodian people.
Samdech Mani President Hun Manet said this on May 2, 2024, on the occasion of Samdech officially presiding over the inauguration of Toyota car assembly plant in Cambodia.
"In the future, we can import the minority and produce most of the local products, and if we have the capacity in the future, we can become the center of supply in any part of the region," he said. Samdech Thipdey claims that Cambodia is a plus and that the production of some places is an element for pushing abroad as well.
In connection with this production, Samdech Hun Sen said, "Cambodia does not want to need the whole production in Cambodia, but we can start production from any part of the input, Cambodia does not need to produce aircraft, but if any part of our aircraft. "Made in Cambodia, even a mattress or a belt can improve our productivity, and so can a car."
"This is a strategic goal that we have already set out in Cambodia's industrial development policy and we will continue to adjust and move forward," he said. In this work, the Royal Government has sharpened many mandates, starting from the Rectangular Strategy, and now comes the Pentagon Strategy and will continue to push further.
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet also encouraged Toyota car assembly companies to continue to examine the potential, especially with the import of equipment for vehicle assembly, and then continue to examine the possibility of using local products and raw materials. The company is leading the establishment of a mattress manufacturer to supply domestic car assembly without having to import from abroad.
