The five recommendations of Samdech Manipheap Hun Manet for the Ministry of Information include: * First: Improving the capacity of journalists through vocational training to maintain ethics and quality of work.
* Second, continue to review the laws and regulations that are still in force to be amended or reorganized in order to respond to the evolution of society and to improve law enforcement in the field of journalism to maintain proper professional order.
* Third: Prepare a professional journalism code to set standard operating procedures on journalistic ethics, which promotes the value of the profession.
* Fourth: Develop guidelines on the production of content and dissemination of citizen journalists to eliminate anarchy on social media.
* Fifth: Organize funds to support the process of building and developing the capacity of members of the Association of Journalists and on the protection and professional development.
* Second: Provide real information to the national and international public about the real situation in Cambodia and disseminate all policies and strategies of the Royal Government to the people and bring information from the people to the Royal Government to solve problems in a timely and effective manner. High in line with the government's reform program
* Third: Educate the public about measures to prevent traffic accidents, dangers of drug use, human trafficking, safe village and commune policy to maintain safety and social order.
* Fourth: Continue to participate in the fight against false information that has a socially polluting nature, can cause national instability, political unrest, chaos and loss of social order, and must adhere to professional ethics, true information, balanced in all aspects.
* Fifth: Training of technical and professional skills to improve the quality of information, information order and the prestige of the media.
Samdech President Hun Manet noted that the freedom of the press in Cambodia is growing and growing healthy
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, noted that the freedom of the press in Cambodia is growing, growing healthily and leading to better order.
The state of freedom of expression remains favorable, as journalists are able to report freely on the basis of ethics and professionalism in journalism.
Hun Manet stated that the Law on the Press, which deals with the rights and freedoms of the press, stipulates that pre-publishing censorship is prohibited in order to maintain the independence of the press. The Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia also recognizes respect for human rights as enshrined in the United Nations Charter, the Universal Declaration of Human Rights, and all treaties and conventions.
