President of the National Union of Cambodian Trade Unions: In order for an enterprise to become a peaceful community, four key stakeholders are required to participate.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Suong Huot, President of the National Assembly of the National Union of Cambodia (NACC), said that in order for an enterprise to become a safe community, it requires the participation of four main stakeholders, including: employers, workers, unions, the Royal Government. .
First, compliance with good working conditions refers to enterprises that have received a certificate of compliance with working conditions from the Ministry of Labor, do not use the most serious forms of child labor.
Second: Compliance with the use of young workers
Third, the conformity of industrial relations refers to enterprises that have a mechanism for resolving labor disputes at the enterprise level and have a mechanism for social dialogue.
Fourth: Compliance with occupational safety and health conditions refers to enterprises that do not have occupational hazards and are effective in the fight against HIV / AIDS in the workplace.
Fifth, the conformity of the social security system refers to the enterprise that performs its obligations in accordance with the law on the social security system.
Sixth: Compliance with the use of disabled workers refers to enterprises that employ more than 3% of the total number of disabled workers.
Seventh: Compliance with the implementation of labor productivity promotion programs refers to enterprises that implement skills training programs and capacity building of workers.
And eighth, compliance with the implementation of the social responsibility program refers to enterprises that participate in supporting the community nursery and kindergarten process, have a green work program and encourage the use of plastic bags, as well as participate in other social activities.
