Samdech Thep Dey considers the reduction of car import tax instead by setting up a car assembly plant as taking money from one pocket to the other.
The Prime Minister stated that the reduction of customs revenue from car imports is not a problem because through local investment has provided job opportunities and skills to the people of Cambodia, and when the car sales company will earn that income. Taxes to the state through taxes.
The Prime Minister added that opening a car assembly plant in Cambodia will enable people to buy cars to use at a lower price than imports because the company has received some favors from the Royal Government.
Prime Minister Hun Manet made the remarks while presiding over the inauguration of a Toyota car assembly plant with an investment of $ 37 million in the Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone on the morning of May 2, 2024.
Please be informed that the income from the import of vehicles and machinery is the main source of revenue of the General Department of Customs and Excise. In 2019, vehicle import revenue accounted for 53% of total customs revenue, by 2020, customs revenue from vehicle imports decreased by 42%, and by 2023, customs revenue from the import of vehicles and machinery will be more than 220 million USD Or equal to 31.1% of total revenue.
