His Excellency made the remarks on the occasion of the inauguration of the Toyota car assembly plant with an investment of $ 37 million in the Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone this morning, May 2, 2024.
On the occasion of the inauguration of the Toyota car assembly plant with an investment of $ 37 million in the Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone this morning, May 2, 2024, Samdech Hun Sen highlighted that the six car assembly plants are located in Banteay Meanchey province. , Koh Kong, Pursat, Svay Rieng, Kandal and Phnom Penh.
"As of now, Cambodia has a total of six factories, of which four are in operation and two are in the pilot phase, located in Banteay Meanchey, Koh Kong, Pursat and Svay Rieng provinces," he said. , Kandal province and Phnom Penh.
As for the Toyota car assembly plant, Samdech Manet now sees not only a good new progress for the industry in Cambodia, but also a positive sign for the diversification of the Cambodian economy.
He added that Toyota has been present in Cambodia since the UNTAC era and has become a symbol of growth in its business. Samdech Hun Sen emphasized that the presence of the Toyota factory now is due to the efforts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia, and the good cooperation between Cambodia and the Japanese side.
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia expressed his optimism and hope that under the umbrella of peace, political and macroeconomic stability with Cambodia's human resources and young skilled labor force and the attractiveness of investment in Cambodia will continue. Continue to invest in this type of industry based on this skill.
According to Hun Manet, Cambodia must continue to develop industrial infrastructure that serves to invest and train skilled human resources in line with the needs of the labor market.
Speaking on the occasion of presiding over the inauguration of the Toyota car assembly plant in the Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone, Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated: “Toyota is a giant company, before they do anything, they think very clearly. So if the giants come to Cambodia, they will encourage me that other companies will come to Cambodia. This is a very big deal. ”
According to the President, the installation of Toyota cars in Cambodia is a source of pride for the Cambodian people, and Samdech expressed the hope that the Japanese friends will continue to stand strong with Cambodia. Apart from assembling cars, Samdech also wants the company to check the investment in screws or car mattresses.
