Ministry of Labor Spokesman: The Ministry of Labor has received a petition from the unions and will review their allegations.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kata On, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said on May 1, 2024 that the Ministry of Labor will review the petitions submitted by unions, civil society organizations and workers to the Ministry. Work.
This statement was made after civil society organizations, unions and about 100 workers gathered to submit a petition to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on May 1, 2024 International Labor Day.
The Secretary of State underlined that around the petition submitted to the Ministry of Labor at this time, the Ministry will look at what the union is saying, what the Ministry has successfully implemented, what the Ministry is implementing and what is not reflecting. True.
He added that the rallies, protests and petitions of unions and civil society organizations showed the freedom of trade unions and civil society organizations in Cambodia, which was completely free, unlike the restrictions on the freedom of trade unions and civil society organizations in Cambodia. No.
Of those, more than 6,000 unions, compared to a population of 17 million, are large because of the freedom of association, the ease with which it is free to register and draft its statutes, and the wide range of functions. Of unions in Cambodia.
He added that Cambodia's trade union law provides for the formation of a union, which requires 10 workers, which is better than some countries, and the ILO recommendation (ILO requires 50 workers, Australia, Philippines, Bangladesh requires 50 workers or 20% or 30%).
He said the ministry was pushing for collective bargaining to sign collective agreements through mediation of unions for unions. Following the amendment of the trade union law, the number of registered registrations increased from 564 in 2019 to 624 in 2024.
At the same time, the settlement of labor disputes was 91.80%, an increase of 80.95% from 2023. According to the procedure, in case of non-recovery, the Ministry shall refer to the Arbitration Council. Amendments to the Labor Law 2021 provide options for parties to individual disputes can also file a complaint to the Arbitration Council.
He added that the use of employment contracts for a fixed period or indefinite duration also has the same additional benefits. Labor and union laws prohibit all forms of discrimination in labor and unions. The Ministry encourages workers and unions to file a complaint to the Ministry in case of any discrimination. The tripartite mechanism of the Minimum Wage Council consists of a coalition of unions chosen by the unions themselves.
