Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie Closes Fire, Rescue and Rescue Skills Training
(Banteay Meanchey): Brigadier General Vong Thi, Acting Commander of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie, presided over the closing ceremony of a firefighting and rescue training course for Banteay Meanchey and Provincial Gendarmerie on Wednesday afternoon, May 01, 2024. Svay Rieng.
The ceremony was also attended by Major General Soeur Rithy, Deputy Director of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Department, from the National Police Commissioner and many other instructors after the three-day training course. 116 people, including 40 trainees from Svay Rieng Provincial Gendarmerie.
Speaking at the closing ceremony of the training course, Brigadier General Vong Thi also thanked the Deputy Chiefs of the Armed Forces of the two provinces for their hard work in acquiring knowledge, lessons as well as ways to save the people in case Fire as well as the practical implementation of firefighting according to the presentation of the trainer for 2 days successfully with a sense of responsibility and good discipline.
At the same time, Brigadier General Vong Thi also instructed the Armed Forces of the two provinces to take all these skills to save people in various accidents, especially fires that often occur.
Major General Soeur Rithy confirmed that during these 3 days, the lecturer presented 5 lessons:
1: Presentation of laws and regulations related to fire, 2: Fire prevention and rescue procedures, 3: Roles and responsibilities of firefighters, 4: Techniques to use fire trucks, 5: Techniques to put out fires (Solid fire extinguishing, liquid fire extinguishing, gas fire extinguishing, multi-storey building construction), etc.
Lt. Gen. Soeur Rithy also clarified the purpose of this training to enable the trainees to understand what is the knowledge in the training related to the use of fire trucks, both on foot and on fire trucks.
At the same time, Major General Soeur Rithy also called on all people to be careful of fires in the summer, fires can occur if we are not very careful through the use of incense, candles, electricity or gas. Original.
It should be noted that after completing the 3-day fire prevention and rescue skills training, a total of 116 participants also received certificates of education for all participants. His Excellency N. Van Vibol, Vice President of the Court of Appeal, donated $ 500 on the occasion of the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2024
