The Cambodian Chamber of Commerce has formed an alliance with the troops of the 8th Intervention Brigade in Preah Vihear province to know about each other's well-being.
(Preah Vihear): Pursuant to the Decision of the Royal Government of Cambodia No. 48 Pillar dated 6 July 2023 on the revision and preparation of the sisterhood alliance between the military units of the 8th Intervention Brigade and the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce. The two agreed to provide information to each other to find out about each other's well-being in order to increase mutual understanding between the two institutions.
His Excellency Lt. Gen. Hun Manit emphasized that due to the factors of peace and stability along the border, we have all had the opportunity to participate in development in all areas, promote economic growth and improve people's livelihood. At the same time, HE thanked Kith Meng for donating 3 sirens to the Preah Vihear Provincial Administration and led a delegation from the Phnom Penh Chamber of Commerce to support the front line troops in spirit and equipment.
His Excellency Lt. Gen. Hun Manit said, "We will continue to work hand in hand, continue to support each other to maintain peace, social stability, territorial integrity and participate in sustainable development."
For practical assignments to effectively implement the above sisterhood content, both units agreed to assign their respective working groups to communicate regularly. This team has the task of communicating, consulting, cooperating, arranging all ceremonies as necessary, as well as monitoring and reporting to the leaders of their respective units about the work results.
