The working group of the Ministry of Water Resources and Kampong Cham Provincial Authority inspected the situation of the case of embankment in Meanchey commune, Srey Santhor district.
(Kampong Cham): On the morning of May 1, 2024, a working group of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology led by Mr. Ouk Vuthy, Undersecretary of State and Kampong Cham Provincial Administrative Team led by Ms. Sopheak, Deputy Governor, inspected the situation River bank at Chey village, Meanchey commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province.
According to a press release issued by the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration, on the afternoon of April 29, 2024, Ms. Sopheak led a joint team to inspect the riverbank. The bank is 165 meters long, with a slope of 10 meters and 16 meters.
The construction was not asked for a written law, but an oral request from Meanchey commune chief. The construction was started gradually until the end of the activities in January 2024. The owner of the site confirmed the purpose of the rock is to prevent the riverbank from collapsing further.
However, as an administrative measure, the working group required the site owners to stop further refueling activities and wait for the results of the assessment study of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on the technical characteristics and impacts.
Mr. Chhun Puthearith, Director General of Technical Affairs of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, said that his team had personally inspected the riverbank case to make a detailed report to the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, as well as the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration. Let me know the real situation in this area.
More than 17 tons of frozen meat and spoiled food were burned
(Phnom Penh): Professional Officer of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Fraud Suppression "KPR" On the morning of May 1, 2024, a total of 17,880 kilograms of expired food products and frozen meat products were inspected and cracked down in the past.
The demolition took place at a landfill in Sangkat Choeung Ek, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh, under the leadership of Mr. Bun Chamroeun, Deputy Director General of the General Department of PPR. Representative of Mr. Phan Aun, Royal Government of Cambodia Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of DPRK And with the participation of Mr. Srun Pov, President of the Cambodian Breeders Association and Dangkor district authorities.
Mr. Bun Chamroeun said that the implementation of the recommendations of the Minister of Commerce, Ms. Cham Nimmol, and under the direct command of Mr. Phan Oun, Investigating Officer of the General Department of the Ministry of Commerce, with the cooperation of district authorities. Three: Khan Chbar Ampov, Khan Sen Sok and Khan Kambol raided three locations and some means of transportation in early April.
He said the purpose of the inspection was to find out the presence of banned chemicals, unsanitary conditions that lead to the transmission of bacteria and other epidemics, outdated products, defects, unsafe quality and compliance. And technical regulations in force relating to the requirements of packaging, shipping and storage.
At the same time, Mr. Srun Pov, who participated in the burning of frozen meat and spoiled food, also thanked Ms. Cham Nimmol, Minister of Commerce, as well as the General Department of KPR, for taking care to crack down on frozen meat and goods. Damage to these qualities.
ASEAN Secretary-General promotes ASEAN-France cooperation in Paris
On the morning of April 30, 2024, in Paris, France, the Secretary-General of ASEAN met with Ms. Chrysoula Zacharopoulou, Senior Minister in charge of the development of Francophonie and the French International Partnership. On that occasion, the two sides exchanged views on ways and means to promote cooperation under the ASEAN-France Development Partnership.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also thanked France for its commitment to cooperation with ASEAN through both bilateral and ASEAN-EU frameworks.
(Phnom Penh): Water shortages have become a challenge in some areas due to the prolonged drought, prompting three ministries, including the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and the Ministry of Rural Development, to meet. Together on this issue to ensure that people continue to have access to clean water, despite the prolonged drought.
The Water Solution Meeting was held on April 30, 2024 with the participation of Mr. Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, together with Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology and Mr. Chhay Rithy Sen. Minister of Rural Development.
The three ministers met to discuss and focus on urgent interventions to address the water shortages that are plaguing some areas, as well as finding long-term solutions.
However, he expressed optimism about Cambodia's water resources sector, citing ongoing construction, rehabilitation and expansion of reservoirs and canals, and future projects, including large-scale reservoirs up to ponds. Will strengthen Cambodia's water resources sector and flood protection capacity in the coming years.
In the past, the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation has introduced remedial measures and has been monitoring and evaluating the plight of water operators across the country, as well as providing important updates to relevant ministries to promote cooperation on water solutions. Areas where water sources have dried up.
On that occasion, Hem Vandy highlighted the urgency of the intervention and requested the relevant ministries and institutions to implement the "living of one character" approach by thinking together, working together and working together on behalf of the same government.
He asked the Ministry of Water Resources to prioritize the supply of raw water for clean water production in the Ministry's projects in line with the national policy on water resources in Cambodia.
At the same time, it is proposed to share important data such as data on water sources, canals, water service areas, wells and rural ponds and urbanization data, etc. for the implementation of the intervention quickly and effectively.
At the same time, Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen requested the three Ministries to sign a Memorandum of Understanding to implement the coordination in the design, distribution and planning to improve water management to meet both urgent and long-term needs.
The Royal Academy of Cambodia continues to provide 100 liters of Techo Sen Russey Trup fresh milk to the orphanage "Borey Infant and National Children's"
