Workers and employers claim that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the seventh mandate, has carefully considered and effectively reformed the labor sector
(Phnom Penh): Workers say that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the seventh mandate, has continued to provide many benefits to workers to improve their rights and livelihoods while working conditions in factories are better and more High attention from the Royal Government of Cambodia for the well-being of workers.
Ms. Nuth Srey Mom, a worker at Sabrina factory, said that after the protection mechanism for pregnant factory workers, she can leave 25 minutes early and receive a stipend of 80,000. Riel, 50% postpartum allowance from the factory and 70% from the Royal Government, including 800,000 Riel allowance from the former Prime Minister Samdech Techo.
She added that she also received many other benefits from the factory, including a one-time free lunch and a decent restaurant. All this clearly shows the Royal Government's consideration for workers, especially pregnant workers.
While constantly supporting the new mechanisms put in place to serve the interests of workers in Cambodia, all workers and the private sector expressed their gratitude to the Royal Government, Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister for continuing to provide many benefits to Workers across the country.
It should also be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the seventh mandate, headed by Prime Minister Hun Manet, has been paying close attention to the implementation of labor rights and benefits for workers, and the Royal Government has a mechanism to Promote the protection of the rights and freedoms of professional organizations, maintain harmony and professional relations, provide benefits to workers, including the provision of social protection.
The Royal Government has provided many benefits to the workers, including free workers, the increase in wages in 2024, taking into account the cost of water, electricity, rent, the establishment of various mechanisms to promote the rights. Workers, support for pregnant workers and many other mechanisms provided by the government, in which workers can also receive free vocational training.
It should be noted that Samdech Moha Bovathibodi also issued four recommendations for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to implement for 2024 to 2025, firstly cooperating with relevant ministries to build community kindergartens, secondly to improve the restaurant. The factory premises, the third enterprise to improve transportation and the fourth to test the skills recognition of workers.
