Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet orders the Armed Forces to intervene to help people solve the problem of lack of clean water during hot weather (Video inside) (Preah Sihanouk): Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet ordered the Armed Forces to be ready to intervene People solve the problem of lack of clean water during the hot weather in the dry season to prolong the time.
Such an order by Samdech Hun Sen was made on the occasion that Samdech presided over a get-together with civil servants, workers and employees working at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port to celebrate the 138th Anniversary of International Labor Day 1. May, held under the theme "One enterprise is a peaceful community" on the morning of May 1, 2024.
Samdech Hun Manet said that these days, the temperature has risen sharply around the world, while Cambodia is also experiencing this heat wave. Samdech also gave guidelines to ministries, professional institutions, especially local authorities to be vigilant in case of fire, water shortage to the people and ready to intervene immediately in this case.
"I urge His Excellency the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the National Police, and the Commissioner General to be ready to intervene in the event that the dry season does not have a longer rainy season, according to the meteorologist," he said. "He guarantees that at the beginning of this dry month there will be rain, now we have about 10 provinces, so we are asking you to pay attention to this work."
In case the temperature rises above 40 degrees Celsius, Samdech Hun Sen also introduced to Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, and issued guidelines to the school management to suspend the study. Urgent to protect the health of children.
With this warming, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology is calling on people to cooperate in using water at a high level, especially in rural areas far from water sources during the dry season in 2024 from March to April. Temperatures across the country will rise above the average for many years, resulting in hot, dry weather.
Regarding the weather forecast in Cambodia in the dry season 2024, the Ministry of Water Resources stressed that the temperature across the country will be higher than the average for many years, which is a factor that makes the weather hot and dry. Rainfall will be lower than the average for many years, and less rainfall will be less than in 2023, along with more thunderstorms and gusts.
According to the weather forecast, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology calls on relevant institutions, local authorities and people to cooperate in using water at a high level, especially in rural areas far from water sources.
At the same time, pay attention to the hot and dry weather, thunder, lightning and strong winds that can occur in April and May 2024.
