An old wooden bridge was repaired by the community to facilitate traffic
(Kratie): A wooden bridge, which is more than 20 years old, is dilapidated. The local community is united to raise funds and renovate it to facilitate the transportation of agricultural products.
The activities of the people in Tonsong Tluak village, Kampong Cham commune, Sambo district, Kratie province have combined both budget and physical and mental resources to repair the 47-meter-long wooden bridge, which was built in 1999 by the local community.
Until now, this wooden bridge is more than 20 years old, and now the community led by Mr. Im Pov, Tonsong Tluak village chief, and with the support of Mr. Chhit Non, Kampong Cham commune chief, has decided to renovate to facilitate traffic. In the travel of people transporting various farmers.
Mr. Im Pov, chief of Tonsong Tluak village, said that this wooden bridge is located in a remote area and in the future, it is planned to build a concrete bridge instead, but in the future, it needs to be resolved and facilitated temporarily, so that the people in a community This has raised funds and united to repair and use at the request of the commune chief himself. Russian defense minister orders more weapons for war in Ukraine
