(Phnom Penh): At a press conference to announce the report on the "Status of Press Freedom in Cambodia" on the afternoon of April 30, 2024, Minister of Information Neth Pheaktra claimed that in recent years there have been no journalists in Cambodia. One died and was imprisoned for pursuing his profession.
At the same time, 99.7% of the total survey participants gave importance to respecting the professional ethics of journalists, while 92.1% supported the implementation of the procedure, he said. The law applies to unprofessional journalists, and 99.4% support the training of journalists to improve their professional quality.
"Although we are not perfect, the news situation in Cambodia is good, and I would like to emphasize that in recent years no journalists have died due to "Professional and no journalists are imprisoned for practicing legal professional ethics. I speak legally, I do not talk about crime, extortion (money) or other (crime) issues."
Mr. Neth Pheaktra appealed and encouraged the younger generation who want to become journalists not to fear that their career as journalists will endanger their lives if they adhere to the code. Professional ethics. On the other hand, the market for journalists in Cambodia is still wide.
