Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet said that the quality of tourism does not reflect the quantity available, but also the number of days that tourists stay, so the longer the tourism, the better.
Please be informed that Prek Chik Funan-Techo project is a project to connect waterways between rivers to the sea of Cambodia, passing through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep provinces, about 180 kilometers long. The project is expected to cost about 1.7 billion US dollars and has already been studied in detail.
Samdech Thipdey said this during a meeting with government officials, staff and workers working at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port on the morning of May 1, 2024.
This is not the first time the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has made such a statement after allegations by Vietnamese researchers that the Funan Techo canal project would serve the Chinese military. President Hun Manet stressed that Cambodia has no law allowing the presence of foreign troops on its territory.
Samdech Mani Hun Manet stated, "Do not take anything, politics is connected with the army. I said no, I was the commander, even though I was not the commander of the navy, but I knew that the warship could not carry the plane in at a depth of 5 meters until I realized that the ferry had entered. Cambodia also has no policy to take the country as a basis for any country against any country. "We live in peace and unity for the benefit of the nation. We only want peace. The war is long over."
He asserted that the project to build the Funan-Techo canal was for economic gain, not foreign military service. Samdech continued that the Funan-Techo canal project has been studied by a total of 40 national and international experts who have clear technology to prevent the Mekong River from flowing into the sea and also comply with international law on the Mekong River. .
In response, former Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen also categorically denied the allegations. Samdech stated that the Chifon canal was built for the purely socio-economic benefit and there was no need for the Chinese army.
Samdech called for no more slander of Cambodia for anti-China purposes, saying: "We call on you not to slander us for anti-China purposes in accordance with the geopolitical strategy. We also know how to think of our national interest like you, and your brains are not sure that they are better than us. Fortunately, you were born in a rich country and we were born in a poor country. You despise us.
The Funan-Techo Prek Chik project has received strong support from the Cambodian people, and Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet thanked the people everywhere for their support. Samdech continued that there was no support movement like in support of the Funan-Techo canal project.
Samdech Hun Manet said that the Funan-Techo canal must be done and that the Royal Government has no plans to raise money for the people to build it, as this project is an investment of the Cambodian private sector and does not have foreign loans.
