Permanent Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth recommends nine key points to help reduce the impact of climate change
(Phnom Penh): At the workshop on "Impact of Climate Change and Response Policy" on April 30, 2024, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, recommended nine key points to contribute. Reduce the positive effects of climate change.
As a position to address issues related to climate change, Mr. Vongsy Visoth stated that although Cambodia is not a country that causes serious impact compared to some developed countries, Cambodia is still highly willing to unite with other countries around the world to Find solutions and launch concrete actions to respond to and manage climate change.
Based on this position, Mr. Vongsey Visoth stated that Cambodia is ready to cooperate with other countries to prevent the effects of natural disasters caused by climate change. In this spirit, Cambodia has ratified the Paris Climate Agreement and set out a roadmap towards reducing greenhouse gas emissions and achieving carbon neutrality by 2030 and 2050, respectively.
Meanwhile, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth said that the Royal Government of Cambodia in the seventh mandate of the National Assembly under the wise leadership of His Majesty Hun Manet has given priority to reducing the impact and adapting to change. Climate change, environmental sustainability, as well as natural resource management and green economy, as stated in the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy.
For Cambodia itself, Mr. Vongsy Visoth also stressed the need to find an appropriate balance between development and response to climate change. In this spirit, Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth made nine recommendations to the workshop to help reduce the positive effects of climate change in Cambodia, including:
* First, all relevant agencies should continue to develop institutional capacity in the field of research and development, planning and budgeting, implementation and monitoring and evaluation related to climate change.
* Second, continue to develop and strengthen laws, regulations and policies related to the environment, water, natural disasters, as well as green diplomacy to ensure sustainable ecosystems and contribute to climate change mitigation.
* Third: Strengthen the harmonization and integration of projects related to climate change adaptation and mitigation, planning and budgeting from local and external sources to ensure alignment and coherence with contributions that Defines Cambodia's National NDCs to Be Carbon Neutral by 2050
* Fourth: Continue to promote private sector investment in smart and green climate projects by considering the implementation of carbon taxation and strengthening the implementation of regulations and strategies for green financing and investment.
* Fifth: Promote and use climate technology, increase the use of technology and the use of artificial intelligence in major areas such as renewable energy, including solar energy, wind power and hydropower, agriculture and water management.
* Sixth: Continue to improve irrigation, climate protection and sustainable water management projects, as well as promote smart agriculture in order to boost agricultural productivity, increase resilience and reduce greenhouse gas emissions through investment. On weather resistant seed technology and agricultural techniques
* Seventh: Continue to raise awareness of the increasing severity of climate change impacts at the national and sub-national levels to improve the preparedness of the public, especially farmers and investors.
* Eighth: Continue to raise external funding to invest in innovative solutions to address climate change.
* 9th: Strengthen the social protection system to respond to climate change.
