Three Chinese nationals arrested for kidnapping Chinese national for more than 60,000 USD
(Phnom Penh): Three Chinese nationals out of 12 factions suspected of kidnapping two Chinese nationals for extorting more than 60,000 USD were arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and Po Sen Chey District Police.
The Chinese national was arrested at around 5 pm on April 30, 2024, on the street in New Town, in Prey Tea 2 village, Choam Chao III commune, Por Sen Chey district.
The suspects then hid the victim at a rented house in Prey Tea 2 village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Sen Chey, extorting more than $ 60,000. However, it is not yet known whether it was a kidnapping case or a case in which the victim owed the suspect money and the suspect refused to pay, so the suspects kidnapped and demanded money.
Separately, the police force of the Bureau of Minor Offenses of the Phnom Penh Municipal Commissioner, after receiving a complaint about this case, also searched through the GPS system installed in one of the suspects' Alphat car.
Just found out the hiding place and cooperated with the police force of Po Sen Chey district to arrest 3 people at once. However, three of the suspects escaped and the police confiscated a Land Rover and a Toyota Alphat and took them to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police for questioning.
