(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, stated that due to the injustice of some international organizations related to the situation of human rights, freedom of expression and freedom of the press, Cambodia needs a report that Reflect from all walks of life to reflect the state of press freedom in their country.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made the remarks while presiding over a press conference to announce the report on "Status of Press Freedom in Cambodia" on the afternoon of April 30, 2024 at the Ministry of Information. National and international journalists and media representatives in Cambodia in large numbers.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the Ministry of Information's first report on "Status of Press Freedom in Cambodia" reflected all media circles. This is a report that reflects all the trends of journalists who have worked in Cambodia.
The Minister of Information continued that the journalists who gave their opinions were those who were playing a role in Cambodia and understood the current situation in Cambodia. This is a self-assessment, not someone sitting in an office tens of thousands of kilometers away to assess the state of Cambodia's press and freedom of expression in Cambodia.
