Chong Kal District Authority in Oddar Meanchey Province Inspects Water Sources and Prepares Means for Distributing Water to Poor People
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Rithy Pak, Governor of Chongkal District, Oddar Meanchey Province, led a team to inspect the situation in the whole district to find water sources to be ready to intervene to transport people in need if the drought continues.
The district governor confirmed that after the inspection, the district administration has prepared the means for transporting water to the people, especially the people who are at risk of lack of means and resources for transporting water to the poor families.
On the other hand, Mr. Nhen Kuon, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, said that to date, no village in Oddar Meanchey province is facing water shortage, but if the heat wave continues to increase and rainfall continues For another month, in Oddar Meanchey province, some villages may face water shortage.
He said that if this problem occurs, the Oddar Meanchey provincial administration, as well as the municipal administration and departments have already prepared the means to transport water to the people in case the heat wave continues to increase and the rain continues to prolong.
