Duke Kouch Mengly encourages people to participate in the development of the securities sector, while this sector is not as developed as other countries in the region
(Phnom Penh): Duke Kouch Mengly on April 30, 2024 encouraged people to participate in the development of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, while this sector is still underdeveloped compared to neighboring countries.
The tycoon made this request at the first general meeting of the shareholders of Mengly J. Kouch Education Co., Ltd. at the American Intercontinental School, Tuol Kork Branch.
Founder, Chairman and CEO of Mengly JSC. Kouch Education MK wants to see investors in the stock market as interested in investing in real estate, and this is not the first time this public speaking expert has encouraged people to take an interest in the sector. Stock Exchange.
At the same time, Duke Kouch Mengly also encouraged all small and medium enterprises in Cambodia to enter the securities market to raise capital for business expansion and support the securities market of Cambodia so that Cambodia has a stable economic growth.
Please be informed that Mr. Hong So Hour, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the General Director of the Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX) has called on the public to invest in the Cambodia Securities Exchange to have a daily exchange of 100 million US dollars in 2023.
In the United States, he said, there is a trillion-dollar-a-day transaction on the stock exchange. This is due to the participation of the masses and the growth of the securities sector also makes the country's economy grow.
According to Mr. Hong Sohour, in 2023, every month, there will be 1,000 regular trading account holders for these months on the Cambodia Securities Exchange. At the same time, daily traders are becoming more active as you open a trading account and leave a lot, and there are less than 100 trading lists per day in the past.
The delegation of Phnom Penh Autonomous Port supported the sacrifices of 20 soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces with a budget of 1 million Riels per family, a total of 20 million Riels, and supported 12 wounded soldiers with 500,000 Riel, 1 basket of fruit for a total of 6 million Riel and 1 million Riel for the CMAC unit and 1 million Riel for the security forces at the scene.
On this sympathetic occasion, the delegation of Phnom Penh Autonomous Port expressed its deepest condolences to the families of the fallen soldiers, as this was the loss of officers, deputies and outstanding soldiers who sacrificed. Fresh meat, fresh blood for the cause of the motherland as a special love, especially contributing to the cause of protecting the territorial integrity, building peace, social stability and sympathy with the Cambodian people until the end of life.
The delegation of Phnom Penh Autonomous Port would like to dedicate our prayers to the souls of the 20 fallen soldiers, wish them a speedy birth in all nations, and wish all the soldiers and victims a speedy recovery.
