(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chheang Vannarith, an international event analyst, said that the world is now in the most dangerous situation since World War II, while two out of five flames are burning.
He said this morning, April 30, 2024, on the occasion of the Royal Academy of Cambodia organized a roundtable discussion on "conflict situation in the Middle East" in response to the rising tensions in the Middle East.
According to the analyst, the Israeli-Iranian conflict is the first fire, and the Russia-Ukraine conflict is the second fire, but the fire that you see most is in the Asia-Pacific conflict in the South China Sea. The other is the Korean Peninsula, the fourth, and India and Pakistan, the fifth.
Dr. Chheang Vannarith added that two fireballs were on fire and if the other three were on fire, the whole world would be on fire. He also said that the Middle East torch is a torch that puts the world in a serious crisis.
Dr. Chheang Vannarith stated, "Our world is in the context of the so-called most dangerous decade since World War II. "If you study the Cold War so far, this situation is the most dangerous after World War II and more complicated than the old Cold War because of the relevance of the characters and the issues, it is more serious than the Cold War."
He said that the Cold War had two distinct poles, the communist pole and the liberal pole, and they traded in their respective blocks. Now, global integration is difficult to distinguish, even if the US allies are all important parties to China, so it is very complicated in this context.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on the morning of April 30, 2024, made eight recommendations to enhance the operational efficiency of the Rural Development Bank (ARDB). Government policy.
The recommendation of Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth was made during the inauguration ceremony of the new head office building of ARDB Bank this morning, April 30, 2024.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth stated that he would like to ask the Board of Directors, management and staff of all levels of the Bank to pay attention to the following important tasks:
First, to consider and set out detailed measures and action plans in accordance with its jurisdiction, in close cooperation with the relevant ministries and institutions in order to implement the good results of the tasks assigned by the Royal Government.
Second, continue to participate in the process of preparing, monitoring and evaluating the implementation of policies and strategies of the Royal Government related to agriculture and rural development to open more opportunities to regulate the Bank's products and activities more and more widely.
Third, to mobilize more investment from the private sector to be integrated into the agricultural value chain to contribute to the development of support infrastructure before and after the harvest, cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions to solve market problems for farmers to increase Wider implementation of contract agricultural production, as well as contributing to the promotion of processing and export of agricultural and agro-industrial products.
Fourth, continue to contribute to improving the financial environment and promoting the expansion of digital banking services in line with the digital business development policy through additional investment in digital infrastructure and new product development.
Fifth, continue to promote the diversification of lending, by regional and priority areas, by increasing wider publicity and bringing services closer to customers.
Seventh: Participate in the development of farmers who produce to support their families to become entrepreneurial farmers by providing loans for the expansion and promotion of agricultural production.
Eighth: Continue to improve the efficiency of the Bank's operations by strengthening the capacity of officers and staff, training additional skills, as well as setting up an appropriate incentive system for officers and staff at all levels, coupled with the strengthening of work discipline. Also.
With the attention and support of the Royal Government through the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the National Bank of Cambodia, the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture has achieved a series of achievements, including the construction of a new head office building. Which was officially inaugurated now as well.
The new head office building is a testament to the proud achievements and a sign of the Bank's energetic progress in rural development and agriculture in fulfilling its mission in the coming stages to expand its scope of operations. , Enhance the quality and ease of banking services, as well as to increase the trust of customers and the general public.
For the future, the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank needs to continue to improve its mission and role as a national policy bank in financing rural and agricultural development, participation in the development of the agricultural belt, and Supply, value chain and productivity, in agriculture and rural economy to be more active and strong, more efficient and higher welfare.
(Preah Vihear): On the morning of April 30, 2024, the National Audit Authority organized a workshop to disseminate the "Law on Auditing and Public Audit Standards of the Kingdom of Cambodia" to leaders and civil servants in relevant departments and units, as well as the Armed Forces. A total of 114 armed forces and leaders of municipalities, districts and communes of Preah Vihear Provincial Administration.
The workshop was chaired by Dr. Ouk Saravuth, Deputy Auditor General and represented by Dr. Som Kimsour, Auditor General of the National Audit Authority, and attended by Mr. Khoy Khun Hor, Acting Provincial Council Chairman and Mr. Ong Vuthy, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province. .
Dr. Prohm Vichet Sophorn, Deputy Secretary General and Lecturer of the National Audit Authority, made a presentation on three main points, namely: First: The purpose of disseminating the Law on Audit and Public Audit Standards, Second: The Content of Law on Auditing and Third: Content of Public Audit Standards to Civil Servants and the Armed Forces, as well as all Municipal, District, Sangkat and Commune officials under the Preah Vihear Provincial Administration.
Two houses were completely electrocuted and two others were damaged, causing damage in Sangkat Chrang Chamres I, Khan Russey Keo, police use 13 water trucks
(Phnom Penh): A fire engulfed a house, causing damage to one house and spreading to another. This incident caused a surprise to the people and the authorities called the fire truck to intervene to spray water at 10:10 am on April 30, 2024, at house number 292, Road Lum Phum 2. Sangkat Chrang Chamres 1, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, told Fresh News that in accordance with the order of Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner. Instruct the specialized force of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Office to pay close attention to the rescue operation in a timely manner.
On the orders of Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner of Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, Lt. Col. Prohm Yorn, Director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, led the direct command of the fire brigade stationed in Phnom Penh. All targets should come out to intervene, spray water to extinguish in time to prevent the fire from continuing to the houses of nearby people.
The fire was caused by an electrical fault that caused the fire. No one was injured.
Russey Keo District Administration Rejects Post on Social Media Related to Prek O Veng Land, Land in Phnom Penh Administration's Infrastructure Development Plan
According to the Russey Keo district administration, under the leadership of Mr. Chin Bunthoeun, the district governor, the location of Prek O Veng land in Sangkat Kilometer 6, especially the land in front of Sambath Meas apartment building in Boeung Salang village, Russey Keo commune, which is surrounded by a zinc fence is The land is in the infrastructure plan of Prek O Veng Development Area of Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
Russey Keo District Administration Press Release Received by Fresh News on April 30, 2024 The District Administration is very sorry for the posting on social media from some individuals which is unbalanced information. Use only one source of information in order to confuse public opinion of Russey Keo district administration officials.
Russia did not mention the arrest of several men allegedly from Tajikistan in the March 22 terrorist attack on a concert hall in Moscow, but in a separate statement, the Foreign Ministry said in a statement. Tajikistan says nearly 1,000 Kazakhs trying to enter Russia have been stranded at Vnukovo airport since April 27 "without proper sanitation".
The Tajik Foreign Ministry added that 27 Tajik nationals had been deported and another 306 were on the list of those deported from Russia. Such restrictions apply only to Kazakhs, while dozens of Tajik nationals are also stranded at other airports in Moscow.
This is a rare expression of dissatisfaction with Tajikistan, Russia's post-Soviet alliance. According to Maria Zakharova, a spokeswoman for the Russian Foreign Ministry, she is temporarily tightening border controls to prevent terrorism, but is tackling the long-delayed issue at the border.
Tajikistan is a member of the Russian-led Security and Trade Bloc and has a Russian military base in the country. The economy also relies heavily on remittances from the more than 1 million Kazakh migrant workers working in Russia.
