Trade Unions in Cambodia: The Royal Government Takes Care of and Resolves Labor Disputes Quickly and Efficiently for the Benefit of Workers
(Phnom Penh): Trade unions in Cambodia see that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the seventh mandate, has a better, faster and more effective mechanism for resolving labor disputes to serve the interests of workers, which is a good sign to promote workers' rights and promote harmony. In the field of employment in Cambodia.
She added that the Royal Government has provided benefits to the workers themselves after the factory encountered problems leading to the closure, which is a quick and quality solution of the Royal Government in this mandate. Such a speedy labor dispute resolution mechanism is a good thing, and it shows the care and protection of the rights of all workers.
Pav Sina, president of the Cambodian Workers' Movement (CCW), said: “In the latest case of labor disputes, we have seen a speedy resolution. For me, the policy that the Royal Government is working for workers, we support and expect to resolve labor disputes as quickly as possible to protect workers' interests.
He added that in addition to resolving disputes for workers quickly and effectively, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has brought thousands of job opportunities in front of the factory for workers to get new jobs after the factory. Problems. This policy is important and innovative for the workers.
In particular, Mr. Fasali, President of the National Union Coalition, is interested in expanding the scope of the UN. In which workers can use the card. To go for free health check-ups and health care. The provision for workers by the Royal Government is to provide benefits and facilitate the lives of workers, especially to control costs.
At the same time, the unions in Cambodia strongly congratulated the Royal Government of Cambodia for continuing to provide many benefits to the workers, including allowing workers to use the UNSD card. Free, allowances for pregnant and maternity workers, prenatal check-ups, pay raises, free technical training and more.
Three Thai nationals sentenced to life in prison, one killed in operation to crack down on more than 40 kilograms of cross-border drug trafficking in Chroy Changvar district in 2022
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ly Sokha, President of the Trial Chamber of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on the morning of April 30, 2024, held a hearing to announce the verdict in the case of cracking down on Thai criminals who transport drugs at Keo Street. Chenda was located in Village 3, Sangkat Chroy Changva, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh during August 2022.
The three Thai defendants include:
* First: Phan Thep Vithya, alias Nako * Second: Nak Rong Rith Chak In Suk, alias Yo * Third: Krieng Saktak Maklikun was sentenced to life imprisonment for "transportation, trafficking, storage, misuse "Drugs law and possession of weapons without permission."
On September 3, 2022, the Anti-Drug Department cracked down on cross-border drug trafficking by arresting four Thai nationals. More than 40 kilograms of drugs were seized.
On the day of the incident, on August 31, 2022, at 8:30 AM, the Joint Special Forces investigated for more than a month and launched an operation to crack down on Thai criminals transporting drugs at Keo Chenda Street in Village 3, Sangkat Chroy Changva, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
In this case, the perpetrators drove a car and fired eight shots at the police, and the police used their right to defend themselves, shooting back, killing one suspect and injuring another, and as a result, the police arrested four perpetrators. .
ILO Cambodia: Supporting What the Seventh Government Achieves in Benefiting Workers Across the Country
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ton Sophoan, ILO National Coordinator for Cambodia, said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the seventh mandate, has accomplished a lot of work to provide benefits, protect the rights of workers and create harmony in factories in Cambodia. Nationwide.
He emphasized that these benefits include that the Royal Government of Cambodia has maintained a regular wage increase for workers in 2024, allowing workers to use the CES card. Get free health care and expand the scope of the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) in this seventh mandate. In addition, the Royal Government has continued to provide benefits to pregnant workers during and after childbirth.
He emphasized that the enterprise competition program, a safe community that the Ministry of Labor has just announced, is also a very important task in harmonizing industrial relations in factories in Cambodia.
Along with this support, he requested the Royal Government of Cambodia of the seventh mandate to correct some shortcomings to improve the employment sector in Cambodia, as well as to improve the rights and livelihoods of workers even better. .
At the same time, in addition to the implementation of the six recommendations, there are four other recommendations that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has been showing continuous progress.
