Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth Inaugurates ARDB Bank's New Head Office
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the new head office of ARDB Bank at the new headquarters of the Bank on April 30, 2024. ARDB is located at Building 168, Concrete Street 7, Prek Leap Village, Sangkat Prek Leap, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
The event was also attended by senior leaders of the Royal Government, national and international development partners, customers and staff of ARDB Bank, a total of 500 people.
In addition, the new head office building will be able to serve the society for a long time and can be preserved as a historic building of ARDB Bank so that ARDB Bank can continue to strengthen and expand its role as a development bank in line with regional and global trends. And serving the policies of the Royal Government.
Dr. continued that under the guidance and guidance of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, the new central building of ARDB Bank was designed and inspected by Cambodian architects and engineers, starting to build on an area of 6,102 square meters. July 16, 2021 and completed on December 25, 2023, taking 29 months.
He said that for the future direction, the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank needs to continue to improve its mission and role as a national policy bank in financing rural development and agriculture, participation in the development of the belt. Agriculture and supply, value chain and productivity, in agriculture and rural economy to be more active and strong, more efficient and more prosperous.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said, "I strongly believe that the new head office building will contribute to improving the efficiency and quality of customer service of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture." I would also like to ask the management, officers and staff to take great care to maintain this new building well and clean for long-term use in the future.
In addition to the above achievements, ARDB Bank is also updating its 10-year roadmap (2024-2033) with the vision of becoming a leading financial institution in providing financing to support the development of agriculture, agriculture and industry. Implement projects related to green financing and participation in tackling climate change as well as sustainable development.
(Phnom Penh): The Faculty of Sociology and Anthropology of the Royal University of Phnom Penh organizes the first of a series of seminars on "Introductory Guidelines on the Process of Doctoral Writing and Research Writing" from 26 to 28 months. April 2024 in Kampot province.
