Cambodia-Laos Border Security Cooperation Committee Holds Meeting to Review Progress of Border Security Cooperation
(Phnom Penh): The Commission for Cooperation in Maintaining Order and Security along the Cambodia-Laos Border held a meeting to review the progress of border security cooperation between the two countries and to continue to develop mechanisms related to the work of the Commission. Also. This is according to Major General Thong Solimo, spokesman for the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
Lt. Gen. Thong Solimo said that this was the second meeting held on the morning of April 30, 2024 at the Royal Angkor Resort in Siem Reap, with the Cambodian side led by General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief. Coalition of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chairman of the Commission for Cooperation in Maintaining Order and Security along the Cambodia-Laos Border.
The Lao side is led by Major General Van Thong But Takvong, Deputy Chief of Staff of the Lao People's Army and Chairman of the Commission for Cooperation and Security along the Lao-Cambodian border.
In his opening remarks at the meeting, General Ith Sarath stated that the Commission for Cooperation in Maintaining Order and Security along the Cambodia-Laos Border has an important role to play in coordinating security and order in order to make the border peaceful and professional. Collaborate to prevent all crimes and development.
