The Nobel Prize is divided into peace, literature, physics, chemistry, medicine / physiology, and economics. The Economic Science Award was first established in 1968, while other awards began in 1901.
The selection and awarding of all the above Nobel Prizes is organized annually by institutions in Sweden and Norway. The Nobel Prize ceremony is usually held on December 10, the anniversary of Nobel death. Each Nobel Prize is accompanied by a cash prize of nearly $ 1.4 million, and the winner also receives a gold medal with the Nobel Prize engraved on it.
It should be noted that as of 2022, a total of 567 Nobel Prizes have been awarded to a total of 889 winners, including individuals and institutions, of which 26 are all Nobel Peace Prizes awarded to institutions. On the other hand, because some winners have won multiple awards, the actual total number of winners is 860 individuals and 22 institutions.
