The following are the guidelines of the Ministry of Education: The hot weather and the prolongation of the dry season have prompted Kep to increase salt production to nearly 40,000 tons in the first four months of this year.
(Phnom Penh): In the first four months of 2024, due to the hot weather and the prolongation of the dry season, salt production in Kep province reached nearly 40,000 tons, increasing at a high level, which will increase supply Nationwide demand.
Mr. Phok Sokhen, Director of the Department of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, told Fresh News on April 29, 2024 that in the first four months of 2024, Kep Province produced 37,298 tons of salt compared to last year. The whole year produced only 2,515 tons of salt. However, the price of salt this year has fallen.
He said that in general, salt production in Kep is supplied within the province and in other provinces in the country.
According to Mr. Phok Sokhen, Kep currently has a total of 497.87 hectares of salt fields, 351.50 hectares of salt fields and eight groups of salt farmers.
In the heat of the day, a group of salt-carrying workers, mostly women, in Neak Chambok village, O'Krosar commune, Kep city, Kep province, are busy harvesting salt from the rice fields and pouring it into a warehouse not far from the salt fields.
According to the salt field workers, they carry salt in the field, and in one morning, between 5 am and 9 am, two workers can earn 50,000 riels.
Please be informed that Kampot and Kep are the salt production sites in Cambodia. In 2023, the two provinces produced a total of 81,904 tons of salt on more than 3,000 hectares of salt fields to supply people across the country without importing salt from abroad.
According to the Ministry of Industry, the current salt production area in Cambodia is 3,987.35 hectares, of which 3,489.48 hectares in Kampot and 497.87 hectares in Kep. There are 191 production teams, of which Kampot produced 78,484 tons and Kep produced 3,419 tons. Thirty-two of the 54 handicrafts licensed to use iodized salt.
King of Brunei Darussalam arrives in Cambodia for breakfast with Samdech Techo Hun Sen (Phnom Penh): The King of Brunei Darussalam arrives in Cambodia at around 7pm on Friday. April 29, 2024. His current visit to Cambodia is to spend the morning of April 30 with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Dharma Brother.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, once emphasized that the visit of the King of Brunei Darussalam, Cambodia, now does not have any official meeting, just a morning meal on April 30 with Samdech, whom he respects. Pov (3 siblings, he is the first brother, Mr. Thaksin is the second brother, Samdech Techo is the youngest brother).
According to Samdech Techo, during the trip, the Sultan had Prince Martin as his son, and Samdech Techo had three sons, Samdech Hun Sen, Hun Manit and Hun Many.
Samdech Techo confirmed that after the meal, Samdech will march to the airport to return to the country.
Samdech Techo will receive the King of Brunei and his son at the airport directly and accompany him to the hotel.
Samdech Techo confirmed that it was not strange to receive such a direct visit to the Royal Palace, because in 2011 when Samdech went to Brunei, he drove himself to meet Samdech at the airport and to the hotel. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, King of Brunei, and Thaksin are the closest former leaders in ASEAN. So far, for the ASEAN member countries, only the King of Brunei is the leader of the ASEAN member countries, the oldest and longest ruling.
