The National Anti-Drug Authority issues a press release on the results of drug testing on civil servants and contracted officials (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The National Anti-Drug Authority on April 29, 2024 Issuing a press release showing the results of drug testing on civil servants and contracted officials.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News today, after receiving Regulation No. 01 dated 20 February 2024 on the introduction of strict measures to combat illegal drugs in Ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations, the National Authority for Combating Drugs have respected and complied with the contents of this regulation with the following results:
* As of April 29, 2024, some ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations have assigned to implement this issue by conducting rapid tests for drugs in the urine of civil servants, national police officers, soldiers and contracted officers. A total of 56,445 people, including 76 positive urine drugs, were expelled.
* Issued Instruction No. 001 of the NCDD 3. Issued on April 1, 2024 on Measures to Assign the Implementation of Royal Government Regulation No. 01 on the Use of Test Equipment, Test Methods, Confirmation of Test Results and Action on Drug-Positive People to Strengthen the Effective Implementation of Regulations 01 Regulation of the Royal Government as follows:
First, we have been trying to mobilize additional support from national and international philanthropists for rapid urine drug testing equipment for immediate use.
Second, cooperated with the Ministry of Health to establish a working group to address the abnormal results of rapid drug testing in saline.
Third, opened training courses for key officers of the leading units at both the national and sub-national levels so that the words of those units are understood and the owners of the rapid test for drugs in the urine themselves.
Fourth, instructed the relevant ministries and institutions that fired officials with drugs from the framework to send them for treatment and rehabilitation.
The National Anti-Drug Authority thanked the cooperation of ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations, as well as the public, both inside and outside the country, for their strong support for the implementation of the above issues to protect the well-being and well-being of the people. The dignity of the people and Cambodia.
