Spokesman for the General Commission: 258 more vehicles were inspected and fined on April 29, 2024
According to the spokesperson, for March 29, 2024, the traffic police nationwide inspected and fined a total of 7,119 vehicles, including 5,251 motorcycles and 1,868 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles include: drunken helmets, drug addicts, firearms / badges, etc. In particular, the vehicles include: drunken recycling, bulky goods, speeding, drunken driving without a driver's license and lights.
