Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The leadership of the new government for the past 8 months has been good
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of Cambodia, noted that the new Royal Government led by Samdech Hun Sen has been doing well for the past eight months, maintaining stability, economic growth and inflation in a manageable state. Yes.
In addition to noting the leadership of the new government, Samdech Techo also briefed the Ambassador on the purpose for which he decided to change and transfer power to the next generation of leaders. Samdech Techo stated that this decision was the right decision and the decision in accordance with the wishes of the Cambodian people who trust the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party.
It should be noted that the new Royal Government, led by His Majesty the King Hun Manet, has been energetically leading to continue the sacred mission of the old Royal Government to maintain peace, which ensures the well-being of the people. Economic growth and development have made new achievements to meet the needs of the people.
In order to achieve this great ambition, the Royal Government of Samdech Hun Sen will actively implement its work activities according to its roadmap of the "Pentagon Strategy" which is the political program for building and defending the motherland 2023-2028.
Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1 has two main historical missions:
First, to maintain and nurture peace, which has been difficult to achieve with priceless sacrifice, and to nurture the momentum of economic growth and overall development.
Second, to build and strengthen the foundation for accelerating the development of the nation by going through the milestones of becoming a high-middle-income country by 2030, towards achieving the vision of Cambodia by 2050 by building The resilience of the five sectors: resilience of the public sector, resilience of the economic sector, resilience of the financial sector, resilience of human capital and society, and resilience of the environment and in response to change. The weather.
The "Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1" is designed to increase employment, equity, efficiency and sustainability, aiming to build the foundation towards achieving the Cambodia Vision 2050. The Pentagon strategy is a forward-looking strategy for 25 years that is considered, laid out and implemented in five stages.
The Pentagon strategy focuses on human capital development, economic diversification and competitiveness, private sector and employment development, resilient, sustainable and environmental development, and digital economic and social development. .
