(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of Cambodia, expressed his desire to see Cambodia and Turkey organize more events to celebrate the 65th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries in 2024. Samdech Techo also expressed his desire to see Cambodia and Turkey launch direct flights to expand people-to-people contacts between the two countries, as well as boost tourism, business and trade.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo expressed his pleasure to meet with the Ambassador again after meeting in August 2022 after she became the Turkish Ambassador to Cambodia.
At the time, the prince discussed with her the strengthening of cooperation between Cambodia and Turkey and other issues, especially Turkey's request for EU membership and the war between Russia and Ukraine. Now that he has taken over the presidency of the Senate, he will further strengthen relations between the Cambodian Senate and the Turkish Parliament. Samdech Techo also sent a message through the Ambassador to visit the President of Turkey.
The Turkish Ambassador expressed her pleasure at the meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as it is an honor for him to allow her to pay a courtesy call. The Ambassador expressed her condolences over the incident that took place over the weekend that claimed the lives of Cambodian soldiers. She also prayed for a speedy recovery for the injured.
Taking the opportunity of this meeting, the Ambassador of Turkey congratulated Samdech Techo on his election as President of the Senate and wished Samdech Techo and all senators success. She also conveyed a message from the Speaker of the Turkish Parliament to Samdech Techo.
The Ambassador expressed her pleasure and pride at seeing the steady development of relations between Cambodia and Turkey. The two countries have agreed to boost trade to $ 1 billion in the near future. The ambassador also wants to see more people-to-people exchanges between the two countries.
During the meeting, Ms. Ul Kulko Chafe also reminded of the cooperation between Cambodia and Turkey, especially the cooperation with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. These include the expansion of schools and the continuous increase in the provision of scholarships to Cambodian students.
She also mentioned that Turkish Airlines plans to expand flights to Cambodia in the near future and hopes that this connection will further enhance people-to-people contacts.
She also stressed that Turkey will strengthen cooperation in the region and asked Cambodia to support Turkey in its relations with ASEAN. She hopes that the President of the Senate will increase relations with the Turkish parliament to a higher level in the near future.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, thanked the Ambassador for her condolences over the incident that took place this weekend and left 20 Cambodian soldiers dead and several others injured.
Samdech Techo also thanked the Ambassador for congratulating Samdech on becoming the current President of the Senate. Samdech Techo also thanked the President of the Turkish Parliament for sending a congratulatory message.
Samdech Techo, President of the Senate, said that in the fifth mandate of the Senate, Samdech will focus on foreign affairs. Regarding bilateral relations, Samdech Techo said that the trade volume between Cambodia and Turkey is still small, which is not yet worthy of the potential that both countries have.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia, has invited the President of the Turkish Parliament to attend the Inter-Parliamentary Forum on Tolerance and Peace and the 12th General Assembly of the International Conference of Asian Political Parties (ICAPP), which Cambodia will host during November 2024 is coming.
FUNCINPEC Party Supports Prek Chik Funan-Techo Project
(Phnom Penh): FUNCINPEC Party, with Prince Norodom Chakravuth as its President, has announced its full support for the Royal Government's consideration and commitment in digging the Funan-Techo Canal and encouraging the successful implementation of this project.
Please note that Prek Fun-Techo project is a project to connect waterways between rivers to the sea of Cambodia, passing through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep, about 180 kilometers long. The project is expected to cost about $ 1.7 billion and will be studied in detail over a period of 26 months.
This project was approved by the Royal Government of Cambodia for the sixth term in 2023, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and also supported by the new Royal Government led by Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet.
Both Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the current President of the Senate, and Samdech Manet, Hun Manet, have pledged their commitment to digging the Funan-Techo canal for economic benefits, especially the connection of Cambodia's rivers and seas. .
This historic project has the support of Cambodians from all walks of life, both inside and outside the country, because they all see the great benefits and values of this canal. Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works sent a team to cut down fallen trees on the way out immediately after the strong wind to facilitate traffic for citizens
