China's gold output and consumption rise in Q1
BEIJING: China's gold output and consumption rose steadily in the first quarter of 2024, industry data showed on Friday. According to the Xinhua news agency.
However, the consumption of gold jewelry in the Chinese market fell 3 percent from the same period last year to 183,922 tons, while gold bullion and gold earrings rose 26.77 percent year on year. Will be the same period last year to 106,323 tons.
Gold consumption for industry and other uses rose 3.09 percent in the first quarter of this year from a year earlier to 18.66 tonnes. According to the Xinhua news agency.
