(Phnom Penh): Three senators from the Khmer Will Party, through a joint petition of the Senate, announced their support for the implementation of the Funan-Techo canal project and strongly opposed the bad intentions of friends who tried to hinder development and progress. Cambodia's economy.
The three senators are: Dr. Sok Hach, Mr. Kong Monica and Mr. Seng Mardy. They joined the petition together with a total of 61 other senators to support the implementation of the Funan-Techo Canal Project.
"We, the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia, fully support the implementation of the Funan-Techo Prek Chik project, an initiative of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, former Director," the petition states. Minister and President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia. At present, the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly is continuing its work and further promoting the development of this canal project to be successful in the future.
The senators also strongly support and encourage the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly to continue to successfully develop this Funan-Techo canal project for both socio-economic benefits and to ensure independence and national sovereignty.
The three senators also called on all citizens to support with the will and courage to contribute to the prosperity of the motherland of Cambodia, and strongly oppose all the bad intentions of friends who try to hinder development and progress. Cambodia's economy.
The inauguration ceremony of a new stone house was presided over by Mrs. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross and her colleagues, along with the leaders and youth officials of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Kampong Chhnang.
During the inauguration ceremony of the new stone house, the Cambodian Red Cross also supported 35 families living nearby, each family received 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish, 1 can of fish sauce, 1 kit ( 1 sarong, 1 mosquito net, 1 blanket and 1 krama) and 20,000 Riels.
During the meeting, the First Deputy Secretary-General sent a message of greetings and deep sympathy from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all the people.
Taking this opportunity, she thanked all the philanthropists from all walks of life who donated generously to the Cambodian Red Cross, especially on the occasion of World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, so that the Cambodian Red Cross can afford to To alleviate the hardships of the most vulnerable and vulnerable people, in fact, today, the Cambodian Red Cross has brought gifts to distribute to you now.
She added that Cambodia is currently suffering from climate change, extreme heat and water shortages almost everywhere, please use water sparingly, and after this warming, Cambodia will have a lot of lightning. So in the coming rainy season, be careful when it rains and beware of dengue fever, please clean the environment around the house, get rid of mosquitoes, as the old saying goes, "prevention is better than cure."
Finally, Mrs. Men Neary Sopheak prayed to the New Year Angel named Mahotra Devi to bless all the people.
