Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Crack Down on Drug Trafficking, Arrest 4 Chinese Nationals and Nearly 6 Kilograms of Drugs
(Preah Sihanouk): The Anti-Drug Police Force cracked down on a case of drug trafficking and processing in Village 1, Sangkat 2, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province, detaining 4 suspects before and after. Chinese nationals and nearly 6 kilograms of drugs and confiscated some exhibits. This is according to the report of Sihanoukville Provincial Police.
A report from the Sihanoukville Provincial Police said that the operation was carried out on the orders of Lieutenant General and Deputy Commissioner of Police of Sihanoukville on April 24, 2024, initially detaining two Chinese nationals. On the afternoon of April 25, 2024, the police continued to detain two more suspects (one female) who were Chinese and confiscated some exhibits.
In addition, there are 8 mobile phones, 6 drug scales, 3 passports, 3 bank cards, 1 motorbike, processing equipment and some drug packaging bags.
According to the Sihanoukville Provincial Police, the four victims and their exhibits are being processed by specialized police officers and sent to court for further legal proceedings.
(Phnom Penh): The Chbar Ampov Market Commission and market vendors have come out in full support for the implementation of the Funan-Techo Canal Project, the first historic canal in Cambodia, an initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Director. Minister and President of the Senate, and currently Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has continued to work and push further in the development of the Funan-Techo canal project to achieve in the future.
Seeing the many benefits of Prek Chik Funan Techo project, people all over the country, including government officials from all walks of life, have issued a petition in support of this important Prek Chik Funan Techo project. As the words of the business people, the informal business people.
This confirmation was made during a meeting with more than 5,000 informal economic unions and academic staff associations to celebrate International Labor Day on May 1, 2024.
On that occasion, Samdech President said that some people mentioned to Samdech that they want to set up a fund, want to set up a bank account so that other people can contribute to support the Prek Chik Funan-Techo project.
"Right now, we do not have the need for you to contribute to the budget, we have been thinking about the financial project for many years, we are very thankful for the spirit of support, the spirit of nationalism, this is "The force is huge, bigger than the $ 10 billion budget."
"Our home is peaceful, harmonious, and together we will build new achievements for ourselves and our children," he said. Our owners have passed on to their descendants for decades.
Samdech asked not to set up a fund or raise any money at all, lest there be any opportunists, the Royal Government has no plans to raise funds from you to implement this project, just ask for support as a force for nationalism.
He added that, with or without the participation of foreign investors, Cambodia must make this canal project irreversible, we have already prepared three scenarios to ensure that if Without funds from foreign investment, Cambodia, we will make it until there is no loss.
His Excellency Hun Manet made the call on the occasion of his meeting with more than 5,000 informal economic unions and academic staff associations to celebrate International Labor Day on May 28, 2024.
"I would like to call on all Cambodians of all faiths and religions to join the Royal Government of Cambodia in supporting the successful construction of the Funan-Techo Canal Project so that we can all see it," he said. .
"Cambodia has a lot of achievements and they are all historic achievements that we have made in the previous mandate and in this mandate, in this mandate, we have inaugurated an international airport in Siem Reap," he said. A history and in 2025 Cambodia will open a new airport in Phnom Penh, another level of history as well.
Please be informed that Prek Chik Funan-Techo project is a project to connect waterways between rivers to the sea of Cambodia, passing through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep provinces, about 180 kilometers long. The project is expected to cost about 1.7 billion US dollars and has been studied in detail.
