This statement was made on the occasion that Samdech Hun Sen met with 5,187 informal economic unions and the Association of Cambodian Academic Students to celebrate the 138th Anniversary of International Labor Day, May 1, 2024, this morning. April 28, 2024.
"I would like to thank His Excellency the Minister as well as the Cambodian people throughout the country for their active support in relation to the Funan-Techo Canal Project," he said.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that people, both inside and outside the country, of all political persuasions, have issued messages of support to ensure that Cambodia has a way to breathe itself and strengthen its economy through the construction of the Funan-Techo canal.
At the same time, Samdech President Hun Manet confirmed that the Prek Chik Funan-Techo project is not for the benefit of the "Hun" family, but for the benefit of all Cambodians. Samdech President Hun Manet emphasized that Samdech will continue the mission of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to make Funan-Techo canal dive.
Please be informed that Prek Chik Funan-Techo project is a project to connect waterways between rivers to the sea of Cambodia, passing through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep provinces, about 180 kilometers long. The project is expected to cost about $ 1.7 billion and has been studied in detail.
On the evening of April 26, 2024, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, strongly announced his decision to build the Funan-Techo Canal in the near future. Provide great benefits to the nation and the people of Cambodia.
This statement of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet was made on the morning of Sunday, 5 Roch Khe Chet, the year of Rong Chhasak, B.E. 2567 is on April 28, 2024, on the occasion of Samdech's invitation to talk with informal economic unions and the association of approximately 5,187 Khmer academic staff.
Samdech President Hun Manet claimed that Samdech will continue the mission of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister, to make Funan-Techo canal possible. And the construction of the Funan-Techo canal is a historic responsibility for leadership, so there is a very clear impact study.
The Prime Minister stated: "Cambodia implements the law and the Mekong River Commission in 1995, the 1995 Mekong Agreement is not required, especially in the tributaries of some countries, he builds hydropower in five or six tributaries." There is no obligation to report, but Cambodia has provided this information to the Mekong Commission responsibly. ”
In addition, President Hun Manet said that through the Funan Techo canal project, fresh water will flow into various irrigation systems to serve agriculture and water transport.
"And other countries are building canals similar to ours, they are building dams, they are building hydropower, they can do it. Why is Cambodia a special country? This canal must be done for the socio-economic interests of Cambodia. This is the additional emphasis of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet.
