(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, organized a program to express his gratitude to the leaders of all generations of civil servants who have worked hard to sacrifice physical, mental, intellectual and spiritual strength to build and develop Oddar Meanchey province for continuous progress. 25th Anniversary of the announcement of the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration.
Oddar Meanchey was the last province in the country to achieve integration to end the chronic civil war on December 28, 1998 under the win-win political strategy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, ending the Cold War completely out of Cambodia.
Oddar Meanchey province has 1 municipality and 4 districts, including Samrong, Anlong Veng, Trapeang Prasat, Chong Kal and Banteay Ampil districts, including 19 communes and 5 communes and 308 villages. Oddar Meanchey province has three border checkpoints with Thailand, including the Choam International Border Crossing in Anlong Veng District, the O'Smach International Border Crossing in Samrong City, and the Chob Koki International Border Crossing in Banteay Ampil District.
Dr. Lim Oun, CEO of SME Bank, said that while some banks are promoting digital lending, traders or small business owners should also increase their knowledge of digital skills to easily apply for a loan over the phone. And for the convenience of their business as well.
He noted that small business owners or small business owners face many challenges in obtaining official loans from banks or microfinance institutions due to their small loan size, which some banks are reluctant to lend. Because the cost of operations or staff is more than they can afford to benefit from small customers.
However, the launch of a digital lending system will make it easier for small business owners to get financing for their business operations.
He said, "The government has taken some action to promote this work, while some association banks have already taken action. "Therefore, business people as well as some business owners should dedicate time to study more to increase their knowledge of digital."
He said that in order to ensure higher access to finance, stakeholders, both banking institutions and borrowers, must work together to promote this work, as both small and large sources of capital are important for business owners to ensure access to finance. Sustainability and growth of its business.
He added that if business owners do not learn more about this technology, they will still face the risk of getting a loan. And in the future, if technology advances, the banking system may not pay staff for small-scale lending as it used to be.
