Mondulkiri Provincial Government Working Group Holds First Quarter Meeting in 2024
(Mondulkiri): Mr. Chuon Vin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Mondulkiri Province, chaired a meeting to review the results of the first quarter of 2024 of the Royal Government Working Group on Mondulkiri Province. Kiri, which took place at Mondulkiri Provincial Hall.
The meeting held on Friday afternoon, April 26, 2024 was also attended by Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Mondulkiri Provincial Board of Governors, Chairman, Deputy Chairman of the Working Group, as well as members of the Royal Working Group. The government visited Mondulkiri province, relevant officials from all units around the province and many other dignitaries.
According to the report, in the first quarter of 2024, the Royal Government Working Group visited Mondulkiri Province to support and implement the 6 priority policy programs and 5 key measures of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, including supporting and promoting Implement the policy of safe villages, communes, sangkats, reform, decentralization and deconcentration, providing services to the people through the OWSO mechanism.
In particular, the five key measures that the Royal Government working group has contributed significantly to the implementation are: (1) the reform program on the public sector (2) the reform program on the education sector (3) to promote the implementation and strengthening Health work (4) Anti-drug work and (5) Legal and judicial reform.
Mr. Chuon Vin encouraged all local government working groups to continue their efforts to implement the work effectively to achieve success in all work under its jurisdiction in accordance with the goals and political programs of the Royal Government.
