The loss of the former Khmer territory came about as the Cambodian leaders at the time allowed neighboring countries to borrow land in the upper Mekong region to grow rice and train troops to fight the war. To another country.
400 years later, the Royal Government of Cambodia, the sixth legislature of the National Assembly, led by the Cambodian People's Party, studied the Funan Canal, the first waterway to the sea in recent Cambodian history. This will provide significant benefits for Cambodia in terms of economic, social development and contribute to the protection and preservation of ecosystems and biodiversity in the region.
