Comment: Allegations of production surplus are just an excuse to stifle China's growth
In 2012, the European Commission accused China of exporting low-cost solar products to European markets, hurting domestic suppliers, and initiated a 47.6% tariff on its products. Those in order to reduce China's competitive advantage. Later in July 2013, China and the European Union resolved the issue peacefully.
Allegations that China's clean energy surplus has undermined global value and production patterns are an inflated propaganda aimed at undermining China's competitive advantage. China's efficient production capacity has really injected new impetus into the global energy revolution, contrary to the false claims of the United States and Europe.
