(Kratie): While parents were busy collecting cashews for their children, three boys and a girl went on a trip to the Mekong River and drowned, killing two and one sister, a fisherman nearby. That sees timely rescue.
This horrific incident happened on the evening of April 24, 2024 at Yav village, Kampong Cham commune, Sambo district, Kratie province. The bodies of the two children were found on the afternoon of April 26, 2024.
According to villagers, at 4:30 on April 24, 2024, the three boys and girls went to bathe in the Mekong River with other children nearby. While taking a bath, a 9-year-old boy, Sot Muth, was the first to drown. Water both at once.
On the day of the incident, the boy's parents were busy picking cashew nuts for them, leaving them with their grandmother. The victim's mother, Kan Vy, 31, and father, Long Vannak, 57, live in the same commune.
In that incident, the villagers and local authorities intervened to search for the bodies for two days before finding the bodies of the two boys on the afternoon of April 26 at Anlong Preah Kor village, Vattanac commune, Sambo district, Kratie province.
The body was handed over to the relatives for a traditional ceremony at home, and this afternoon, Mr. Chhit Nonn, Kampong Cham Commune Chief, together with the commune village team, brought 685,000 Riels and 2 rice to the family. 15 bottles of pure water as well.
General knowledge: How do solar and lunar eclipses occur?
(Phnom Penh): Eclipses can only occur during the Earth's orbit and the Moon around the Sun, the three objects reach a point where they are arranged in a straight line by the Sun. And the earth is on one side of the moon. As for the eclipse, it is when the earth is between the sun and the moon. Generally, solar eclipses and lunar eclipses occur between 2-5 times a year.
1. A total solar eclipse: It occurs when we look at the earth, the moon obscuring the sun almost immediately. This type of solar eclipse can only be seen in a small part of the earth when it occurs.
2. Incomplete solar eclipse: It occurs when we look from the earth, the sun is not obscured by the moon, it can occur below 100 percent, the sun is still just softer. A little.
Officials, who asked not to be named, said Israel had not made any new proposals but was open to considering a limited ceasefire, provided that Hamas released 33 hostages instead of the previous 40 talks.
The talks did not involve direct talks between Israel and Hamas regarding the hostages, but an Egyptian attempt to resume talks with an Egyptian request that would require the release of 33 hostages. This includes elderly and disabled women.
Israeli intelligence estimates that 33 of the 133 hostages, women and the elderly were being held by Hamas and other Palestinian militants in the Gaza Strip.
The duration of any possible ceasefire has not been determined, but it is stressed that if an agreement is reached, the hostilities are likely to last less than six weeks.
The Egyptian delegation's visit comes after the United States and 17 other countries urged Hamas to release all hostages as part of resolving the Gaza crisis. However, Hamas responded by rejecting international pressure and vowed not to give up. Cambodia promotes support for "open science" at OECD Ministerial Conference
(Phnom Penh): At the Ministerial Conference of the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD) on 24 April 2024 in Paris, Cambodia reaffirmed its commitment to support "Open Science". ) »And ready to engage with the international community to address key global issues such as climate change and public health crises.
In his intervention for the Conference of Leaders and Policymakers on Science, Technology and Innovation, Mr. Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, emphasized the potential of the evolution of open science, which is a catalyst for progress and can help. Countries solve complex problems more effectively.
Addressing the conference, the Minister called on stakeholders, including scientists, policy makers, educators and the people to work together to promote this open science initiative.
"Let us work together to create a future where science serves the common good of all and is a driving force for sustainable development and global prosperity," he said.
At the same time, he also briefed on the agenda of Cambodia's technological revolution, emphasizing the process of integrating science, technology and innovation into the Royal Government's strategy, including sectoral roadmaps, including education technology roadmaps. Up to green technology roadmap to capture the potential of each sector.
