Sea Cleanup Organization in collaboration with Kandal Provincial Administration celebrates the 5th "Good Day" to encourage people to love the environment, pack and store garbage properly
Nou Sovann, executive director of the Clean Sea Rivers Organization, said this afternoon that environmental issues, rising temperatures, floods, droughts and water shortages were threatening global problems caused by individuals in all sectors of the country. That requires the participation of all.
"Just getting involved in tree planting and proper waste disposal in Cambodia can also help bring some improvements to the global environment," he said. "Therefore, Cambodia's involvement with the world is necessary to address global environmental issues."
He said that the Sea Cleanup Organization helped clean up the Bassac River on the day of the Royal Water Festival, Ok Ambok, to worship the moon in front of the boat race forum. More than 5 tons of garbage was collected and another 15 tons in the Chaktomuk River.
He added that from 2020 to April 2024, the Sea Cleanup Organization collected 1,750 tons of garbage from the Mekong, Tonle Sap and Tonle Bassac rivers, which is a good deed for the benefit of people across the country. Attract tourists and take care of our natural resources.
It should be noted that in Cambodia, the Day of Goodness began in early 2020, when the 19 season of Kovid is spreading rapidly throughout the country and the world.
However, a group of volunteers from the Clean Sea Rivers Organization, led by a young man named Hong Kibora, the head of the Rivers Cleanup Mission, raised funds from local and foreign philanthropists and distributed food to some poor people to facilitate. To daily life in those difficult times.
It should be noted that good deeds are simple actions that give any positive effect, big or small, which makes it better for human life, animals and the sustainability of nature. Good deeds come from each of us from good thoughts, good words and good deeds, and the results will be better for us, our families, our villages, our provinces, our country and our world.
