The island nation's economy is projected to shrink 2.3 percent in 2023 after a slump in 2022 as it plunged into its worst financial crisis since gaining independence from the United Kingdom in 2023. 1948 and after the decline in foreign exchange reserves to a record low in early 2022.
"Sri Lanka has not completely emerged from the crisis," Reuters reported, citing a report released by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. "There is no space that can cause a fall from the promised path."
