Mr. Pich Sros's remarks came after Cambodian opposition politician Sam Rainsy, who was living in France, escaped the Cambodian legal trap on April 25, 2024, to oppose the Funan Techo canal project. Sam Rainsy also painted the project like a Vietnamese researcher, saying that the project serves the Chinese military.
The 180-kilometer-long Funan-Techo canal project connecting the waterways between the rivers and the sea of Cambodia is of great benefit to Cambodians. This project is supported by the Cambodian people, both inside and outside the country, even if the Cambodians tend to oppose the Royal Government of Cambodia living abroad.
Political Analyst: Prek Chik Funan Techo Leads to National Unity and Pride
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's Funan Techo canal project has become a focal point of national pride and unity among the Cambodian people throughout the country.
This important infrastructure project aims to create a waterway that can navigate the Mekong River to the Gulf, has received strong support and admiration from people from all walks of life in Cambodian society. From government officials to local communities, it is clear that Prek Chun Funan Techo represents an important opportunity for Cambodia's economic development, connectivity and national progress.
To understand the importance of the Funan Techo canal to the Cambodian people, it is essential to understand the historical context of Cambodia. Cambodia, with its rich cultural heritage and history, has long been associated with rivers and waterways. Ancient civilizations, such as those of Funan and Angkor, relied on trade and water transport, demonstrating the importance of the maritime network in Cambodian history.
At the heart of Cambodia's solidarity with the Funan Techo Canal is Cambodia's economic potential. This canal is seen as changing the destiny of Cambodia, leading to smoother transportation of goods, reducing transportation costs and opening up new business opportunities for Cambodians. On the other hand, the project is expected to boost economic growth, create jobs and attract investment to other parts of Cambodia.
For Cambodian businesses and entrepreneurs, this canal represents a gateway to regional and global markets. The canal will also pave the way for expansion, diversification and increased competition in the region. The prospect of better connectivity through the canal has drawn the support of the private sector and institutions, with many seeing it as an important mechanism for Cambodia's economic transformation.
In addition, the canal project is expected to boost urban development along the canal road, with new economic zones, residential areas and commercial centers emerging in the future. The prospect of this joint development, along with opportunities for both rural and urban areas, has received strong support and admiration from the Cambodian people, except for politicians who want to destroy Cambodia, who oppose the project.
While the economic and development aspects of the Funan Techo canal are paramount, the Cambodian government is also concerned about environmental sustainability. The project includes measures to reduce environmental impacts, preserve natural habitats and ensure responsible water management. This balanced approach combines economic development with environmental management in line with the Cambodian ethic of harmony with nature.
Cambodia must overcome all obstacles to build this historic project, and all Cambodians must support and have a common spirit with the current Cambodian government led by the Cambodian People's Party.
The strong solidarity among the Cambodian people regarding the Funan Techo canal further strengthened the support of the government and led to the active participation of the public. The government has set a clear vision for the canal project, emphasizing the economic potential and benefits that the canal will bring to the Cambodian nation.
By: Dr. Son Sam is a Policy Analyst of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and Deputy Director of the Department of Public Relations and Protocol of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, National Assembly of the Cambodian National Confederation of Trade Unions.
