A man was hacked by a neighbor in Takhmao City, causing serious head injuries, the assailant was immediately arrested by police
(Central): Starting from a feud between neighbors, a man was stabbed in the house by another man armed with a machete, causing serious head injuries. The incident of violence occurred on the afternoon of April 24, 2024 in Prek Anchanh village, Sangkat Prek Russey, Takhmao city, Kandal province.
According to the report of Takhmao City Police Inspectorate, the victim, Keo Neang, 60 years old, resides in Prek Anchanh Village, Sangkat Prek Russey, Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
Police confirmed that at the time of the incident, the victim was sitting in the house, suddenly the suspect on a motorcycle arrived home, took a machete at his chicken coop and went to cut the victim, causing severe head bleeding and serious injuries. The suspect ran back to his house.
The victim was later taken by his family to Victory Hospital for treatment. As for the suspect, the Prek Russey police force, in cooperation with the Takhmao City Criminal Force, detained the suspect, brought him in for questioning and built a case file according to the procedure. In front of the police, the suspect confessed that he was angry with the victim and also used a machete to cut the victim's head, bleeding for sure.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Justice has issued a new announcement announcing the launch of the Digital Judgment Bulletin Service in the second phase from May 2, 2024.
The Ministry of Justice has launched a pilot phase of the first phase of the Digital Judgment Bulletin Service on February 6, 2023, which will make it easier for the public to access comprehensive information and to complete the Judgment Bulletin application. Punishment from a distance.
To further facilitate and expedite the public's request for a bulletin, the Ministry of Justice will launch a second phase of the digital bulletin service from May 2, 2024.
The launch of the second phase of the Digital Judgment Bulletin will facilitate and allow applicants to complete the Judgment Bulletin application by attaching some necessary documents online and making electronic payments. ).
On the day of receipt of the Judgment Bulletin, the public in the country must come to the Judiciary Department of the Ministry of Justice in person and receive the relevant original documents, and for the public abroad, Directly at the Cambodian Embassy or Consulate or at the nearest post office and attach the relevant original documents.
Please note that the public can still come and fill out the application form for the bulletin directly at the Department of Judgment Affairs of the Ministry of Justice, as has been done in the past. HE Khoy Khun Hour and Lok Chumteav Un Sokunthea Donate 1 Million Riels to Kantha Bopha Hospital through Humanitarian Football Tournament Led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen
