(Phnom Penh): A group of 14 hippies riding 7 motorbikes, armed with swords, knives and machete, cut two victims on the back and front (24 stitches) in Kakap commune 1 Khan Po Sen Chey has been arrested by the Phnom Penh Armed Forces and is building a case to send to court while other factions are pursuing arrest.
After receiving a complaint from the victim's family, the Phnom Penh Municipal Armed Forces in Po Sen Chey district conducted a search and arrested the perpetrator, Lay Makara, a 19-year-old male, and brought him to the district for interrogation. Procedural answers. The suspect confessed that on the day of the incident, he and several other accomplices actually chased the victim, causing real injuries.
The suspect is currently being investigated by the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie's Office of Criminal Investigation and sent to court for legal action. . Bank of Thailand to cut interest rates by 0.25% for vulnerable customers
BANGKOK: Bank of Thailand will lower its lending rate by 25 basis points, or 0.25 percent, to vulnerable groups for six months, the Banking Association of Thailand said on Thursday. According to Reuters.
The decision comes after Thai Prime Minister Setha Thavisin said this week that he had asked four major Thai lenders to cut interest rates to help small businesses and the economy. Setha has repeatedly urged the Bank of Thailand to cut interest rates to boost the economy.
The Banking Association of Thailand said the move would ease the interest burden, but did not specify how many banks would be involved in the initiative. According to Reuters.
Blinken's visit represents the latest in high-level relations between the two countries, which have helped reduce hostilities that reached unprecedented levels last year. Despite persistent tensions, the efforts of the working group on trade and military relations eased the atmosphere of confrontation.
During a meeting with top Chinese official in Shanghai, Chen Jining, Blinken expressed concern about China's trade policies and practices that are different from market principles. He stressed the importance of fair economic competition and equal respect for American workers and companies operating in China.
In response, Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Wang Wenbin reiterated China's commitment to economic and trade cooperation based on international market principles. Wang called for mutual respect for the principles of fair competition, adherence to WTO rules.
The case of bokator teacher for a fee! Ministry of Education spokesman says the ministry encourages each school to add arts and sports programs to students' preferences
Her statement after seeing the broadcast that bokator instructors in private schools are too expensive to be included in the curriculum. At the same time, this martial art is not yet taught in public schools.
"Currently, the ministry has incorporated arts and sports programs into the school," the spokesman said. In addition to basic education in these two subjects, each school can also add arts and sports programs to suit local student interests and available resources. In the past, some schools have already started trying out sports. ”
Recently, an expert on Khmer civilization, Mr. Rath Sandab, also asked all stakeholders, whether the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Cambodian Bokator Federation and bokator teachers to jointly develop this martial art to be trained in the field of education. According to Mr. Rath, listening to bokator is a national martial art that we must promote, especially in the public and private schools.
The request of Khmer civilization experts after the Bokator Federation of Cambodia rejected the opinion that bokator teachers charge too much for training services.
Countries with national martial arts like Korea promote taekwondo, while Japan promotes karate, as China promotes kung fu, and according to Un Jim, a political science and culture scholar, both public and private schools should teach. Bokator for students is both a sport and a martial art. It is an exercise for students to be healthy and a fighting style for students to protect themselves from enemies.
Mr. Un Chim also suggested that stakeholders have the idea to promote bokator, a traditional Khmer martial art, Khmer culture to revive, stating that "do this to strengthen our bokator."
Mr. Kong Samneang stated, "It is a bit difficult to find teachers and teachers seem to charge too much, which increases the cost of school." Intentionally, we also want to put. "Private wants to raise the value of national culture, especially bokator, but the price is too high."
Mr. Kong Samneang claimed that the intention of the private school was to raise the price of Khmer martial arts, but because the instructors were too expensive, it made it difficult for the school to organize because the cost increased if bokator was added during school hours.
Mr. San Kim Sean, Dr. Kramas Meas, Elder of the Golden Bokator Academy of Cambodia, claimed that the paid bokator instructors may not be from the Academy of Bokator of Cambodia. Legal bokator teachers must be from the Cambodian Bokator Academy, and he is not responsible for instructors from the federation.
According to San Kim Sean, the Cambodian Bokator Academy is setting up a training ground for professional teachers.
Please be informed that bokator is a traditional Khmer martial art that is deeply rooted in Cambodian society for centuries and continues to survive in Cambodian society until today. The carvings on the walls of Angkorian temples are clear evidence of this martial art practice. The training of bokator from generation to generation is to strengthen the wisdom and ability to defend themselves from wild animals and enemies, as well as to protect the society and the motherland.
For Mr. Rath Sandab suggested that if the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports together with the Federation of Cambodian Bokator facilitates the training of bokator in the field of education, this national martial arts will grow throughout the country.
