Owners of unregistered and updated properties have the opportunity to receive administrative sanctions waivers until the end of June
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to grant property tax exemption by exempting administrative penalties, including additional taxes and interest on real estate not yet registered with the tax administration (never paid property tax) or properties declared and paid. Taxes were incorrect last year.
The weekly newsletter of the General Department of Taxation, published on April 25, 2024, states that in order to receive the exemption of administrative sanctions, property owners must hurry to register or update their property information at the General Department of Taxation or The tax branch where the property is located before the end of June 2024.
For immovable property that has been repeatedly transferred or occupied, the property tax is exempt from the tax from the time the last owner acquired the right to occupy the property, but the property owner must hurry to register the property. Get it before the end of June 2024.
In addition, the General Department of Taxation also provides important documents that property owners need to prepare for property registration or update property information.
Taxpayers who own property worth more than 100,000,000 Riels are required to register with the tax administration in the geographical area where the property is located or at the General Department of Taxation no later than September 30 of the taxable year.
In order to register to pay property tax, the taxpayer who owns the property must prepare some important documents such as:
The taxpayer must provide information to the tax administration (property information update) by enclosing the documents specified above, along with the receipt of the previous tax payment or property identification number (PIN) or ID card. Property tax payment for property that:
* The tax base is changed as land is used to build houses, buildings and / or structures, or houses, buildings and structures are added or reduced or demolished * Property is changed, owner, occupant or beneficiary The last of the real estate.
