Armenian police have arrested 96 people in connection with an anti-government protest in Yerevan on Wednesday, local media and Russian news agencies reported. This is according to the release of Reuters on Thursday, April 25, 2024.
Protesters blocked traffic roads in the city center and police did not listen to their instructions, so forced to break the demonstration. Armenian Prime Minister Nikol Pashinyan is facing domestic criticism after agreeing to hand over some border areas to his neighbor and longtime rival, Azerbaijan, as part of a peace deal.
Armenia is a party to the Russian peace treaty and has traditional ties in the South Caucasus, but bilateral relations have deteriorated sharply in recent years as Yerevan seeks to build ties with the West. Blame Russia for its failure to defend Armenia from Azerbaijan.
