(Stung Treng): Mr. Thong Sran, Deputy Governor of Stung Treng Province and Ms. Kang Savorn, Provincial Councilor, celebrated the 26th National Cultural Day on March 3, 2024 under the theme "Youth for National Culture" organized by the Provincial Administration in collaboration with Department of Culture and Fine Arts of Stung Treng Province at Stung Treng Provincial Hall on April 24, 2024.
Ms. Nouch Saroeun, Director of the Provincial Department of Culture, stated that 2024 is the 26th time to celebrate the Cultural Day and for the past 9 years, the National Cultural Day has been celebrated under the same theme: Youth for National Culture to promote awareness. From all walks of life, about the endless task of preserving the national arts and culture, about the obligations that are necessary for the youth to take turns.
She added that the purpose of this event is to contribute to the preservation, protection and promotion of the values of arts, culture and fine traditions of our nation, aimed at increasing the love for cultural heritage, increase awareness of the value and diversity of national arts and culture. To all the masses through dissemination, training and cultural arts events that focus on the participation of young people to be better in line with the goals of Cambodia, the Kingdom of Culture.
Mr. Thong Sran said that the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Hun Sen, always pays attention to celebrate this National Cultural Day every year to commemorate the merits and achievements of our ancestors, who have left a rich cultural heritage to future generations. Next.
The Deputy Governor continued that the celebration of the National Cultural Day on March 3 is to promote the transfer of knowledge, food, technical skills and cultural talent, as well as to remind and inspire all people, especially young people who are vines. Bamboo successors have an obligation to preserve and sustain the national and multicultural culture of ethnic communities in the Kingdom of Cambodia under the theme "Youth for Culture."
The Deputy Governor of Stung Treng Province added: “The participation of young people in the field of arts and culture is indispensable for the socio-economic and prevention of the spread of other cultures that can affect the originality of our culture. "Respect for the national culture is easy to say, but in order to have true respect, we first need to have a good understanding of the national art and culture and to participate in all aspects of protecting and promoting our national culture."
He said that in this regard, training, dissemination and awareness raising increase the opportunity to participate, create more attractiveness to the general public, especially young people, and strengthen the respect for the culture, both tangible and intangible of the nation. Pursat Governor. Request the permanent forces in the development area of Bun Rany Sen Chey village, Damnak Troyeung to cooperate in preventing and suppressing all forest crime activities
