The 180-kilometer-long Funan-Techo canal project connecting the waterways between the rivers and the sea of Cambodia is of great benefit to Cambodians. This project is supported by the Cambodian people, both inside and outside the country, even if the Cambodians tend to oppose the Royal Government of Cambodia living abroad.
However, Cambodia's historic canal project has been criticized by some Vietnamese researchers and accused of serving China's military interests. Initially, it was thought that only Vietnam opposed the project and tried to paint a link to China's military geography to thwart the project because it was detrimental to its economic interests.
Suddenly, on the morning of Thursday, April 25, 2024, this is the most shocking story, a veteran opposition politician, Mr. Sam Rainsy, who is living in France, escaping the law of Cambodia, also came out to oppose this project. Also. Sam Rainsy also painted the project to serve the Chinese military, as well as some Vietnamese scholars.
Mr. Sam Rainsy's message against the Funan-Techo canal project is an act of self-immolation, causing Cambodians from all walks of life to express strong anger with Mr. Sam Rainsy.
Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, expressed surprise and outrage. He considered Sam Rainsy's message to be stupid and completely betrayed the nation's strategic interests.
"I do not think that in the 21st century, as a prominent politician, I do not understand the geography, politics and strategic interests of the nation." Mr. Kin Phea emphasized.
"Although this message was written to undermine the ruling party's national development plan for personal political gain or to be used by any neighbor or superpower," he said. "Stupid acts and betrayal to the whole national interest."
Cambodians on Facebook and Tektok have also reacted and expressed their outrage at the opposition leader Sam Rainsy.
In addition to the messages quoted above, many other messages came out reacting and condemning Mr. Sam Rainsy's remarks.
Please note that this Funan-Techo canal project is not only supported by the Cambodian people, but also by Laos, a country in the upper reaches of the Mekong River.
During his visit to Cambodia on April 23, Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit announced his full support for the canal project.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has stated that the Funan-Techo canal is a purely socio-economic benefit that helps Cambodia in the southwest to have waterways to the sea in addition to the existing Mekong River transport routes.
