Siem Reap Provincial Administration Holds Dissemination and Training Course on the Process of Organizing a Forum between the Royal Government and Sub-National Administration
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Administration on April 25, 2024 held an outreach and training session on the process of organizing a forum between the Royal Government and the sub-national administration under the theme (Decentralization and Decentralization Reform to participate in achieving the vision). Cambodia 2050) to the administration of 12 districts and 250 commune chiefs, commune chiefs, 100 commune clerks at the Siem Reap Provincial Hall.
Mr. Nak Neron, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, said that after the Royal Government of Cambodia for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly was recently formed, Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia, recommended the organization of an inter-royal forum. Government and sub-national administration on decentralization and deconcentration reforms for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly.
Pursuant to the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development Guidelines on the organization of this forum, Commune / Sangkat administrations are required to convene an extraordinary meeting to review, discuss and resolve the proposal. Blessings in addressing the challenges that are emerging in its jurisdiction on 8 topics (Technical Working Group will present shortly).
The main purpose of organizing this forum between the Royal Government and the sub-national administration is to review the progress of the process of implementing decentralization and deconcentration reforms in order to clearly assess the challenges related to this reform, as well as Identify specific measures for addressing challenges at each administrative level, both at the national and sub-national levels, as well as at the Royal Government level as a whole.
