(Phnom Penh): A group of gangsters who caused violence and were the subject of robbery, nicknamed "Chet Tan JT", acted on April 22, 2024, at the point of concrete road, Prey Tea 1 village, Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Sen Chey. Three injured people were suppressed by Phnom Penh police.
Police confirmed that a group of 40 suspects attacked the victim, injuring and damaging a motorcycle, as well as robbing a wallet and a mobile phone. The victims were Chhorn Bunthoeun, 23, Nuon Lin, 21, and Seang Sat, 16.
According to the confession to the authorities, the gangster nicknamed "Chet Tan (JT)" lived around the DP football table in Prey Pring Khang Cheung village, Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh. Daun Penh district, Phnom Penh, came to take revenge on the gang named "Grand Chhouk Slouy Market" who live around Prey Tea market, Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Sen Chey, who had quarreled with a group of suspects in the past.
At the time of the incident, the suspects were riding a motorbike to the scene and saw the three victims, Chhorn Bunthoeun, Nuon Lin and Seang Sat, riding a gold Honda C125. In 2019, the suspects thought that they were a gang of gangsters named "Grand Chhouk Slouy Market" who had been arguing with a group of suspects in the past, so they got on a motorbike and chased the victim's motorbike.
