On Wednesday, the Ukrainian government announced a temporary ban on men of all ages applying for or applying for passports abroad to address a reduction in the number of troops on the battlefield against the Russian army. According to the announcement, men between the ages of 18 and 59 living abroad will not be able to renew their expired passports or obtain new ones.
As of January 2024, about 4.3 million Ukrainians were living in the European Union, of which about 860,000 were adult males, according to Eurostat. So far, Poland has provided temporary protection to 950,000 Ukrainians, the second largest after Germany.
Phnom Kulen is officially named "Preah Jayavarman-Norodom National Park, Phnom Kulen". Most tourists who visit Siem Reap rarely miss this tourist resort. In addition, Phnom Kulen, originally known as Mahindrapot, is a place of worship rich in culture, history and the former capital of the Angkorian Empire, representing peace and national unity after the Khmer Empire was overthrown. Javanese.
Until now, the former capital of this glorious Khmer empire is known as a tourist destination with great potential for natural resources, especially the ancient temples, waterfalls, as well as many other unique landscapes.
Among the tourist sites on Phnom Kulen, "Srah Damrey" is a tourist site located in Khnong Phnom commune, Svay Leu district, Siem Reap province. A bridge a little further to the Bat Cave, then a motorbike lane to the left, about 300 meters to the "Elephant Pond".
Regarding the image of the frog king, we are reminded of a legend: "Once upon a time, there was a drought all over the kingdom, except for a forest with a green pond. Only then did the king send them to spy and see that there was a frog bigger than all the animals lying on the ground. He and his army plan to capture the giant frog to bring rain and coolness to the kingdom.
Please be informed that according to the speech of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the 19th Royal Government and Private Sector Forum on November 13, 2023, this work reflects the "Pentagon Strategy", Phase 1, Angle 2, Point The fourth and fifth are "Ensuring sustainable social, economic development and building resilience to climate change" by declaring "Phnom Kulen" National Park in Siem Reap as a nature tourism destination.
At the same time, Dr. Eang Sophalleth urged the Ministry of Environment to organize a study program to understand the basic information for the strategic plan for the development of green corridors in the Jayavarman-Norodom "Phnom Kulen" National Park to improve community life. Basis for the conservation of biodiversity and traditional culture for the benefit of all generations of Cambodians.
Pursuant to the "Pentagon Strategy" Phase 1 and based on the "Environmental Chakra Strategy" 2023-2028 and direct guidance from Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, introduced the designation of Preah Jayavarman-Norodom National Park Kulen ”is a nature tourism destination.
Targeting of green recreation refers to the potential of eco-tourism in existing protected areas, which has been studied by maintaining three principles: cleanliness, greenness and sustainability to ensure natural resource management, biodiversity conservation and sustainable development. Promote sustainable community life, maintain and maximize forest cover and achieve carbon neutrality by 2050.
In Preah Jayavarman-Norodom National Park, "Phnom Kulen" has a total of 85 waterfalls, ancient temples and natural attractions, as well as a total of 1,246 families, 5 people in total. 036 people, including 2,446 women in Khnong Phnom commune, Svay Leu district, Siem Reap province.
At the same time, in "Preah Jayavarman-Norodom Phnom Kulen National Park", the Ministry of Environment organized a total of 5 community protected areas, including: 1 community of Prey Thom Anlong Thom protected area, second: community of Prey Thom protected area, time 3 "Phnom Phnom Ktouch Protected Area Community 4: Prey Phnom Mnas Protected Area Community and 5: Chub Ta Sok Community Protected Area Community".
