The ban was announced by the Ukrainian Foreign Ministry on Wednesday, April 24, just days after Foreign Minister Dmytro Kuleba suspended the provision of consular services for men between the ages of 18 and 60. May 18, 2024 and also criticized some Ukrainian men abroad who have not served in the army in the war against Russia for more than 26 months.
According to the Ukrainian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the consular service will resume as usual on May 18. The ban is in line with a new law on the recruitment of additional Ukrainian troops aimed at increasing the number of troops and punishing those fleeing the recruitment. Hundreds of thousands of Ukrainian men of all ages are living abroad, including more than 860,000 living in EU member states.
