Cambodian, Chinese experts discuss climate change, waste management and recycling
(Phnom Penh): Experts from the Royal Academy of Cambodia and experts from the Guangxi Academy of Sciences of China have met to discuss issues related to global warming and how to manage waste to ensure environmental balance in the country. Society.
This discussion was held at the seminar on technological cooperation of building the ecological civilization of Cambodia-Guangxi at the Royal Academy of Cambodia on the afternoon of April 24, 2024, chaired by Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Prof. Yean Chang'an, president of the Guangxi Academy of Sciences, as well as experts from Cambodian and Chinese ministries and institutions.
The workshop comes as the world faces global climate change, which has had a devastating effect on humanity, animals and plants on Earth.
On that occasion, Dr. Sok Touch said that climate change, global warming, other natural disasters are the response of nature, this requires the joint efforts of all stakeholders and put Appropriate scientific and strategic policy solutions to ensure the balance of the environment and natural resources aimed at maintaining green growth.
According to Professor Yuan Chanan, President of the Guangxi Academy of Sciences of China, as a joint natural research institute supporting science, the Guangxi Academy of Sciences has researched the marine environment, the use of natural resources, plants, cooperation in defense technology. Environment Ecology Modern information science with a team of more than 800 experts in various fields, especially related to the environment.
He said that the crisis of global climate change, green development is a model of new development to achieve economic growth and environmental protection, carbon trade and carbon neutrality are very important in promoting economic development, better resource allocation. Re-protecting the environment and raising environmental awareness are important ways to achieve low-carbon green development.
In particular, Mr. Yang Pin, CEO of Jinshan Hi-Tech Group Co., Ltd., said that his company has found a mechanism to deal with daily waste that does not bury, do not burn or pollute and can use it completely successfully, especially the technology that the company The new design can separate plastic waste from other waste and can be recycled into fuel, gas, powder, coal for reuse, which can completely solve the problem of waste pollution.
He strongly believes that the introduction of this new technology will help solve the problem of waste to contribute to making the environment of Cambodia more attractive to tourists than ever before.
