(Phnom Penh): The body of Mr. Sambo Manara, a famous professor of Khmer history, was cremated on the evening of April 24, 2024 at Wat Toul Tompong. With deep respect for the virtues of the life of Mr. Sambo Manara, at the crematorium there was the final departure of hundreds of family, friends and students.
Sambo Manara, a professor of Khmer history, died on April 20 at the age of 67.
The following is a brief biography of Mr. Sambo Manara:
Mr. Sambo Manara is the first of six children, with a father named Chap Sambo, a Sangkum Reastr Niyum teacher and a mother named Suon Lang, a farmer. Born on September 24, 1957.
Mr. Sambo Manara graduated from Bak Ang class during the 1970s. Mr. Sambo Manara has been a diligent person since childhood. After taking time off from school, Sambo Manara learns to earn money to support his family and study by selling noodles at night, playing the microphone at the festival and pouring water into jars (in front of the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital or Russian Hospital) in Phnom Penh.
After the end of the Khmer Rouge regime in 1979, only five of Manara's family survived: his mother and four siblings. Although the distance from study for 3 years, 8 months and 20 days did not stop the feelings and educational process of Mr. Manara. This young man who loves education continued his studies until he became a professor of history at the Royal University of Phnom Penh in 1983.
Through this historical expertise, Mr. Sambo Manara continued his studies in a total of 16 countries, including the United States, Japan, South Korea, France and some other ASEAN countries. He graduated locally and received a master's degree from Yale University in the United States during the 1990s.
* Sow education and cultivate the mindset of young people to love the motherland!
All of Manara's ideas always embed the mindset of young people to love and preserve the national culture. Through his ideas, the public who had listened to his advice and understanding immediately understood that he was really worried about the loss of national culture and traditions.
Due to this will, the professor was honored by the King as a personal adviser to Samdech Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister, in February 2023.
He was also appointed by the King as a personal adviser to Samdech Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the 7th legislature, in August 2023. He has also received numerous letters of commendation, medals and medals from national and international institutions for his dedication to national and intellectual development in Cambodian society.
Professor Sambo Manara married Ms. Oum Pharan in 1979 and had three children, two boys and a girl. Including Mr. Ra Chhay Ran, Mr. Ra Socheat and Mrs. Ra Chansokany.
Excerpted from a brief biography and analysis of Mr. Sambo Manara, Professor of Khmer History.
