Samdech Hun Sen: Cambodia is closer to eradicating all forms of malaria by 2025
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, stated that in the context of peace, political stability, freedom, unity, dignity and progress throughout the country, Cambodia is moving closer to eradicating all forms of malaria by the year. 2025.
This was confirmed by a message on the occasion of the National Malaria Day under the theme "Promoting Equity, Health, Gender Equality and Human Rights to Fight Malaria" by President Hun Manet, Fresh News Received on April 24, 2024.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that in the context of peace, political stability, freedom, unity, dignity and progress throughout the country, Cambodia has moved closer to eradicating all forms of malaria by 2025 through the following significant achievements:
Prevention of malaria resistance since 2016 * Continued decline in the number of malaria cases to 2038 cases by 2023 and no deaths from malaria since 2018 to the present.
"With these progresses and achievements, we must not forget that we have not yet achieved the goal of a complete malaria eradication plan, with major challenges that we must work together," said Hun Sen. Let's solve and speed up the implementation of the action plan to eradicate malaria, the second phase, 2021-2025.
He added that the focus should be on providing diagnostic and treatment services for the remaining malaria cases in remote, inaccessible areas and the mobile population, the poor, pregnant women, children and Indigenous peoples at high risk regardless of color, sex, race, religion, socio-economic status or other status with quality, efficiency, equity and environment.
In addition, Samdech Hun Sen also called for the continuation of activities to raise public awareness, change attitudes and habits by making the community hygienic, clean environment, prevent mosquito bites, which is not only a disease prevention measure. Effective, but also the right of every citizen to be granted.
