Cambodia calls for global cooperation in science, technology and innovation at OECD Ministerial Conference
(Paris): Mr. Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation of Cambodia, reaffirmed Cambodia's commitment to promoting international cooperation in the fields of science, technology and innovation.
Hem Vandy made the remarks at the opening ceremony of the Ministerial Conference of the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD) held in Paris on April 23-24, 2024, which brought together world leaders. He came together to address common challenges and promote scientific, technological and innovative activities.
In his address to the conference, Minister Hem Vandy stressed the importance of Cambodia to regional integration, especially through regional institutions such as ASEAN to promote economic growth and increase trade relations. He also highlighted Cambodia's various initiatives to attract foreign direct investment in high value-added sectors, such as improving the business environment and necessary infrastructure.
One of the core strategies of Cambodia's science, technology and innovation sector is the 2030 Science, Technology and Innovation Roadmap, which prioritizes governance, education, research, cooperation and ecosystem development.
Mr. Hem Vandy emphasized to the conference on the importance of human capital development and technological integration into enterprises, especially in the private sector, so that they can increase productivity and better contribute to economic diversification.
At the same time, Cambodia has demonstrated its commitment to promoting an equitable and sustainable environment in the development of science, technology and innovation, in line with the objectives of the Committee for Science and Technology Policy 2024 (CSTP 2024).
He stressed the need for intergovernmental and cross-sectoral cooperation to promote sustainable change and ensure social benefits from technological advances. He also called for joint efforts to work together to create a roadmap for science, technology and innovation, using common strength to build a more sustainable future.
