Vietnam overtakes India, Thailand to become Singapore's largest rice supplier
Vietnamese rice has become popular in Singapore due to its abundance and ease of purchase. In addition to high-quality white rice, Vietnam also has an 80% share of the parboiled rice market and 73.3% of Singapore's fragrant rice market.
Thailand, India and Japan are Vietnam's biggest rivals. In order to maintain Vietnam's position as Singapore's top rice supplier, Vietnamese companies need to increase promotion and marketing and maintain the quality of their products consistently, according to the Vietnam Trade Office in Singapore.
The signing of a memorandum of understanding with Singapore to increase rice exports to Singapore will also be an effective strategy.
Chief of Staff of the General Command sends condolences to Ms. Lim Thavy and her family on the death of Lt. Gen. Seng Samnang
