(Phnom Penh): Khmer civilization expert Rath Sandab on April 24, 2024 expressed his appreciation for the performance of Khmer bokator and Sao Linh as part of Chinese kung fu and proposed Next time, set a weekend or holiday for visitors to visit.
The expert statement was made after seeing the success of the joint performance of Shaolin and Bokator in order to promote the joint tourism destinations of Henan and Siem Reap, as well as to celebrate the implementation of the "Visit Siem Reap" campaign. "2024" and "Year of People and People Change - Cambodia-China 2024". But there are other public opinion, sad because they did not visit in person on weekdays like this.
Mr. Rath Sandab said that if such events continue to be held on holidays or public occasions, many people will visit and learn about the national martial arts of the two countries.
Khmer civilization experts stated, "We see a lot of young people interested in this program, so I would like to encourage a wide range of martial arts performances." "We can find time for Saturday or Sunday or organize for major national events."
Bokator was inscribed on the UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list on November 29, 2022. Bokator is a traditional Khmer martial art that has been deeply rooted in Cambodian society for centuries and continues to survive in Cambodian society to this day. The carvings on the walls of Angkorian temples are clear evidence of this martial art practice.
Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that both martial arts are inscribed in their respective cultures and civilizations. The social science expert said that kung fu martial arts is an ancient Chinese martial art, while bokator is an ancient Cambodian martial art, and performing together like this is really good, making both countries familiar with martial arts. Mutual nation.
Dr. Yong Pov stated, "So, we hope that there will be more performances, not just once, but many times, I request to connect the hearts of the two nations as a way to cultivate the emotions between the people and the people." People through martial arts.
Un Jim, a political science and culture scholar, said he was happy that Cambodia and China had the idea to introduce martial arts between the two countries, a symbol and symbol of national martial arts to the world. Know. He said that if we do it ourselves, it is not easy to explode and bring attention, but if we join hands to do this kind of promotion, the world will soon know and recognize the ancestral martial arts, which is the national identity.
Mr. Un Jim stated, "I am very happy and would like to support the organization of our ancestral martial arts show for the world to know. In the past, only Taekwondo, Kung Fu, Karate and Muay Thai were known." "So now we have to show the world what we have."
Please be informed that Khmer civilization experts also requested all stakeholders, whether the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Cambodian Bokator Federation and bokator teachers to jointly develop this martial art to be trained in the field of education. According to Mr. Rath, listening to bokator is a national martial art that we must promote, especially in the public and private schools.
(Mondulkiri): Recently, herds of wild elephants or Asian elephants have appeared in protected areas in Mondulkiri province, which is more than seen in previous years. Recently, a herd of about 20 Asian wild elephants was found in O'Am village, Sre Khtom commune, Keo Seima district, Mondulkiri province, which is a sign that wild elephants live in peace and give birth to a series of offspring.
Park rangers have observed the presence of wild elephants roaming the forest, and sometimes entering the protected area community in groups of between 20 and 30, an increase of three to five. Itself in the past.
According to Mr. Sos Milem, Deputy Governor of Keo Seima District, the Keo Seima District Administration is taking steps to instruct village chiefs and commune chiefs to issue notices to local people to be very careful and to avoid entering the forest in search of vegetables near the Elephant area. Pain at the O'Pam point, prevent any possible accidents. In addition, he also asked the relevant officials to monitor the health and disease of elephants.
He said that according to the DNA analysis on the number of wild elephants by the Ministry of Environment officials and partners in the past, there are about 350 Asian elephants in the eastern highlands in Mondulkiri province.
