(Phnom Penh): The President of Laos, Mr. Thongloun Sisoulith, has firmly stated that despite the problems in the region and the world, Laos still maintains good relations with Cambodia.
During a meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet during his state visit to Cambodia on the afternoon of April 23, Mr. Thongloun Sisoulith affirmed that he will strive to address all regional and global challenges in order to Continuing the close and lasting friendship and solidarity, as well as further promoting the level of bilateral relations that will bring mutual benefits to both peoples and countries.
In addition to declaring efforts to maintain good relations between Cambodia and Laos, the President of Laos also thanked Cambodia for supporting Laos as the rotating chair of ASEAN in 2024. Laos will strive to learn from the success of Cambodia, which chaired ASEAN in 2022.
The President of Laos also announced that he would always welcome the presence of the President when attending the ASEAN Summit in October 2024.
Cambodia and Laos established official diplomatic relations on June 15, 1956. Cambodia-Laos relations were promoted as a comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership during the official visit of Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit as the Prime Minister of Laos in Cambodia on September 12-13, 2019.
Relations between Cambodia and Laos, which are bordering countries, have been continuously enhanced and have always maintained a spirit of helping each other in times of adversity.
