"In the spirit of national unity, I would like to accept your apology," he said. "I will ask my lawyer to withdraw the complaint from the court to end this case as soon as possible."
Along with announcing favor to Mr. Chea Poch, Samdech Techo also announced that he would accept any apology from other people who had been wronged and declared independence from three generations of traitors.
It should be noted that from Australia, on April 23, 2024, Mr. Chea Poch wrote a letter of apology to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party again and announced his separation from Sam Rainsy and the opposition party.
In a letter to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Mr. Chea Poch stated: "I, Chea Poch, former Member of Parliament for Prey Veng and Kampot, really regret that I acted and used some words in the past. To affect the process of development, peace, stability and policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially to affect Samdech Techo. I apologize to the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia, especially to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen.
Mr. Chea Poch continued: "In this sense, I would like to inform Samdech Techo that I have decided to secede from Mr. Sam Rainsy and stop political activities with the former CNRP and the Candlelight Party. "And parties that have a tendency to oppose because of a lack of faith in foreign policy, slander, insults, slander, divisions that can not lead to unity and reconciliation."
He respectfully asked for Samdech Techo Metta's forgiveness and asked the court to drop the charges against him for his past wrongdoing and to give him the opportunity to be a good citizen living under the roof of peace. The leadership of Samdech Techo as well.
Please note that in the past, there was a leak of Mr. Chea Poch's voice, which showed his uncle's determination to overthrow Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
In connection with this case, in May 2023, Mr. Chea Poch had already sent a letter to apologize to Samdech Techo, but the prince refused to accept.
Secretary-General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, disseminating and training on rapid drug testing for professional officers in ministries and institutions
(Phnom Penh): On April 23, 2024, General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, presided over the Closing Ceremony of Dissemination and Training on Understanding Test Methods. Urgently find drugs in the urine to professional officers of ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations.
The event was attended by more than 200 participants from the Armed Forces and civil servants from all ministries, institutions and the Capital and Provincial Drug Control Committees.
The General Secretary instructed the trainees who have gained knowledge on how to quickly test for drugs in the urine, please apply and share with colleagues in their units with a professional spirit. Correct and transparent.
