Hamas: Palestinian death toll in Gaza rises to 34,183
Gaza: The death toll from a Palestinian death in the Gaza Strip as a result of the ongoing Israeli attacks has risen to 34,183, the Hamas Ministry of Health announced on Tuesday. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on April 23, 2024.
In the past 24 hours, Israeli forces have killed 32 Palestinians and wounded 59 others, bringing the total to 34,183 and wounding seven, the ministry said in a statement. 7,143 since the outbreak of conflict between Israel and Hamas in October. Day 7, 2023.
Meanwhile, Israeli army spokesman Avichay Adraee said the army had launched several airstrikes overnight, destroying two Hamas positions in the southern Gaza Strip. He added that the sites were targeted before rockets were fired from them into Israeli territory.
