What weapons does Ukraine expect from the United States to rectify the war situation?
A Russian airstrike has cut off a television tower in Kharkiv province in two as Ukraine awaits US air defense assistance. Ukraine has urged the United States to ratify the final agreement so that Ukraine can gradually receive aid from the US administration. What advanced weapons does Ukraine expect to receive to rectify its combat situation on the battlefield?
A Russian airstrike has cut off the Kharkiv TV tower in two as Ukraine awaits US air defense assistance. Ukraine has urged the United States to ratify the final agreement so that Ukraine can gradually receive aid from the US administration.
A White House statement confirmed to Zelensky that the Joe Biden administration would provide a new military security package to meet Ukraine's urgent needs on the battlefield, after which the Senate would approve an additional national security package. That is, the US President will have to sign the final ratification as soon as the military aid will be transported to Ukraine.
The need for an air defense system is one that the Zelinsky government has repeatedly called on the West to seek military assistance to counter Russian air strikes, especially the protection of power infrastructure. Russia's air strikes have left many civilians without power in cold weather.
An earlier tactic was to override the air defense system by launching a large number of missiles at targets, which would control the radar, monitor the attack and damage the missile stockpile system. More.
2024 is also the year that Ukraine is expected to have F-16 fighter jets for its air defense use. Ukraine's allies hope that the war in Ukraine will help improve Ukraine's position by giving Russia an advantage over the supply of F-16 fighter jets to the Kiev government.
Putin warned at the same time that Russia had no intention of attacking NATO members. But he said that if the West supplied F-16 fighter jets to Ukraine to attack Russia, those F-16s would be shot down by Russian forces, no matter where they were.
