(VOVworld) - Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), attended the opening ceremony of the ASEAN Future Forum hosted by Vietnam on the morning of April 23, 2024. Of a people-centered ASEAN community ”in Hanoi, Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
In his remarks, the ASEAN Secretary-General highlighted the role of the ASEAN Future Forum, a forum for ASEAN and its partners to share new ideas and policy recommendations. He stressed the appropriate timing of the forum to consider the future, especially as ASEAN is shaping the ASEAN Community Vision 2045 and strategic planning of this vision.
In the morning of the same day, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn paid a courtesy call on Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam. During the meeting, the two sides discussed key issues on the ASEAN agenda, including the formulation of the ASEAN Community Vision 2045 and the four strategic plans, the progress of East Timor's process towards full membership in ASEAN. ASEAN, providing humanitarian assistance to Myanmar.
In the afternoon of the same day, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, met with Mr. Bui Thanh Son, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam. On that occasion, the two sides discussed ways to accelerate efforts to build the ASEAN Community to strengthen the ASEAN Center and ASEAN Solidarity at a time when regional architecture is evolving. The two sides also discussed maritime cooperation as well as other important regional and international issues.
In addition, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn allowed Dr. Dino Patti Djalal, President of the Indonesian Foreign Policy Community to meet on the occasion of the ASEAN Future Forum. On that occasion, the two sides exchanged views on developments in the region as well as finding ways to enhance the ASEAN vision on the Indo-Pacific region. Spokesman for the General Commission: Another 291 vehicles were inspected and fined on April 23, 2024
According to the spokesperson, for March 23, 2024, the traffic police nationwide inspected and fined a total of 5,060 vehicles, including 3,757 motorcycles and 1,303 vehicles.
Notable offenses for motorcycles include: drunken helmets, drug addicts, firearms / badges, etc. The vehicles include: drunken driving, heavy goods, speeding, drunken driving without a license and lights.
It should be noted that for April 23, 2024, there were 8 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 2 people were killed and 22 people were injured (13 people were seriously injured). In 23 days, there were 214 traffic accidents, resulting in 121 deaths, 304 injuries (190 serious injuries).
