Authorities crack down on flooded forest clearing in Chit Borey district, Kratie province
(Kratie): Coalition forces cracked down on and confiscated a machine (Escar Motor) that was clearing flooded forest land at Mreum village, Dar commune, Chit Borei district, Kratie province on the afternoon of April 23, 2024.
The above operation was carried out by the Fisheries Administration District Officer of Kratie Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in collaboration with the Police Force, Economic Crimes Office of Kratie Provincial Police and local fishing communities.
Mr. Mok Ponlok, Director of the Provincial Fisheries Administration, said that the criminals used an excavator to clear the flooded forest to take ownership of about 10 hectares of state land, but when the police arrived. Only one hectare of the above clearing equipment was confiscated, stored and the case was sent to the Kratie Provincial Court to continue to take legal action on fisheries.
In this operation, the police have not arrested the owner of the machine yet, because when the police arrived, they escaped, leaving the machine at the above location. Experts claim that they will continue to research and identify targets to build a case to proceed with the procedure. HE Yim Chhay Ly and Lok Chumteav Ton Khon donated $ 5,000 on the occasion of the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2024
