Ministry of Cult issues guidelines on Vesak
The Vaisakhi festival is one of the most important festivals celebrated by Buddhists and Buddhists around the world, as well as Cambodia, every year to commemorate the three epochs, the day the Buddha was born. Enlightenment and Nirvana on the 15th day of the full moon in the same month of Pisak.
Meanwhile, Vesak was recognized by the United Nations on December 15, 1999 and is held annually at the United Nations.
This year, the Royal Government of Vesak Festival is officially held on Wednesday, the 15th day of the month of Pisak, the year of Rong Chhasak, BE 2567, and on Thursday, the 1st day of the month of Pisak, the year of Pisak, the year of Rong Chhasak, BE 2561, corresponding to May 22-23. In 2024, in the compound of Preah Moha Sak Moni Chet, Phnom Preah Reach Top (Udong), with the participation of national leaders, government officials at all levels, monks and Buddhists in large numbers.
In particular, in pagodas across the country organized this festival simultaneously in accordance with the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which states that Buddhism is the state religion.
