Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Wang Wenbin said: "The United States has presented a draft law on large-scale military aid to Ukraine while making baseless allegations about normal trade between China and Russia. "Such an approach is hypocritical and irresponsible, and China is firmly opposed to this."
"On the Ukraine issue, China has always maintained the right position, advocated for peace talks and pushed for a political solution," Wang added. China strictly adheres to regulations on the export of military and civilian equipment. "China is not the creator or party to the Ukraine crisis and has never set fire to it, so we will not accept any blame."
China and Russia have stepped up economic cooperation and political ties in recent years, and the strategic partnership has been closer since Russia's war in Ukraine. US officials say China has not provided direct military assistance to Russia, but has provided equipment that could serve both the military and civilian areas.
