Cambodia-China Friendship Radio The Cambodian and Chinese governments have agreed to deepen the Belt and Road Initiative and the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Cambodian and Chinese governments have agreed to streamline the Belt and Road Initiative. And the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy and Strategy to deepen to build a deep and practical Cambodia-China common destiny community.
The agreement was reached during a three-day visit to Cambodia by Wang Yi, Member of the Political Bureau, Chairman of the Foreign Affairs Committee of the CPC Central Committee and Foreign Minister of the People's Republic of China. April 21-23, 2024.
The Belt and Road Initiative is a strategy developed by President Xi Jinping in 2013 that has two main components: the Silk Road Economic Belt along the Silk Road and the 21st Century Maritime Silk Road, which aims to connect China through some Asian countries to Europe.
The first phase of the Pentagon Strategy was launched by the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, under the leadership of Samdech Hun Manet, prioritizing "people, roads, water, electricity and technology" in order to push Cambodia to achieve its goals. Developed countries by 2050.
Minister of Public Works Chairs the First Meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Technical Working Group to Promote Railway Development in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Peng Po Na, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this morning, April 23, 2024, chaired the first meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Technical Working Group to promote the development of railways in Cambodia with the participation of You are the leader and representative of the relevant ministries and institutions of the Royal Government.
The purpose of this meeting was to review the Cambodia-China railway cooperation mechanism and set the direction for further work, focusing on capacity building, master planning, railway project study and project implementation mechanism.
The Funan-Techo canal project has become one of the topics discussed during a meeting between Senate President Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Lao President Thongloun Sisoulith on Tuesday morning. This April 2024 at the Senate.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen's social media, during this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit to support the Funan-Techo canal project because it does not affect the environment or the flow of the Mekong River.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that this canal project plays a very important role for connecting the river to the Cambodian sea.
After listening to the explanation of the technical characteristics and the request for support from Samdech Techo, the President of Laos announced his support for the Funan-Techo canal project without any hesitation.
Laos' support is an important part, as Laos is a member of the Mekong River Commission, if any decision is required from the countries along the Mekong.
However, the project is being reacted to by Vietnam and requires further explanation from the Cambodian side. At the same time, some Vietnamese analysts have tried to accuse the canal of serving the Chinese military.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen came out and denied all these allegations. Samdech Techo stated that the Funan-Techo canal is a pure socio-economic benefit that helps Cambodia in the southwest to have waterways to the sea in addition to the existing Mekong River transport routes.
Samdech Techo also stated that this canal does not affect the flow of the Mekong River, because this canal does not connect from the Mekong River, but from the Bassac River, and on the other hand, there is a sluice gate to prevent fresh water from falling. Not into the sea. General Sao Sokha Announces Change of Position and Rank of New Commander of Kampong Cham Provincial Gendarmerie
(Kampong Cham): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, on April 23, 2024, conferred the title of Mr. Theng Chheng Lim and announced his inauguration. Kampong Cham Provincial Gendarmerie Command replaces General So Savoeun, who has been transferred to Ratanakkiri Provincial Gendarmerie Command.
The ceremony was held at the Kampong Cham Provincial Gendarmerie Headquarters with the participation of Mr. Khlot Phorn, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham, as well as leaders of various relevant departments.
On that occasion, the Governor of Kampong Cham expressed his appreciation to the officers, deputies and soldiers of the Provincial Gendarmerie Command who have played an important role in maintaining security and public order, strictly respecting the guiding principles of the Gendarmerie Command. The country adheres to the principles of laws, regulations, professional ethics.
The officers, deputies and gendarmes of the Provincial Gendarmerie Command performed their duties with honesty, dedication and high will to perform their duties with pride. The Provincial Governor commended Brigadier General So Savoeun, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, for fulfilling his role in directing the Provincial Gendarmerie in his previous term.
He said this on the occasion of his courtesy call and discussion with Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia this morning, April 23, 2024, at the Senate Palace during his visit. Official state road in Cambodia for two days from 23 to 24 April 2024.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen warmly welcomed the visit of Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit, President of the Lao People's Democratic Republic. Samdech Techo considered that Mr. Thongloun's current visit to Cambodia will further strengthen the relationship between the country and the people of the two countries, which are good neighbors, and tomorrow, the two parties, the People's Party. Cambodians and the Lao Revolutionary Party will also meet.
In response, the President of Laos expressed his pleasure to visit Cambodia now and also met Samdech Techo, an old friend and teacher, and Samdech Techo has a lot of experience in leading Cambodia to develop. Progressively, as Samdech Techo is the President of the Party, even though Samdech is the President of the Senate, Samdech can still control and lead the good conduct of Cambodia as well as other institutions.
Once again, the President of Laos, as well as the National Assembly and the people of Laos, congratulated the CPP and warmly congratulated Samdech Techo on his election as President of the Senate. The President also described that he had previously met with His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia in a very warm and pleasant atmosphere.
The President of Laos also thanked Samdech Techo, President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia, who has always supported Laos, and the President noted the progress of Cambodia and was pleased to continue to visit Cambodia. Also participated in the last SEA Games, which Cambodia successfully held and now visited Cambodia with a warm welcome.
The President of Laos recalled that Samdech Techo shared many good lessons in maintaining political stability and praised the transfer of positions from the old generation to the new generation and the assignment of positions to civil servants. The visit of the Royal Government as well as other institutions was smooth and also confirmed that he was glad to meet Samdech Techo now and also observed that Cambodia is politically stable and is making good progress.
Finally, Samdech Techo asked the President of Laos to support the Funan Canal project of Cambodia because this canal is not harmful to the environment or the flow of water, but this canal is a connection between Tonle Bassac to the Cambodian Sea, and the President of Laos has supported this project as well. TikTok Says US Laws That Can Ban Its Social Media Will Step on Freedom of Expression
Reuters reported that the US House of Representatives passed the bill on Saturday by a vote of 360 to 58. The law is now in the hands of the upper house, where it could be voted on in the coming days. US President Joe Biden has said he will sign the TikTok Act.
Many U.S. lawmakers from Republicans and Democrats and Bidy's government say TikTok poses a national security risk because China could force the company to share data with 170 million users in the United States.
According to Reuters, measures that integrate the TikTok ban law as part of the U.S. Comprehensive Foreign Aid package for foreign states could quickly track deadlines for any possible ban following the law. Another ban previously stuck in the U.S. Senate.
"It is unfortunate that the House of Representatives is using significant foreign and humanitarian aid excuses to pass a new ban that would trample on the right to freedom of expression," Reuters reported, quoting a press release issued by TikTok. "The free speech of 170 million Americans."
The American Civil Liberties Union has opposed a bill passed by Congress, citing freedom of expression. TikTok insists it has never shared US citizen data and will not do so. Oddar Meanchey Provincial Referral Hospital receives an ambulance from Sar Kheng
