National Authority for Combating Drugs and Ministry of Cult Disseminate Drug Issues to Interfaith in Battambang Province
On behalf of Mr. Sok Lou, Provincial Governor and Chairman of Battambang Provincial Drug Control Committee, Mr. Ou Dary, Deputy Governor of Battambang Provincial Drug Control Committee Secretariat, expressed his gratitude and appreciation and asked Imam, pastor, priest and church to work hard to capture Knowledge of the drug problem to be disseminated to the family in the home and community to reduce and eliminate drug problems from home and community.
Speaking on behalf of Mr. Chay Borin, Minister of Cult and Religion, Mr. Chhit Sokunthy, Secretary of State, thanked and appreciated all parties who took the time to attend the workshop to gain knowledge and experience to Prevent yourself from the effects of drugs and share with other believers to prevent and avoid drugs.
On the other hand, based on past experience in the fight against drugs, Dr. Neth Savoeun considered that clear understanding and active participation of the masses is indispensable and determines the effectiveness of the fight against drugs. That's why he has come up with innovative initiatives and measures, including a mobile app that is officially launching on this occasion.
Mr. Thong Sokunthea, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, presented the APP NoDrug mobile application of the National Authority for Combating Drugs. Nationwide, public and private modifications. Citizens can report all drug cases to the authorities secretly and promptly.
In addition, so that they can understand and be able to cooperate with local authorities and law enforcement to prevent, suppress and solve all problems related to drugs. He also called on all stakeholders to use the NoDrug APP together and help spread the word to all family members and friends to use it.
At the same time, they can also participate in making suggestions, requesting information or reporting to the authorities related to drug crimes in order to get a response or intervention based on the problems they have encountered, including the response to those who have Children or relatives of drug addicts can also search for information and request intervention through the mobile app. Why Chinese people always say, "Study hard to grow every day"
From time immemorial, Chinese society has had an atmosphere of respect for intellectuals and knowledge, which is the ancient Chinese morality, recognizing that "not reading a book one day can not do everything." There is a consensus: any task done well and successful will benefit from learning.
In fact, the phrase "strive to learn to grow every day" is a recommendation for Chinese children by Mao Zedong, mentioned as the new China begins to build. He used words that were easy to understand to show the understanding of the Chinese people's learning, so it has become a popular Chinese phrase to this day.
The Chinese Communist Party has continued the good tradition of this nation, whether during the war, the struggle with the enemy, or now, in the era of peace, each party leader and party member attaches great importance to learning. . For example, China's reform and opening-up, which "transcends, touches, touches," is a cause for learning from the Chinese Communist Party's global experience.
In 2024, the CPC Central Committee will hold two collective study meetings on specific topics to promote high-quality development, new energy technology development and national energy security. Under the chairmanship of Xi Jinping, Secretary-General of the CPC Central Committee, experts in the field were invited to give training.
It should be noted that the collective study mechanism of the ruling party of the ruling party of China since 2002, which is held every 45 days, members of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee jointly study and discuss the key issues of China's national development and knowledge. Various skills related to national development in order to further enhance the capacity and level of national governance.
Building a modern country requires a long-term strategy in education, technology and human resources. Entering a new era, the Chinese Communist Party continues to study books through practice, learning from the people and experts, as well as learning useful experiences from abroad. As Chinese top leader Xi Jinping has repeatedly stated, "We have reached the present by relying on education, we need to continue to move towards the future based on study."
