Ministry of Water Resources announces weather forecast for May-June and calls for water saving
After monitoring, analyzing and forecasting the weather situation of the Ministry as well as from international institutions, especially the World Meteorological Organization (WMO), the Ministry of Water Resources would like to inform the public about the weather situation in At the beginning of the rainy season from May 1 to June 30, 2024 as follows:
2: Weather forecast in Cambodia Such a situation will cause low temperature in the lowlands, highlands and coastal areas of Cambodia with a minimum temperature of 26 degrees Celsius and a maximum temperature of 36 degrees Celsius. Moderate to moderate rainfall covers 40% of the land area and rainfall is higher than the average for many years, with thunderstorms and strong winds.
According to the above-mentioned weather conditions, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology would like to inform the relevant ministries, institutions, local authorities and the public to cooperate in maintaining water use at a high level, especially in remote rural areas far from the source. Water.
The Ministry of Water Resources also warned to pay close attention to the phenomenon of thunder, lightning and strong winds. Spokesman: Thirteen coconut plantations and five licensed packaging sites are busy preparing to export coconuts to the Chinese market.
(Phnom Penh): Thirteen coconut plantations and five packaging locations that have allowed the export of fresh coconuts from Cambodia to China are busy preparing to export Cambodian fresh coconuts to the Chinese market. This was stated by Ms. Im Rachana, Undersecretary of State and spokesperson for the Ministry of Agriculture.
After receiving the application from the plantations and processing plants for fresh coconuts, the General Department of Agriculture assigned professional officers to evaluate in accordance with the technical procedures as stated in the protocol and send the list of plantations and processing plants to the parties. China for review and evaluation.
So far, the General Administration of Customs of China has officially recognized 13 coconut plantations and 5 registered packaging sites for exporting fresh coconuts from Cambodia to China.
She added that coconut plantations and packaging sites registered with the Chinese Customs Administration are busy preparing to export Cambodia's fresh coconuts to the Chinese market, with the first leg of exports expected to be completed. In the year 2024.
