A resident of Kampong Leng district asked the provincial governor to intervene after wanting to sell agricultural land with a soft title and enjoy it since 2000, but the district governor did not allow it, the district governor said it was land in area 2
(Kampong Chhnang): A villager asked Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province to intervene after wanting to sell agricultural land with a soft title and enjoy since 2000, but Mr. Yem Leakena, Governor of Kampong Chhnang District, did not allow it.
This resident, Ms. Ing Sopheap, currently resides in Andong Ranok village, Trangel commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, with a land area of Keng Ta Sok village, Kampong Hao commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, 18181 square meters. Recognized by the Office of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Land on April 9, 2024.
"My family is an honest citizen who lives and works well as a result of peace under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister, and the successor to Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet," she said. "Not allowing me to sell the land leads to my loss, especially serious economic problems."
(Kampong Speu): General Sem Sovanny, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee and Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center, on the morning of April 22, 2024, inspected the construction site at the Multinational Peacekeeping Force Training School. The busy construction site consists of three buildings: a school building, a dormitory building and a meeting hall building, which were built to receive national and international trainees in the upcoming tripartite training project.
General Sem Sovanny inspected the three buildings to ensure that the construction was technically in line with international standards. However, these buildings will play an important role in receiving national and international trainees on the tripartite training project hosted by Cambodia.
In addition to inspecting the construction of the building, the General also paid close attention to the preparation of road infrastructure, water system, land improvement and landscaping to make the school more beautiful.
It should be noted that the construction of the three buildings, including: school building, dormitory building and meeting hall building, started construction in June 2023, and so far, 71% of the school building has been completed, 75% of the dormitory building and the building 60% of the meeting hall. The three buildings are scheduled to be completed in September 2024.
Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many instructed the Royal Government's working group to visit Kampong Speu province to continue organizing public forums to improve the provision of good public services to the people and increase opportunities for local youth.
(Phnom Penh): This morning, April 23, 2024, Mr. HUN Many, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Public Function, chaired a meeting to review the first quarterly report of the Royal Government Working Group on Kampong Speu Province to understand the actual work situation. In addition to the basic work direction, including collecting challenges, proposals and suggestions to take action.
The meeting was attended by the chairperson of the National Task Force for Municipalities, Districts, the focal point of the Ministry of Public Function in charge of the work of the Royal Government of the Capital and Provinces, the Mobile Working Group of the Royal Government of Kampong Speu Provincial Working Group, the Provincial Council and the Board of Governors. Provinces, departments, units around the province and related units, about 120 people.
After listening to the report, Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many praised and appreciated the work results as well as thanked the Royal Government working group in Kampong Speu province, as well as the leaders of government officials and local authorities in Kampong Speu. Achieved many achievements in a short period of time in accordance with the guidelines and indications of the Royal Government.
He continued to encourage and recommend to all working groups to continue the core work that the team has been doing and make regular reports to the management.
He strongly believes that all working groups as the staff of the Royal Government will continue to perform their roles and responsibilities more consistently in accordance with the guidelines and orientation of the Royal Government and be creative according to the actual situation of each base.
