US troops in Iraq again attacked by drones and rockets
US forces in Iraq and Syria have been hit by two separate attacks, rockets and drones, in less than 24 hours, which could be the first attack on the force. The United States after a suspension of nearly three months. This was released by Reuters on Tuesday, April 23, 2024.
Attacks on US troops ceased in late January 2024 under pressure from Iraqi and Iranian authorities after the United States launched an attack on an Iranian-backed armed movement in retaliation for three US soldiers killed in the attack. By drone in Jordan.
The United States invaded Iraq in 2003 to overthrow former Iraqi leader Saddam Hussein and withdrew in 2011. But US troops were re-deployed to Iraq in 2014 at the request of the Iraqi government to help fight ISIS. About 2,500 US troops are currently stationed in Iraq and 900 in eastern Syria.
