Senior Minister Ly Thuch holds bilateral meeting with Deputy Foreign Minister of the Republic of Fiji to seek support for globalization of Ottawa Convention
During the meeting, Senior Minister Ly Thuch outlined Cambodia's three priority goals as chair of the 2024 Ottawa Convention, including the globalization of the Convention on Mine Action and Mine Action.
In the globalization of the Convention, Cambodia seeks to support and mobilize countries that have not yet become States Parties to the Convention, including three countries, including Tonga, Macedonia and the Pacific Islands.
At the same time, Cambodia intends to mobilize these three countries, among other countries, to turn the entire Pacific into a demilitarized zone, which requires the support of Fiji to persuade and mobilize the three countries to become States Parties to the Convention. Ottawa.
On that occasion, Dr. Ly Thuch thanked Fiji for supporting the implementation of the Ottawa Convention, a humanitarian convention to eradicate anti-personnel landmines.
On behalf of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister, Senior Minister Ly Thuch invited the leaders of the Republic of Fiji to attend the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit, which Cambodia will host in Siem Reap in November 2024.
In response, Lenora Qereqeretabua said Fiji welcomed Cambodia's proposal to demine the entire Pacific region and expressed support for Cambodia's presidency for the 2024 Ottawa Convention, which led a delegation. Cambodia attends 46th Session of the Supreme Council of the Islamic Alliance in Saudi Arabia
The purpose of this meeting is to select and renew the mandate of the Supreme Council members, which are leaders, dignitaries, representatives of more than 100 countries and Islamic communities from around the world.
