The following is the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs: Senior officials of the Ministry of Interior request all administrations at all levels to provide good cooperation with the working group of the General Department of Internal Audit in order to make the audit process run smoothly.
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Mak Sambath, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, requested all levels of administration to cooperate with the working group of the General Department of Internal Audit of the Ministry of Interior in order for the audit process to be successful. Improve and accept recommendations to improve the management of each unit to be better and more effective.
Mr. Mak Sambath, Deputy Secretary of the Ministry of Interior, made this request on the occasion of his participation in the internal audit of the Svay Rieng Provincial Administration for the period of 2023 and related years (Civil Administration, Public Security and Banking) in the afternoon. April 22, 2024.
The meeting was also attended by Mr. Sok Ros, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng, representatives of Mr. Peng Po Sa, Provincial Governor, as well as many other stakeholders.
Mr. Sok Ros said that the meeting was important for the internal audit work because it was considered as one of the important priorities and received a lot of attention, and the implementation of this work has become an obligation determined by law and Legal documents.
He added that at the same time, it is an independent task and a function of the institution that provides added value and enhances the efficiency and effectiveness of the various operations of each institution, which helps to achieve the objectives through monitoring and Evaluate institutional risk management, oversight, and governance processes.
The commitment between the Cambodian and Chinese governments was made during a three-day visit to Cambodia by Wang Yi, a member of the Politburo, chairman of the Foreign Affairs Committee of the CPC Central Committee and foreign minister. April 21-23, 2024.
A joint Cambodian-Chinese statement on the outcome of the visit said: "Both sides stressed their commitment to fully and effectively implement the Declaration on the Implementation of the Parties in the China Sea. "The South China Sea (DOC) will push for a consultation on the Code of Conduct in the South China Sea (COC) for preliminary conclusions."
In the past, Cambodia has always called on all parties to implement a peaceful solution and continue to use the ASEAN-China mechanism for the full implementation of the Declaration on the Implementation of the Parties in the South China Sea. South China Sea (DOC) and urge ASEAN and China to work more closely to achieve the South China Sea Code of Conduct (COC).
The Chinese announcement was made by Wang Yi, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, Chairman of the Bureau of Foreign Affairs and Foreign Minister of China, during his visit to Cambodia from the 21st to the 23rd. April 2024.
The two sides also agreed to modernize the coordinating role of the Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee to build a common destiny of Cambodia and China in the new era with high quality, high standards and high standards, as well as jointly promote multilateralism and globalization. Economic privatization that provides free, open, equitable and inclusive common interests.
"The Chinese side reaffirms its support for Cambodia's choice of development path in line with national conditions, and supports Cambodia's efforts to safeguard its national sovereignty, security and interests," the statement said. "Development as well as absolute opposition to external interference in Cambodia's internal affairs."
