(Phnom Penh): Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi has announced his government's position to continue to support Cambodia's development by promoting agriculture, industry and technology.
In a meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet on Monday afternoon, April 22, 2024, Wang Yi said that China and Cambodia are close and loyal friends. Wang Yi expressed his pleasure that the two governments have carried out good cooperation in a comprehensive strategic partnership and pushed China-Cambodia relations as strong as steel.
The Chinese diplomat, who frequently visits Cambodia, emphasized that Cambodia is playing an increasingly important role in the international arena, and that Hun Manet's first official visit to China in 2023 reflected and contributed to the strengthening of ties of friendship and solidarity. China-Cambodia to be more cohesive.
The Chinese diplomat stressed that his current visit to Cambodia will continue to support and promote cooperation in building a new China-Cambodia common destiny community in the new era.
President Hun Manet extended a warm welcome to Minister Wang Yi and his delegation on their visit to Cambodia. The President thanked and highly appreciated the Cambodian-Chinese cooperation, which has contributed to the promotion of socio-economic development of Cambodia.
In addition, he praised the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI), which has contributed to Cambodia's ability to build infrastructure such as the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway and the Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport. Cambodia's economic growth.
He also expressed his pleasure and appreciation for the progress of the diamond cooperation framework agreed by the two countries in 2023.
By designating 2024 as the year of people-to-people exchanges, the President is confident that the flow of investment and tourists from China will increase.
Samdech Hun Manet asked China to examine the possibility of promoting cooperation in the establishment of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Area and more special economic zones. Permanent Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth opens training course on "Political Philosophy - Administration - Law"
