Week 13 Registration Case As of April 19, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Court has handled 359 cases
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Oum Chanthol, President of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Court, stated that in the 13th week of civil registration cases as of April 19, 2024, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Court has handled 359 cases.
Speaking to Fresh News on the evening of April 22, 2024, Mr. Oum Chanthol confirmed that there were 140 pre-campaign registrations, 285 civil registrations during the campaign, and 3 cases were processed within 3 months. 359 cases and the case of Kampong Cham registrar is 66 cases.
According to the President of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Court, there were 407 cases of birth certificate correction, equivalent to 95.76%, 11 cases of marriage certificate correction, equal to 2.58%, 7 cases of death certificate correction, equal to 1.65%. He stated that the cause of the mistake that led to the request for correction was due to the fault of the registrar and by the person concerned.
Mr. Oum Chanthol further stated that the request to amend the civil status case does not require payment and for a period of at least one week, people can come to receive to use. Ministry of Public Works signed the MoU. With the Ministry of Personnel, Public Complaints and Pensions of the Republic of India
