(Phnom Penh): The changing situation of the war in the Middle East is in the eyes of economic analysts as it will continue to affect the world economy. Dr. Ky Sereywat, an economist and chairman of the China Institute of Education, argues that the world economy would grow if Iran did not go directly to war in the Middle East.
According to the expert, in an interview with Fresh News last week, global economic growth projected at around 2% could turn into a slowdown if Iran is a big brother. One in the Middle East directly intervened in the Middle East war against Israel, with the United States as its base.
He added that if Iran were directly involved in the Middle East war, the oil crisis could lead to oil shortages and rising oil prices. At the same time, many other crises may also emerge due to the war in the Middle East.
However, for Cambodia, which is far from the region can also suffer from negative and positive effects. This is an additional confirmation from Dr. Ky Sereyvath.
Khmer civilization experts ask stakeholders to jointly develop this martial art to be trained in education
(Phnom Penh): Expert on Khmer civilization, Mr. Rath Sandab, on April 22, 2024, requested all stakeholders, whether the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Cambodian Bokator Federation and bokator teachers to jointly develop this martial art training. In the field of education. According to Mr. Rath, listening to bokator is a national martial art that we must promote, especially in the public and private schools.
The idea of Khmer civilization experts after seeing that bokator teachers in private schools are too expensive to be included in the curriculum. At the same time, this martial art is not yet taught in public schools.
For Mr. Rath Sandab suggested that if the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports together with the Federation of Cambodian Bokator facilitates the training of bokator in the field of education, this national martial arts will grow throughout the country.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Education has not yet commented on the matter.
Ministry of Commerce prohibits the use of certain words and actions in the promotion of products, goods and services
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce has issued a proclamation banning the promotion of certain words to sell products, goods and services that contain false commercial descriptions.
In a proclamation issued by the Ministry of Commerce on April 22, 2024, the Ministry of Commerce stated that it is prohibited to advertise the sale of products, goods and services that contain false or misleading advertisements:
* Encourage minors to think, act, speak or act contrary to tradition and morality, adversely affect the health, safety or natural development of minors.
* Use the best words or phrases, number one, superior, unparalleled, or words with similar meanings without proper documentation specified by the relevant ministries, institutions and authorities
* Use words or phrases such as win, scratch, win, buy, win, open, win, win, win, win, win, win, win, buy, win, buy more, buy more, or use words or phrases that have similar meanings by individuals The business does not specify to the consumer the types of products, goods and services to be provided.
* Use words, writings or pictures that are false, misleading or distorting the truth, pornography, erotic, obscene words
* Hiring or harassing an individual to spread falsehoods that they have received rewards or other benefits from any product, goods or service
* Compare its products, goods and services with the intention of degrading or affecting the products, goods and services of other persons
* Perform any gesture that harms the products, goods and services of another person in violation of other relevant provisions.
Please note that this post identifies some unfair practices in business that are not covered by the Consumer Protection Act in relation to advertising and sales promotion to protect the rights and interests of consumers. Mr. Kheng Song and Ms. Sum Thavy donated $ 2,000 on the occasion of the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2024
