Minister Peng Porna chaired a meeting to review the report on the situation of traffic signs along the national road to contribute to reducing traffic accidents
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Peng Po Na, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this morning, April 22, 2024, chaired a meeting to review the study report on the traffic signs along the national road based on the road study report. National No. 1, No. 6 and No. 61 by the General Technical Department of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. The meeting was attended by the leaders of the Ministry and professional officials from the relevant General Departments.
The purpose of this meeting was to review and comment on the study report to evaluate the pilot implementation on National Road No. 1, No. 6 and No. 61 based on the data collected from traffic signs, especially speed limit signs. Technical standards and requirements for current traffic growth.
The whole meeting discussed vigorously, providing additional input for effective and sustainable implementation, contributing to reducing traffic accidents, saving travel time and improving the beauty and public order.
(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of Mr. Bui Thanh Son, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, led a delegation of the ASEAN Secretariat to pay an official visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and participate in future forums. ASEAN and on the morning of Monday, April 22, 2024.
In Hanoi, the ASEAN Secretary-General met with Vietnamese Minister of Industry and Trade Nguyen Hong Dien. The two sides discussed the progress of ASEAN economic cooperation as well as Vietnam's contribution to regional trade, strengthening supply chain resilience and the implementation of regional economic partnerships.
Later, the ASEAN Secretary-General met with ASEAN youth to discuss the role of ASEAN youth in shaping the future of ASEAN. The ASEAN Secretary-General acknowledged the significant impact of youth-led initiatives and the active participation of young people in promoting awareness, solidarity and progress, and encouraged them to continue to actively contribute to building ASEAN Community.
The ASEAN Secretary-General also met with representatives of the Vietnam Diplomatic Academy. During the meeting, the two sides discussed ways to strengthen the cooperation and participation of research institutes and stressed the importance of increasing educational exchanges in the region.
Finally, the ASEAN Secretary-General hosted a welcome dinner hosted by Bui Thanh Son on the occasion of the ASEAN Future Forum. Ministry of Information Spokesperson: Professional journalists must respect professional ethics in order to gain trust and social value
