(Phnom Penh): On Monday evening, April 22, 2024, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, allowed Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi to pay a courtesy call and discuss work.
Wang Yi, a member of the Politburo and chairman of the Foreign Affairs Committee of the CPC Central Committee, arrived in Cambodia on the afternoon of April 21, 2024 for a three-day official visit.
Immediately on Cambodian soil, Mr. Wang Yi came to meet and hear with the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni. Afterwards, Mr. Wang Yi met with Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Head of Cambodian Diplomacy.
On the morning of April 22, 2024, Mr. Wang Yi attended the 7th Meeting of the Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee at the Council for the Development of Cambodia, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice Chairman of the Group. Cambodia Development Advisor.
Both sides also held a handover ceremony of the diary of the kingdom of Chenla about the territory, traditions and customs translated into Khmer.
On Monday afternoon, April 22, 2024, Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, also allowed Mr. Wang Yi to pay a courtesy call and discuss work.
Wang Yi is the most frequent Chinese diplomat to visit Cambodia. He just visited Cambodia in August 2023. Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia: Education as a Priority in Social and Economic Development
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sum Sansith, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, stated that education is an important priority in the social and economic development of the Royal Government, in which the Royal Government has continuously restored and strengthened the education sector to improve the quality of education and Build school buildings with the goal of creating human resources everywhere.
Mr. Sum Sannisith made the remarks at the inauguration ceremony of O Teuk Thla Primary School in Kraya Commune, Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province on April 22, 2024.
Mr. Sum Sanisith said, "Under the umbrella of peace led by the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia and the current Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has made education a priority. Social and economic development in this sense, the Royal Government has restored and strengthened the education sector.
He continued that, in fact, Kampong Thom province has Dr. Chea Chanto, Honorary Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia and a Member of Parliament for Kampong Thom constituency, has always worked hard to build many achievements in the province, including the construction of school buildings. Primary, secondary and high schools.
Mr. Sum Sannisith thanked KBR PRASAC Bank for funding the construction of the new O Teuk Thla Primary School at the request of the National Bank of Cambodia. All banks to contribute to social development and human resources in Cambodia.
Mr. Long Kiseng, Governor of Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province, said that Mr. Sum Sanisit's good gesture at this time clearly demonstrated the values of the leadership and the virtuous leadership that is always associated with happiness. Citizens, teachers, students of all local educational institutions.
