(Phnom Penh): The meeting of the Organizing Committee for the 6th Meeting between Samdech Moha Bovatei Hun Manet, Prime Minister and Journalists 2024 was held on the morning of April 22, 2024 at Chaktomuk Mongkul Meeting Hall, Office of the Ministry of Information. Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information and Chairman of the Organizing Committee.
Meeting on this occasion to review all the work that each sub-committee has decided to implement and expedite the remaining work as soon as possible to make it easier for journalists to register and participate in the meeting between the King. Hun Manet with about 5,000 journalists for the 6th time in 2024 at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Convention Center on May 3, 2024.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra confirmed that the meeting between journalists and the head of government, which is scheduled to take place on May 3, 2024, coincides with the celebration of World Press Freedom Day.
Mr. Neth Pheakdra also emphasized that the decision to select May 3, 2024 for the meeting between journalists and the head of the Royal Government is the decision of the Prime Minister as well as the decision of the Royal Government.
The Ministry of Information will prepare for this meeting and will also collect issues and concerns raised by radio, television and journalists in a joint framework to submit to the Prime Minister for review and resolution.
Please be reminded that every year on January 14, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister, authorizes the organization of a meeting between journalists and the Prime Minister to provide an opportunity for journalists to discuss issues. Any suggestions or concerns to submit to the head of the Royal Government for review and assistance.
