International Mathematics Competition in Australia, the best student of Cambodia won the first place and won 12 gold, silver and bronze medals
Raised on the occasion of bringing success to the first place and gold medal on April 22, 2024, the best student Meng Lay Sun said that in order to be able to get this medal abroad, we must first Measure your ability to do a lot of math exercises, strengthen the ability to solve a lot of homework and do a lot of research, do self-study and learn more and leave less time to play.
Outstanding student Meng Lay Sun also stated that he is very proud to be able to succeed in this competition, which is also a demonstration of the ability of Cambodian children on international chat. This outstanding student also encourages the younger generation to study hard and do not give up studying hard when faced with small obstacles, to work harder to get better knowledge.
Ms. Phon Serey Vathany, a teacher and a parent, said that all competitions for students to show their ability is very important for students and through the excellent results of students now really prove that. Khmer children are really capable, not inferior to foreigners, so parents of all students should encourage their children to study harder.
According to Kong Salimin, Bright's Coordinator for Overseas Students, the IMEC International Mathematics Competition is open to students from grades 3 to 12, and there are candidates for the qualifying round. There are 378 candidates in 12 districts in the country.
Mr. Kong Salimin added that for the finalists in Australia, there were students from 10 countries with more than 150 candidates, and for the 12 candidates from Cambodia, all 12 winners won 3 gold medals. With the first place winner, 5 silver medals and 4 bronze medals.
Mr. Kong Salimin also expressed his happiness after seeing the success of Cambodian students and claimed that Cambodian students are really capable and have the opportunity to compete on a world-class level. For the IMEC International Mathematics Competition, it shows that Cambodia's best students are really good, while Cambodia won the first place and has 12 more gold, silver and bronze medals than our neighboring countries.
