(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, expressed his hope that the three-day visit of Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi to Cambodia will have some discussions on the Funan Techo Canal project. He also expects the visit to boost investment and trade between the two countries.
Dr. Kin Phea said that Wang Yi's visit to Cambodia was not linked to the Funan Techo Canal, nor was it necessary to clear up the US-Vietnam accusation on the canal, but he hoped that There was some discussion about Prek Chun Funan Techo.
Dr. Kin Phea said that China and Cambodia are the countries that have signed an agreement to build a community of Cambodia and China with a common destiny, and in addition, the two countries are steel friends with many important agreements. In particular, the hexagonal diamond cooperation between Cambodia and China, which was just signed in 2023.
He added that the visit would improve the outcome of the agreement between the two leaders, especially to promote investment, trade and people-to-people exchanges, as this year is a year of exchanges between the two countries. People and people of Cambodia-China.
He added that from a political point of view, Cambodia has become an important country for China, the world's second largest economy. China and Cambodia need each other in the international arena, and the deep and close relationship between Cambodia and China is also an important scale in balancing its foreign policy, both regionally and internationally. The world.
He added that the visit will also encourage more Chinese investors to come to Cambodia, especially to restore the image of Sihanoukville, which has been relevant to the Chinese people in the past, and the volume of trade between the two countries is also hopeful. That will be encouraged as well.
