(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Urban Solid Waste Management Enterprise has opened a recruitment session for the Phnom Penh Municipal Solid Waste Management Enterprise (CSF) by designating Chea Sim Santhor Mok High School as its center. Exam on the morning of April 21, 2024.
According to Ms. Kong Rattanakvatey, Deputy Director General of the Enterprise (CES), there were 114 female candidates, 68 of whom were female. 31 people in Phnom Penh.
She added that this exam is held throughout the morning of April 21, which is divided into two subjects: * First: general knowledge and foreign languages, * Second: professional knowledge.
There are 3 hours of specialized knowledge, including Procurement, Auditing, Accounting, Administration, Personnel (IT), Secretariat, Business Services. The general knowledge exam lasts 50 minutes. This is the first recruitment exam for a solid waste management enterprise in Phnom Penh, formerly the Phnom Penh Solid Waste Management Authority.
Through this recruitment exam, it will fill the staff who have enough ability to contribute to the management of garbage, solid waste in Phnom Penh to be more effective, maintain the aesthetics of the city environment that Phnom Penh administration is taking. Very attentive.
It should be noted that through the growth of the population and the living standard of the people in Phnom Penh, there is an increase in the problem of solid waste (garbage) is a challenge that the Phnom Penh administration has introduced a number of measures to educate people about Keep trash in order, both in packaging and in a timely manner. Penalties for dumping rubbish at the wrong location.
