Chinese Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Regular Press Conference on April 21, 2024 This is to complete a three-day official visit from April 21 to 23, 2024. His Majesty the King allows Wang Yi to attend court hearing
(Phnom Penh): Immediately after stepping on Cambodian soil, on Sunday afternoon, April 21, 2024, Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi received a royal permission from His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni to pay his respects. And hearings in the Royal Palace.
It should be noted that Mr. Wang Yi, Member of the Political Bureau and Chairman of the Foreign Affairs Committee of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China, arrived in Cambodia at 2:30 pm on April 21, 2024. This is for a three-day official visit.
The Chinese diplomat will pay an official visit to Cambodia until April 23, 2024. In addition to paying a courtesy call on the King, Wang Yi will also pay a separate courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, and Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Mr. Wang Yi will also co-chair with Mr. Sun Chanthol, Deputy Prime Minister and First Vice-Chairman of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, to chair the 7th Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee Meeting. He will also hold bilateral talks with Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation Sok Chenda Sophea to exchange views on further strengthening existing and better relations in all fields.
Wang Yi is the most frequently visited Chinese diplomat in Cambodia. He just visited Cambodia in August 2023. Minister Tho Chetha inspects the condition of Bat Roka Reservoir and the location to be rehabilitated in Samrong District, Takeo Province
Please be informed that Bot Roka Reservoir is located in Samrong Commune, Samrong District, Takeo Province. It is capable of irrigating 268 hectares of wet paddy land and 238 hectares of dry paddy land.
According to the Minister, according to the actual inspection on the use of basin water in the past, there is no shortage of water for irrigating wet and dry season rice, there is a shortage of water only to produce clean water to supply people between the months. March to June due to shallow basins and increasing demand for water.
At the same time, the Minister continued that since 2012 until now, the Bot Roka Water Treatment Plant has been pumping about 4,000 cubic meters of water per day to produce clean water to supply to 6939 families living in 57 villages of 5 communes in Samrong district, Takeo province.
It should be noted that as an urgent solution, the authorities, together with the Bot Roka water treatment station, took water from a private pond near the station to supply water to the daily use of the people, and at the same time, the machine also sent Reach the pool restoration site as well.
