(Kampong Speu): On Sunday morning, April 21, 2024, Mr. Hun Many, Meditation Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Working Group of the Kampong Speu Provincial Assistance Party, chaired a meeting with the working group and the Party Committee. The 10 districts and communes of Samaki Monichey district at the district party headquarters.
Attending the meeting were Mr. Sam Rithy, Deputy Chairman of the Working Group, Mr. Yim Sokhom, Vice Chairman of the Provincial Party Committee, His Excellency the Chairman of the District Assistance Team, Mr. and Mrs. Chairman of the Working Group of the Party and District and Commune Party Committees, a total of 60 people. The meeting was held to update the work and control the situation towards the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council elections on May 26, 2024.
According to the report of Mr. Muong Thi, Chairman of the Samaki Monichey District Party Committee, in the last 5th Senate election, the district party together with the working group at all levels tried to move according to the guidelines of the middle level. Promote the election movement and ensure a huge victory for the party.
Towards the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council elections, the district party has prepared a plan and is continuously implementing it. At the same time, the meeting also discussed and shared some experiences and challenges encountered directly to the meeting to review and make recommendations.
Mr. Hun Many thanked the working group and party committees at all levels for their hard work for the party in the past. He recommended that the working group should work harder to build the party and serve the people at the local level to provide more warmth and confidence in the party.
At the same time, for the upcoming election, please work hard to pay attention to the health status and other issues of the electorate to ensure the victory of the party.
Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al urges officials and relevant authorities in Oddar Meanchey province to work together to achieve the land registration plan as soon as possible
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Say Sam Al, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, urged the relevant officials and authorities in Oddar Meanchey province to work together to achieve the land registration plan. As soon as possible.
The Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province stated that there are an estimated 180,000 plots in the whole province, 122,600 plots for the two-year registration period (2024-2025), with a total of 54,445 titles already registered. The title includes the systematic registration, the first piece of land registration, the state land registration, the pedagogical land registration work, and the pagoda.
Mr. SAY Sam Al emphasized that in order to promote land registration in accordance with the land registration policy, the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration, which has a Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, must work hard to resolve disputes out of court and Internal unity and solidarity only make the institution grow and give confidence to the people.
Khmer Civilization Expert: Can a retaliatory attack between Iran and Israel erupt into war?
In this tense situation, the question arises as to whether a retaliatory strike between Iran and Israel could erupt into war.
Israel's attack on Iran is a symbolic equation because Israel wants to divert the international community's attention against the Gaza Strip, as Israel has been using artificial intelligence technology since the start of the Gaza war. The goal is to draw pictures of buildings and homes to serve the war sector, causing the deaths of tens of thousands of women and children in Gaza.
For this reason, there are two grounds to calculate Iran's intentions in retaliation:
* Scenario 1: It is possible that Iran miscalculated to try to cause real damage to Israel by simply being dissatisfied with the actions of the enemy, especially the use of ballistic missiles and targeting military bases in the south. Of Israel.
* Second scenario: It is also possible that Iran did not intend to cause serious damage to Israel, as Tehran only intended to create a symbolic revenge after Israel attacked its embassy.
