Villagers in Talat Commune, Sesan District, Stung Treng Province Collect Fruits
(Stung Treng): Before the growing season, people in Talat commune who used to enjoy non-timber forest products came into the forest to pick dried fruits if soaked in water, mixed with sugar and eaten as cold food when Hot weather.
Mr. Talit, Commune Chief of Talat, supported the efforts of our people, but to enter the forest to find this fruit, the sleeper must know to inform the local authorities such as village chiefs or police officers to make it easier for us. To help each other when there is a risk by accident.
Ms. Phoun Kham Phay, a resident of Svay Rieng village, Talat commune, confirmed that this business is a tradition that our people have been following for a long time, according to the ancestral tradition of living in Sre Chamkar district.
She said that at present, these fruits are not abundant because some of the dense forests that people used to go to have been cut down by crooks and cleared a lot of natural resources, and in this case, the district authorities are taking action.
Please note that this fruit is collected in the village for 50,000 riel per kilogram and sold at the market for 60,000 riel, the number one quality fruit that customers like to eat, thinking that it is a kind of fruit. Medicines help health. 3 suspects arrested for drug trafficking and storage in Trapeang Prasat and Anlong Veng districts
(Oddar Meanchey): Three suspects living in Trapeang Prasat and Anlong Veng districts of Oddar Meanchey province were arrested by the Provincial Anti-Drug Bureau for drug trafficking and storage.
According to the report of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie, on the orders of Brigadier General Ly Darith, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, on April 19, 2024, the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Investigation and Cooperation Force cooperated with Trapeang Prasat District. Led by Lieutenant Colonel But Savuth, Director of the Anti-Drug Office, cracked down on cases of illegal storage and trafficking of drugs in Srah Chrey village, Trapeang Prasat commune, Trapeang Prasat district.
As a result, one suspect, Sim Bo, a 27-year-old man living in the upper commune, was arrested and confiscated a large package of white gram powder (ice cubes) and 15 small glasses weighing 4.61 grams, a mobile phone. 20,000 Khmer Riel and some drug paraphernalia.
In the afternoon of the same day, the specialized forces continued to crack down on Svay Chek village, Thlat commune, Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province.
Currently, the suspect and the above exhibits are being processed by the Provincial Gendarmerie to be sent to the Provincial Court for legal action.
Deputy PM Say Sam Al Urges Land Registration Working Group to Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Say Sam Al, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, urged the land registration team for the people in Preah Vihear province to fulfill their duties properly and promptly in accordance with the principles of the Royal Government with the President. Hun Manet is the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Mr. Kim Rithy said that Preah Vihear province has a total area of 13,419.63 square kilometers, with a total population of 277,465 people, equivalent to 66,683 families, with a population density of 20 people per square kilometer. 1 city and 7 districts equal to 51 communes, sangkats and 232 villages.
Regarding the progress of land registration in Preah Vihear province, the provincial governor registered 99 villages in 232 villages, equal to 42% of the total number of villages in the province, and issued 70,661 title deeds. 37% of the estimated number of plots throughout the province, a total of 186,990 plots.
On that occasion, Mr. Kim Rithy also urged all members of the meeting to pay attention to the recommendations and guidelines of the Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs. To successfully implement land registration work in Preah Vihear province.
Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al stated that the Royal Government's Pentagon Strategic Policy under the leadership of His Majesty King Hun Manet, land registration is an important issue that the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia pays close attention to, so urge the Land Registration Working Group. The people must strive to fulfill this task well, accurately and quickly in accordance with the principles of the Royal Government.
