However, many people choose to deposit money in the bank because of the high interest rate and easy withdrawal, unlike the deposit through the purchase of insurance at a lower interest rate.
On this question, Mr. Bou Chanphiro, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, told about the benefits of buying insurance, both protection and savings.
He explained that although savings with insurance earn less interest than banks, saving with insurance allows you to both protect against financial burdens when risks arise and get savings plus interest rates.
He explained that insurance is a service to protect the financial burden when there is a risk. If an individual buys a package of insurance services at risk, they will be reimbursed.
He said that for depositing savings in the bank is higher, but if there is a risk or no risk is to get the amount of savings. In particular, for the purchase of insurance, if there is a risk during that time, you will receive a large amount of money in excess of the amount saved. And if there is no risk, you will also get your savings back plus interest.
Mr. Peru said that the cost of insurance varies from country to country, and the compensation also varies according to the cost of the service. However, the price of insurance packages in Cambodia is similar to other countries in the ASEAN region.
