An unidentified bomb exploded in a forest in Sen Monorom City, Mondulkiri Province, killing four people and injuring two others.
(Mondulkiri): A report from Mondulkiri province said that on the afternoon of April 20, 2024, an unknown source explosion occurred in the forest in Sre E village, Romnea commune, Sen Monorom city, causing people Four were killed and two were seriously injured.
According to the report, the victim was a rattan picker in the forest, and after the horrific explosion, only the mother and two children survived and tried to walk to the village with full injuries. It is very sympathetic to tell the villagers and ask for their help.
According to preliminary information from the victim told the villagers, all the victims were walking in the forest, enjoying the natural fruit like a corpse, and found an unexploded ordnance. After seeing this, the mother and her two children walked out of the scene. The bomber struck shortly after noon in front of a police station, killing four people. The bomber struck shortly after noon in front of a crowd of mourners. Well.
Currently, the competent authorities are intervening to rescue and further research.
