Interior Ministry spokesman: 84 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on April 20
(Phnom Penh): At least 84 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on April 20, 2024 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on April 21, 2024.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 84 suspects, 74 were arrested in 22 drug cases and 10 were arrested in eight criminal cases.
San Sang, a former CNRP lawmaker and vice-president of the Khmer Krom Association, said the ark was established in 2002 and that he personally proposed naming it "Khmer Kampuchea Krom Meanchey" to the organizing committee. National and International Festival as the President of the Khmer Krom Association at that time.
Mr. San Sang reminded that the name "Khmer Kampuchea Krom Meanchey" led to a lot of discussion and balance in the National and International Festival Organizing Committee at that time because of concerns about affecting the relationship between Cambodia and Vietnam.
According to Mr. San Sang, after disagreeing on the use of the name "Khmer Kampuchea Krom Meanchey", Mr. Min Khin also called Samdech Techo Hun Sen because only Samdech Techo could achieve it.
Mr. San Sang continued that immediately after consulting, Samdech Techo decided and allowed the use of the name "Kampuchea Krom Meanchey" on the Khmer Krom boat.
Mr. San Sang considered Samdech Techo as the founder of the name of the Khmer Krom boat and also embedded the deep meaning of Samdech Techo's heart to the Khmer Kampuchea Krom.
Khmer Krom from Preah Trapeang province, Mr. San Sang, after joining the political life with the Cambodian People's Party, he also intends to make two boats to take to the pagoda on the territory of Khmer Krom as a souvenir and as a contribution to preserve the culture of the Khmer Krom.
