Deputy Prime Minister Say Samal urges land registration team to work diligently and accurately in accordance with Royal Government policy
(Siem Reap): Deputy Prime Minister Say Samal, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, urged the Land Registration Working Group to fulfill its duties accurately and expeditiously in accordance with the guidelines set by the Royal Government.
He stressed that the expert team must continue the activities of preparing the land registration around the Tonle Sap Lake to be completed effectively and accurately with the correction by cutting off the people who actually settled and lived for a long time. Come on. However, the work of registering land for those people is not over yet, which requires the continuation of activities in the new government.
Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al made a strong speech on the occasion of chairing a meeting to promote land registration in Siem Reap province this morning, April 20, 2024, at the Siem Reap Provincial Hall with the participation of Mr. Prak Sophoan, Provincial Governor. Leaders of the armed forces, heads of departments and units around many provinces also participated.
The Deputy Prime Minister continued that recently, Samdech Hun Sen said that the work to be done is divided into two parts: face-to-face work and long-term work. The work ahead must be completed efficiently and accurately through proper land registration and systematic registration. The second step is to complete the registration after the Tonle Sap Lake Authority has re-mapped and re-erected the poles and put them into the system.
Deputy Prime Minister Say Samal stressed that in order to promote land registration in accordance with the policy of "Land Registration, End of Satisfactory Services and Conflict-Free Environment", the Provincial Administration, with the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs as its staff, must strive to resolve disputes out of court. And internal unity and solidarity only makes the institution grow and give confidence to the people.
