Dr. Kao Kim Hourn will lead a delegation of the ASEAN Secretariat to pay an official visit to Vietnam and participate in the ASEAN Future Forum from 22 to 23 April
At the invitation of Bui Thanh Son, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), will pay an official visit to the ASEAN Secretariat to pay an official visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam. ASEAN from 22 to 23 April 2024.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn will also meet with leaders of the Vietnam Diplomatic Academy and meet with youth representatives from Vietnam and other ASEAN members. The ASEAN Secretary-General will also address the ASEAN Future Forum, where he will convey the message of the ASEAN story to the media.
Thai army says fighting resumes on Thai-Myanmar border
BANGKOK, April 20 (Xinhua) - Armed clashes between Myanmar military forces and ethnic armed groups have erupted again near a major city on the Thai border on Saturday. Quiet for a week. This is according to a release by the AFP news agency.
Fighting erupted around Myanmar's Myawaddy town on the Thai border in early April and military forces withdrew from the city. The lull lasted only a week with no reports of fighting, although ASEAN issued a statement expressing concern over the situation in Myanmar on Friday, April 19.
(Stung Treng): 88 families in Vern Sean village, Ou Svay commune, Borey Ou Svay Sen Chey district, Stung Treng province are happy to get a bridge and a convenient road, while in the past, people had to use boats as a means of transportation.
Vern Sean village is a remote village in O'Svay commune, more than 20 kilometers away from the district town. There are no roads and bridges for travel.
On the occasion of inspecting the achievements of the bridge from Borey O'Svay Senchey district town to Vern Sean village on the evening of April 19, 2024, Mr. Limina, Borey O'Svay Senchey district governor confirmed that "the district administration has solved this difficulty by using The district development budget to build a wooden bridge, a concrete bridge connecting the red gravel road, which the Department of Rural Development built in 2021 for about 700 families to use for public use.
The district governor said that after the bridge is connected, the district administration has another vision is to build a road along the mouth of the Mekong River to connect to the land of Stung Treng to serve the means of transportation of agricultural products. Farmers will encourage tourism to grow in this area as well.
Ms. Hee Chandon, Vern Sean Village Chief, supported this vision because the people living in this area since 1960 have never had a road for bicycles or motorbikes, using only boats as a means of transportation and transportation.
She continued: "This new achievement is the hope of the people in the countryside, because in the past, our farmers, agricultural products have no market to order, the bride is not engaged. And now there are roads, bridges, car dealers to buy a house, showing the value that comes from the development under the leadership of our government.
Mr. Phan Ra, representing the people in this village, was very happy when there was such a good road and bridge in the village, because the people could easily travel as fast as when they were sick to the children's health center to go to school on time.
