Samdech Techo Hun Sen Sends Condolences to Ms. Oum Pharan on the Death of Professor Sambo Manara, Her Husband
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of Cambodia, on April 20, 2024, sent a letter of condolences to Ms. Oum Pharan on the death of Professor Sambo Manara, her husband.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's letter reads as follows: "My wife and I are sad and upset after receiving the sad news that His Excellency Professor Sambo Manara, Personal Adviser to the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, who is the husband of Lok Chumteav He passed away on Saturday, April 20, 2024 at 5:40 AM at the age of 67 due to illness.
In this sad time, my wife and I would like to express our condolences to Lok Chumteav and her family for the loss of their beloved husbands, fathers, grandfathers, and great devotion to their wives, children, grandchildren, and all their close relatives and friends.
The death of His Excellency Professor Sambo Manara is the loss of the nation's important human resources who sacrificed their physical and mental strength to serve the country in all circumstances in order to serve the national interests in the past. Even though His Excellency's body has really disappeared, the deeds of merit, honor and dignity will remain in the hearts of his wife, children and close relatives forever.
