The Club of Cambodian Journalists calls on journalists, users of social media, to consider all aspects before posting or posting information linked to violent images.
(Phnom Penh): Recently, the Club of Cambodian Journalists (CCJ) has observed that a number of newspapers and social media outlets have published information with images showing serious atrocities committed from professional ethics. Press.
Recently, both the press and some social media published a video link of the violence against a woman in a Borey in Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The Club of Cambodian Journalists considers that the broadcast completely deviates from the ethics of the journalism profession, affecting the social ethics and values of the journalism profession in Cambodia.
The Club of Cambodian Journalists calls on journalists, users of social media, to consider all aspects before publishing or posting any information, especially journalists must be involved in promoting the implementation of professional ethics, which is a strong barrier. Strong for journalists.
The Club of Cambodian Journalists hopes that both journalists and social media users will take a responsible approach to professional ethics, social ethics in order to maintain the values and dignity of citizens living in civil society. The National Assembly has been paying close attention to reform and good governance.
