(Phnom Penh): The building of modern surgical equipment at Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital worth nearly 20 million dollars with the help of the Royal Government and the people of Japan was officially inaugurated on Saturday morning, the 12th of Chet Chhnang Rong Chhasak 2567 is on April 20, 2024.
The inauguration ceremony of the surgical service building, called the "Surgical Service Center Building", was presided over by His Majesty the King of Cambodia Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Ou Nou Atsushi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia.
Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital is a hospital that plays an important role in providing health services, which was opened in 1929 when Cambodia was under French colonization and continued to provide services until April 17, 1975. The hospital was completely shut down during Democratic Kampuchea for almost four years.
The inaugural "Surgical Service Center Building" will further improve the provision of health services in the Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital.
Construction of the "Surgical Service Center" began on December 1, 2021 and was completed on October 30, 2023. The building has 4 floors and has different service functions.
Ground floor: Used for outpatient services, emergency services, medical imaging services, support services, laundry and generator rooms.
1st floor: Used to provide services in the field of surgery, surgery and sedation, and sterilization and equipment management.
2nd floor: Used to provide orthopedic and traumatic services and specialize in ear, nose, throat and facial and jaw surgery.
3rd floor: Used to provide services in abdominal and thoracic physiology, urology and neurology.
Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al urges stakeholders to work together to achieve the Royal Government's plan to register land for citizens
(Kampong Thom): During a meeting to discuss the systematic registration of land in Kampong Thom province on the afternoon of April 19, 2024, Mr. Say Sam Al, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, stated that land registration Cadastral units do not work alone, but must work together.
The meeting was attended by a delegation from the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, provincial governors, commanders of the three forces, heads of departments, units, district governors, commune councils and relevant officials, as well as deputy chiefs, chiefs, deputy chiefs of offices. And several officials of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, confirmed that the systematic land registration in Kampong Thom Province is under the close supervision of the Director of the Department and officials of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral. The Systematic Land Registration Working Group has registered 382 villages in 34 communes, measuring 368,264 plots and distributed 339,057 titles.
Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al stated that the Royal Government's Pentagon Strategic Policy under the leadership of Samdech Hun Manet, land registration is an important issue that the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia pays close attention to, so please urge the Land Registration Working Group to The people must strive to fulfill this task well, accurately and quickly in accordance with the principles of the Royal Government.
He added that in order to promote land registration in accordance with the policy of "land registration, termination of satisfactory services and conflict-free environment", the provincial administration, with the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs as its staff, strives to resolve disputes outside the judiciary and solidarity and unity. In order to make the institution grow and give confidence to the people.
