Cambodian Association of Gastroenterologists and Private Sector Organizes World Liver Health Day
(Phnom Penh): Liver cancer (HCC) is classified as the most common cancer in the world and has a high mortality rate, which causes and risk factors for liver cancer, including various diseases that cause inflammation. Chronic liver disease and cirrhosis, such as hepatitis C, hepatitis B, chronic alcohol consumption, fatty liver disease due to overweight and other risk factors, including diabetes and eating poisonous mushrooms. .
The ceremony was held at the Phnom Penh Hotel in the presence of Prof. Oum Serey Vichet, President of the Cambodian Association of Gastroenterologists, and with the participation of representatives of Mega Company and many specialists from all public hospitals. Private clinics in Phnom Penh and other provinces.
At the same time, according to Dr. Thea Vuthy, Deputy Director of Stomach, Intestine, Liver, Hemorrhoids of Ang Duong Hospital, said that in order to maintain good liver health, you should avoid drinking alcohol and smoking and oily things. And too much fat, in which over-the-counter medications can also lead to liver damage.
Dr. Theavuthy said that until now, hepatitis C has been found to be cured. For hepatitis C with cirrhosis, the treatment period is only 3 months, while for cirrhosis, the treatment is up to 6 months. For the treatment of hepatitis B, there are some complexities that require a number of conditions that should be treated and should not be treated.
Dr. Theavuthy also sent a message urging people with pre-existing liver disease to see a specialist for timely evaluation and treatment and to avoid smoking and drinking alcohol. For those who do not have liver problems to protect the liver should also avoid smoking and drinking alcohol and should see a specialist for a thorough examination.
