(Phnom Penh): The Office of the Spokesperson of the Ministry of Information on the evening of April 19, 2024 issued a press release announcing the results of the orientation and input collection workshop to prepare the "Journalism Professional Charter" held in Framework for improving the quality, ethics and professional values for journalism careers in Cambodia.
The workshop was chaired by Mr. Neth Pheakdra, Minister of Information, with a total of 325 participants, consisting of journalists from both traditional and modern media, from the Media Unit of the Cambodian Press Association and officials. Receive information from other institutions.
Minister Neth Pheakdra emphasized that this workshop was recorded as the first event for this type of meeting to provide an opportunity for journalists, media units, media associations and all participants to express their views in discussions and Provides key inputs for the establishment of a common "Professional Journalism for Journalism" in Cambodia.
Once established, the Press Professional Charter will become the standard of national professional ethics for all stakeholders to respect and abide by, in order to continue to contribute to the better development of democracy in Cambodia through Continuing to provide a conducive environment for the effective and professional implementation of press freedom and freedom of expression in Cambodia.
The Minister stressed the importance of initiating the establishment of the Professional Code of Journalism, saying that it would contribute to the promotion of press freedom in Cambodia by strengthening the quality and capacity of the profession, strengthening respect for professional ethics and maintaining order in the country. Information sector.
