(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dim Sovannarom, Member of the NEC and Chairman of the NEC Information Reaction Team, stated that since the NEC held its own elections since 1998, Cambodia has never postponed the election. Once upon a time, elections went as planned, which is the pride of the NEC of Cambodia, which is one of the conditions for free, fair and just elections, the true heart of democracy that the international community considers. That democracy is working well.
Mr. Dim Sovannarom made this remark while holding a press conference with the media before leaving to observe the parliamentary elections in the Maldives on the afternoon of April 19, 2024 at Phnom Penh International Airport. (VIP port).
Mr. Dim Sovannarom stated that the true heart of democracy is free and fair elections, and that free, fair and just elections, which respond to planned elections without delay, are considered by the international community. As a democracy, it works well.
Please be informed that the election in Cambodia through the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991 required Cambodia to hold free and fair general elections to end the conflict, establish a governing body and build the rule of law.
Elections are organized in a universal and non-universal manner. For the general election, the eligible voters refer to Cambodian citizens of either sex who are 18 years of age or older and have their names on the voter list. All districts in position. All elections allow political parties, national and international organizations to observe.
