It should be noted that the road to be auctioned on this occasion is 4,500 meters long, 6 meters wide and 0.15 meters thick, two drains and the bid price is 500,814,709 Riels. The winning bidder is 150,000,000 Riels. ASEAN Secretary-General Congratulates Cambodian PM on 25th Anniversary of ASEAN Membership
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, sent an official congratulatory letter to His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia on the occasion of the 25th anniversary of Cambodia's accession to ASEAN on 30 May. April 1999.
The contents of the letter dated 17 April 2024 of the ASEAN Secretary-General have the following meanings:
2024 is 25 years since Cambodia officially became the 10th member of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) on April 30, 1999. On the occasion of this important 25th anniversary, I would like to extend my warmest congratulations to the Prime Minister and the people of Cambodia.
Since joining ASEAN on April 30, 1999, Cambodia has made remarkable strides toward strengthening peace, stability and economic prosperity in the region. Despite being severely affected by Kovid-19, Cambodia has succeeded in maintaining economic growth above 5% for the second year in a row while achieving some notable achievements. In social, educational and cultural development.
For ASEAN, Cambodia's membership has expanded the geographical scope of this regional organization to cover almost every country in Southeast Asia. It is true that Cambodia has made a significant contribution to ASEAN community building efforts, and its leadership was evident during Cambodia's chairmanship of ASEAN in 2002, 2012, and more recently in 2022.
In terms of ASEAN's external relations, Cambodia is currently playing an important role in facilitating ASEAN's dialogue partnership with Russia and will continue to be responsible for coordinating ASEAN-US relations this year, with both Russia and the United States The United States is a region with strong ties.
I firmly believe that under the skillful leadership of the President of Cambodia will continue to play an important role in building the ASEAN Community. I reaffirm the readiness of the ASEAN Secretariat to fully support Cambodia and ASEAN in achieving a peaceful, stable and prosperous ASEAN Community, which is our common goal.
Please accept, Excellency, the assurances of my highest consideration and the best wishes of the people of the Kingdom of Cambodia for greater prosperity.
Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia: Purchasing insurance is a purchase to protect the financial burden when the risk arises (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Bou Chanpirou, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia explained the benefits that people should buy and Use insurance because purchasing insurance is a purchase to protect the financial burden in the event of any eventual risk.
Mr. Bou Chanphiru said that in order to buy insurance, you must first know what is insurance? Insurance is a contract to protect when any risk arises because we do not know what will happen in the future, what happens is dangerous and when there is danger There is damage, loss of material or life, and if these problems occur, the next problem is the financial burden.
"Therefore, buying insurance is a financial purchase, which means that if there is an immediate risk, there will be an insurance company, a guarantor and a financial package to use in the future," said Bou Chanpiru. "Continue."
He added that if in a country people buy all the insurance, it means that people live in peace without worrying about any problems because people have the financial burden to be provided. By the insurance company if any accident happens to them.
Listen to Mr. Bou Chanphiro, Director General of the Cambodian Insurance Regulator:
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Bou Chanphiro, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, said that there are no exclusive insurance companies in Cambodia, there are currently three main types of companies: general insurance companies, life insurance companies and insurance groups. Small scale selling competitively.
Mr. Bou Chanphiru said that the insurance market in Cambodia still has potential, but after all, the knowledge of the Cambodian people is still limited in the insurance sector, even if they can afford to buy insurance.
In 2023, the insurance market in Cambodia will grow at an average annual rate of about 20%, with gross premiums continuing to reach more than $ 342 million.
There are 41 insurers operating in Cambodia with more than $ 1 billion in assets, including 18 general insurers, 15 life insurers, seven micro-insurers and one reinsurance company.
