General Department of Taxation issues guidelines on minimum tax exemption for enterprises as qualified investment projects
According to the instructions, the General Department of Taxation would like to introduce the following enterprises that are qualified investment projects (SEC-QIP):
1: Obtain the minimum tax exemption by having an independent audit report and keeping proper accounting records.
2: For enterprises as a SEC Newly registered entrants will receive a minimum tax exemption for the first year without having to submit an independent audit report to the General Department of Taxation. The following year, the SEC is required to submit an independent audit report to the General Department of Taxation no later than the end of June of each subsequent year.
