In a statement issued on Thursday night, the ASEAN foreign ministers said ASEAN was "deeply concerned" about the recent escalation of the conflict, including in Myawaddy, and urged both sides to work together. Immediately end the violence in Myanmar, which has been in turmoil since the military took power in a coup in February 2021.
It is the latest setback for Myanmar's military regime, which in recent months has suffered a series of casualties on the battlefield, with some analysts seeing it as the biggest threat to the military government. So far, so good. Myawaddy is Myanmar's main trading port with Thailand and sees an annual trade flow of at least $ 1 billion.
The escalation of fighting in Myanmar has caused many people to flee across the border into Thailand, where gunfire and shelling can be heard. The Bangkok government has said it is ready to accept refugees from Myanmar, but the Thai foreign minister has warned that Thailand will not tolerate any violation of its sovereignty.
Capital Council Election Has 209 Polling Stations and 11,622 Voters
(Phnom Penh): For the 4th Mandate Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council Election in 2024, the NEC has decided on the first voter list with 209 polling stations and 11,622 voters. This is according to Mr. Heng Sileng, a member of the NEC.
A senior NEC official stressed that after reviewing and deciding on the initial voter list, the Department of Voter Data and Voter Registration has made four more copies of the initial voter list to be packaged and sent to the commission. Capital and Provincial Election Commission (CEC) to make public postings for the purpose of reviewing and correcting through complaints and / or objections.
Heng Sileng made this statement during a meeting with stakeholders on the preparation of the first voter list, the posting of the first voter list, the complaint or objection and the resolution of complaints on the voter list. First, the election of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council, 4th Mandate 2024, this morning, April 19, 2024.
Mr. Heng Sileng continued that the Department of Voter Data Management and Voter List must keep the original copy of the first voter list which the NEC has already decided, one copy as a document at the NEC and must be packaged at the office. Each voter shall submit the first voter list, one original and four copies, and send them to the NEC in time before the deadline.
Mr. Heng Sileng continued that the first voter list was posted on April 20, 2024 at the Secretariat of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (CEC) and posted at different places in the town. People in the capital and province in each place, 3 copies.
Mr. Seila was very happy and thanked Samdech Techo for allowing him to work for Samdech and Cambodia, especially to help Cambodian children by attracting investors to Cambodia, as well as accompanying the Cambodian delegation to Davos. Switzerland many times.
In response, Samdech Techo thanked Mr. Seila for reminiscing about the past of meeting him and his daughter in 1997 in Kampong Som. We have had peace and stability for more than 25 years since 1998. Eight months ago, Samdech Techo decided to transfer leadership to a new generation, and as a result, the legacy of peace continues, and economic growth continues. The new cabinet works well, maintaining stability and continuing to drive development.
Samdech Techo emphasized that in 1987, Samdech set four priorities: "Water, Road, Electricity, People", then more than 10 years ago, Samdech Techo changed people to the first priority. The new government has set the fifth angle of the Pentagon strategy as the technology angle and set a policy for vocational training of 1.5 million young people, and the Cambodian economy is based on knowledge and skills.
Samdech Techo thanked Mr. Sen Seila for his past training in hospitality skills and encouraged him to continue this training. Ministry of Interior and Phnom Penh Capital Administration Hold a Meeting to Disseminate Strategic Plan to Improve Territorial Administration, National Security, Public Order and Social Security 2024-2028
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Santi Dr. Mao Chandara, Acting Minister of the Ministry of Interior and Mr. Hun Surithy, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, this morning, April 19, 2024, held a meeting to disseminate the strategic plan on promotion. Territorial administration, national security, public order and social security 2024-2028 of the Ministry of Interior.
Mr. HUN Srithy stated that the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Manipur Hun Manet, has been paying close attention to the areas of national security, public order and social security, which are one of the main priority areas to support the parallel socio-economic development. According to the political program and strategy of the first phase.
Dr. Mao Chandara said that under the leadership of Samdech Hun Manet, the first phase of the Pentagon strategy for employment growth, equity, efficiency and sustainability, focusing on five priority areas from people, roads, water, electricity and technology to continue to build the foundation towards Achieve the vision of Cambodia 2030 as a high middle income country and 2050 as a high income country.
He said that in order to ensure the responsible role of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Interior has prepared a strategic plan on "improving territorial administration, national security, public order and social security as a road map." A clear roadmap for implementation from 2024 to 2028 aims to contribute to the implementation of the first phase of the Pentagon strategy to achieve the set goals, objectives and vision.
This statement was made by Samdech President Hun Manet on the occasion of presiding over the inauguration ceremony of the achievement and closing of the training course at the National Defense University this morning, April 19, 2024.
"In a context where the world is evolving and impacting Cambodia, the understanding and capacity building of our officers, especially the strategic officers in charge of planning, "It's not just a battle plan, even an international relations plan, a logistics plan, it has to interact directly with other countries, so it needs to understand what to do or what not to do."
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet advised to perform good duties, be disciplined, set an example for the people, respect the state law, all general rules and regulations, prevent and eliminate the production, trafficking and use of drugs in the military. Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
Samdech stressed that in carrying out military duties at all levels of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, it is necessary to implement and adhere to the "mirror, bathe, scrub, treat and operate" approach. Therefore, commanders at all levels must take measures to assign, disseminate, manage and listen to the soldiers' minds in order to make timely adjustments.
In order to ensure the successful completion of the above tasks, Samdech has set out some basic recommendations for implementation, including:
1. Continue to carry out in-depth reforms in all areas of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, from the leadership to the unit to achieve transparency and accountability in the spirit of unity and responsibility.
3. Reform of the organizational structure of the unit must follow the principle of "function inequality, role, duty" of the unit in order to eliminate the "overlap" to achieve each step strictly. As for the number of troops of the unit, the problem of construction sites of the units must be at an appropriate level.
A. Thoroughly study the existing law on military service and the relevant legal documents, and consider the full amendment to propose amendments and additions to the relevant legal documents necessary to implement the law on military service step by step. In accordance with the situation and defense duties in the coming years.
B. In the recruitment and promotion work, the principle of "meritocracy" must be applied in accordance with the position and the general statute for the soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, and must pass the evaluation of the council and the evaluation committee of the unit according to the hierarchy.
C. Priority should be given to local training, with the exception of advanced technical skills training, which relies on overseas training to train young officers to lead, command, and manage young officers to take turns leading and managing units. The deployment of military personnel in military academies must adhere to the principle of selection of military qualifications for each course in accordance with the principles of the Ministry of National Defense.
4. For training and training on human resource development training, that is, the nursery for young officers who will become officers, problem leaders and managers at all levels of the unit:
B. At the same time, the core tasks must be closely coordinated to turn the school into a center for the study, research, and construction of all military documents in all disciplines, including technology, military science, economic, political, military, and psychological education.
C. Must create conditions for each other and cooperate to quote from the performance of their duties, build important indicators necessary to serve in the field of defense and exchange information necessary for research and experimentation for Basis for strategic planning.
D. To study and learn from the experiences of wars in countries, both past and present, with the grasp of practical equipments in line with the latest developments in the field of military technology.
E. Pay more attention to the training and management of human resources, try to study, research, continue to develop their skills constantly to strengthen, expand knowledge, keep up with the development of military technology in the context of the digital technology revolution (Digital) Universe.
F. Take care to strengthen the infrastructure of the existing schools and training centers in accordance with the standards and goals of each profession, as well as modern training equipment as possible.
G. In addition to strengthening the training system in the schools of the Ministry of National Defense, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, officers at all levels must pay more attention to training on the field by the unit according to each specialty in order to manage the army, equipment and increase capacity. Troops.
5. Continue to maintain good cooperative relations with foreign partners as well as friendly countries to exchange experiences, including providing both spiritual and material support to our field of training, based on the spirit of protecting the best interests of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in line with the "Reform" approach. In increasing external friends in the spirit of independence.
6. Education, psychology, information and policy are indispensable in building the patriotic conscience to achieve the task of national defense, which is the main quality of every officer.
7. For the reform of all types of equipment for all types of professional troops, while filling the quantity according to the equipment framework, "quality must be a priority". In the past, the Royal Government and the Ministry of National Defense have tried to find and create sources by adding more modern weapons to respond to the request of national defense duties and will continue to work step by step.
9. Be always ready to fulfill the duties of the Royal Government in all circumstances, pay attention to prepare all forces, means, materials to participate in rescuing people in the event of an accident, with a proactive and cooperative spirit. In close coordination with local authorities and relevant ministries and institutions.
Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet shares some ideas to strengthen the capacity of Cambodian officers (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet shares some ideas to the National Defense University to strengthen research and expand the capacity of the army, especially officers Respond to the latest technologies of the world war.
Samdech Maniphat Hun Manet's ideas were made at the inauguration ceremony of the co-educational building, dormitory building and canteen building at the National Defense University, together with the closing ceremony of the training course and training in 2023 and the opening of the course for 2024 on the morning of the 19th This April 2024.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that in the context of the evolving world, especially the impact on our country, the understanding and capacity building of officers, especially strategic officers in charge of planning, play a greater role. More importantly, in the future, the National Defense University will train not only at the military strategy level, but also at the national defense and security policy, which can be open to senior officials from various institutions to attend.
"Digital information is now and in the future, we do not need to investigate armed infantry anymore, send a team of detectives into the deep forest, it is difficult to lift the drone up a little to see 5 to 10 kilometers inside," he said. " Samdech further explained that the analysis of the current battle shells using only a remote computer can also shoot accurately, at the same time, the drone has a standard GPS system that is more modern than before.
Samdech added, "Of course, we can not abandon the basic knowledge skills, can not take a calculator and stop learning to add numbers, the foundation is the same, but we also do not abandon the use of technology, so the Faculty of Technology, Faculty of Information Technology "It plays an important role in adding more technology to help with research."
He urged the National Defense University to strengthen the qualifications of the Cambodian military at all levels and expand the military's ability to conduct military research. Samdech also mentioned that the university also needs to build documents for further study.
Ministry of Labor collects input from international organizations to prepare community nurseries for workers to international standards
At the meeting held at the Ministry of Labor, experts from the World Child and Development and World Bank (WBB) presented procedures for building community nurseries for workers, surveying workers and collaboration and Discuss with employers to build community nurseries and provide targeted benefits.
After watching the presentation, Mr. Heng Sour praised the sharing of the presentation of the community nursery for garment factory workers by the World Organization for Children and Development and the World Bank, which is an important input on the future establishment of community nurseries. .
In this regard, the Minister pointed out that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the relevant ministries have set out the Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for the establishment of community nurseries, in which the Ministry of Labor has already discussed with the employers of some factories. Regarding the support for the establishment of this community nursery.
He also highlighted that the establishment of a community nursery for workers is one of the ten recommendations of the Prime Minister Hun Manet, which was submitted to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on August 29, 2023. Go here.
The United States has raised concerns over its plans to attack Rafah with Israel and Iran.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Senior US officials raised concerns with their Israeli counterparts on Thursday over plans for an Israeli military operation in the southern Gaza town of Rafah and discussed attacks by the United States. Iran's drones and missiles. This is according to the release by Reuters on Friday, April 19, 2024.
The talks followed a similar meeting on April 1, which ended in a far-reaching difference in their role over the plan for Rafah. US officials told Israel during the initial talks that their plans were lacking in evacuation and protection of the more than one million Palestinian civilians living there.
