Eleven people experience nausea, diarrhea and fatigue at the same time in Sambo district, Kratie province, doctors are testing the cause
(Kratie): At least 11 people suffered from nausea, diarrhea and fatigue at the same time and were sent to Sambo District Referral Hospital in Kratie Province while doctors were testing samples. The exact cause, whether caused by food poisoning (suspected noodles) or from other causes.
The 11 people with the same symptoms live in Tonsong Tluak village, Kampong Cham commune, Sambo district, Kratie province, while this incident happened on the night of April 18, 2024.
Sources from the villagers said that the villagers bought noodles sold in the village to eat yesterday (April 15) and after eating the noodles for a few hours suddenly had nausea and diarrhea. Fatigue was sent to the local health center, but due to nausea, diarrhea, fatigue, up to 11 people were sent to Sambo District Referral Hospital last night. .
Dr. Phat Tola, director of Sambo District Referral Hospital, said that this morning their condition had improved, but it was not yet known if it was a case of poisoning, pending the outcome. Test a sample of a team of doctors first.
"The reason they were sent there was nausea and diarrhea, which could be due to the hot weather, so we can not conclude from the actual case yet, wait for the results," he said. However, now they seem to be back to normal.
