The Cambodian government has decided that the Ministry of Environment will hold an exhibition and promote seedlings under the theme "Green Sprouts" from July 10.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of the Ministry of Environment, said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to organize the Ministry of Environment to organize exhibitions and seedlings under the theme "Green Sprouts" from July 10, 2024. Office of the Ministry of Environment for the display and distribution of seedlings to people to plant in homes, schools, pagodas, public places and private places for free.
This statement was made by Dr. Eang Sophalleth on the occasion of chairing a meeting with leaders and government officials at the Ministry of Environment on Thursday afternoon, April 18, 2024.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth confirmed that the Ministry of Environment, through all provincial and municipal Departments of Environment, has already planted all kinds of seedlings ready to distribute to people to plant more than 1 million trees, and HE himself will provide more than 30 palm seedlings. Tens of thousands more for the Cambodian Green Campaign, which aims to plant at least 1 million seedlings from 2024.
(Koh Kong): Due to the lack of clean water for the people living on the island, which lacks clean water for household use in the dry season, Kirisakor district authorities have sought to provide clean water to the people to have clean water to use in the dry season. Extremely hot and lack of clean water.
Mr. Toun Ooty, Deputy Governor of Kirisakor District, said that at Koh Sdach, Koh Sdach Commune, Kirisar District, in the dry season, the people on the island always have a shortage of clean water to use every year, his people are very careful. In the dry season, he stockpiled water for use, but it was not enough for the family.
Mr. Toun Ooty continued that seeing the lack of clean water for the people to use, the authorities sought to intervene and meet with Mr. So Virak's company to ask him to facilitate the provision of clean water to the people on the island. This king has clean water for the household.
He said that with the generosity of Mr. So Virak decided to provide clean water to people to transport water at the stop of the water as needed without paying. The tycoon decided to set up a water supply system to connect the people's homes to have clean water to use soon.
The deputy district governor said that after the company connects the water supply to the house, the company will charge 4,000 riel per square kilometer, which is a reasonable price.
NEC: Anonymous Complaints Are Not Considered Legal and Must Not Be Resolved
Mr. Heng Sileng made this statement when he chaired a meeting with stakeholders on the preparation of the first voter list, the posting of the first voter list, the complaint or objection and the settlement of complaints on the list. The first election, the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council, 4th Mandate 2024, this morning, April 19, 2024.
The senior NEC official said that the posting of the initial voter list was to serve the purpose of reviewing corrections through complaints or objections related to the initial voter list, with due process and procedures. The stages of the complaint are as follows:
* Complaints or objections
Complaints: Complaints may be made about the loss of a voter's name or name on the voter list, but inaccurate or inaccurate records or names on the voter list of other municipalities, districts or Khans.
Complaints: Objections can be made to any person whose name is on the initial voter list, a person who does not have the right to vote, who is not a member of the Commune / Sangkat Council in a position within the framework of the city. Each district and case where the voter has more than one name on the voter list.
Filing, Receiving and Resolving Complaints Any person or representative has the right to file a complaint and / or object in writing according to the complaint (T. 1202) related to the initial voter list according to the hierarchy to the BEC. And the NEC according to the procedure and time of filing and receiving the complaint. The complaint must state the following necessary information:
First, the name and address of the complainant or representative - Second: The subject of the complaint and respect for the deadline for filing a complaint no later than 5 days after the date of the first voter list posting.
Mr. Heng Sileng added that complaints or objections related to the initial voter list must be submitted to the NEC within five days after the first voter list is posted. The last day to receive complaints is April 25, 2024. After receiving the complaint, the CCC shall resolve it within 3 days.
