(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Friday, April 19, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, presided over the inauguration ceremony of a co-educational building. And the canteen building at the National Defense University. Along with the inauguration of the buildings, there will also be the closing of training courses and training in 2023 and the opening of courses for 2024.
The co-educational building, the dormitory building, and the canteen building were officially donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. Construction began on October 4, 2020 and was completed on the 5th. June 2023.
The National Defense University is a higher education institution of the Ministry of National Defense that studies security situation analysis, assesses threats to national security, defense policy, border protection, national security, military reform, participation in national defense, and security. International arena for the study of military sciences, social sciences, real sciences and foreign languages for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
The National Defense University is responsible for training and retraining senior officers, officers, professional officers and specialized officers to become competent and qualified officers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in researching, analyzing and evaluating the implementation of measures. Strategy, defense policy, and performance of duties as an officer, commander, and chief of staff.
In April 1997, Samdech Techo Hun Sen changed the name of the above school to the Military Academy of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. In 2001, it was renamed the Cambodian Military Institute. In November 2006, the institute was renamed and upgraded to a "National Defense University" under the Ministry of National Defense.
From 2019 to 2023, the National Defense University trained and trained a total of 75 courses of 4,929 students of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and foreign military students.
Separately, the 2023 course, the National Defense University has trained and trained 18 courses with 1,420 students, including the 2023 end of the 2023 course with 959 students and continue the course in 2024 6 courses with 491 students. There are 93 foreign military students from 54 countries: Vietnam, 20 from Laos, 8 from Thailand and 11 from Myanmar.
In the 2024 academic year, the National Defense University will run 17 courses. There are 11 new courses with 613 students and 6 follow-up courses with 491 students with a total of 1,104 national and international students.
