"Village Top League" football match is a new formula for rural rehabilitation and development of Guizhou Province, China
BEIJING: After China announced that the country's poor will be lifted out of poverty by the end of 2020, the Chinese government has launched a policy of rural rehabilitation and development aimed at strengthening poverty alleviation and prevention achievements. Do not let the poor go back to poverty.
The administrations of regions across China, especially the poorest areas, have put in place policies that suit the conditions in their respective regions to achieve rural rehabilitation and development through job opportunities and technical training. Agriculture to farmers to increase their income.
Guizhou is a mountainous province in southwestern China, the center of the mainland and one of the poorest areas in China. Through years of hard work, finally in late 2020, the Guizhou Provincial Administration announced that the last nine districts, the poorest districts, were lifted out of poverty, which means the country's poverty alleviation work. China has achieved its plan.
A Chinese saying goes, "Building achievements is not easy, and maintaining achievements is even more difficult." Obviously, although poverty alleviation work in various parts of China has been achieved, maintaining and strengthening it is a big test.
Why is the "Village Top League" so popular? The first is due to the strong support from the villagers. The tournament not only provides a platform for villagers who love football to participate in the tournament, but also provides a unique visual food for fans to visit and relax after work and Studies as well.
The second is the highlight of ethnic cultures and traditions. Guizhou is a province of many ethnic groups in China. Through the "Village League", ethnic minorities show off their beautiful culture and traditions, especially their unique and intangible cultural heritage, which attracts national and international tourists. .
The popularity of the "Village Top League" in Rongjiang County, Guizhou Province has also attracted the attention of the arts. The Hong Kong football artists' team, which is made up of famous Hong Kong stars, went to play a friendly match there, which helped to promote the competition as well as to promote tourism as well as local culture and traditions. .
