The United States has vetoed a draft resolution recommending that all 193 members of the UN General Assembly recognize the Palestinian state as a full member of the UN. In Thursday's Security Council elections, Britain and Switzerland voted against, while 12 other Security Council members voted in favor.
Palestine is currently a United Nations observer state after receiving this status from the UN General Assembly in 2012. Requests for full membership in the UN must be approved by the Security Council and, at least by a two-thirds majority of the UN General Assembly.
