(Phnom Penh): A woman died suddenly in a pool of blood in her home because another man, armed with a machete, stabbed her several times, but it is not yet known what caused the dispute. The killer stabbed the victim to death but did not die. He was seriously injured and was taken to Techo Santepheap Hospital for emergency treatment.
This incident happened on the afternoon of April 18, 2024, at house number 31, street 36, Borey Piphop Thmey, Chhouk Va 2, Tek Panho village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The victim, 24-year-old Meas Leakena, was married to 37-year-old Hua Sin, a Chinese national who works for a stone grinding company in Kampong Speu province. The victim and her husband stayed in the house and had two sons in the family.
The killer, Lim Kineth, 25, of Chak Chrouk village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey, was taken to hospital for emergency treatment. No source has yet confirmed the cause of the stabbing, and it is unknown at this time what he did to cause the killings.
According to sources, at the time of the incident, while the victim was on the porch of the house in front, the suspect walked in and stabbed her several times, causing her to die immediately in a pool of blood. The assailant then did not escape, then committed suicide by slaying the victim, causing her to fall asleep next to the victim's body, but did not die, but suffered serious injuries.
