The idea of Khmer civilization experts after seeing that bokator training in private schools is too expensive, making it impossible to include in the curriculum. At the same time, this martial art is not yet taught in public schools.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Rath Sandab suggested that if the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, together with the Cambodian Bokator Federation, facilitates the training of bokator in the field of national martial arts education will grow. Nationwide as it was inscribed on the UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list on November 29, 2022.
With the attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the efforts of the community of teachers, bokator students, all Cambodian bokator is preserved, valued and widely disseminated in the country and on the international stage.
