China has stepped up measures to strengthen its fragile real estate sector, including allowing state-owned banks to lend to qualified real estate projects after cracking down on debt-ridden real estate developers. Leads to liquidity crisis.
New construction starts fell 27.8 percent in the first quarter from a year earlier after falling 29.7 percent in the first two months of the year.
