IMF forecasts another year of steady but steady global economic growth
WASHINGTON: The International Monetary Fund (IMF) said on Tuesday that the global economy will experience another year of slow but steady growth. According to Reuters.
The IMF has forecast that the world's real gross domestic product (GDP) will grow by 3.2 percent for 2024 and 2025, the same rate as in 2023. The 2024 forecast is up 0.1 percentage point from the January World Economic Outlook report, largely due to the US US growth forecast.
Many countries are also showing less impact from the Kovid-19 pandemic and the relief of the cost crisis, with economic output returning to pre-existing levels, the IMF said in a report. Outbreaks appear to be exacerbated during pre-existing conditions.
