* New Year History
It is said that at the beginning of the story, there was a rich man who had a son named Dhammabal Komar, who was a highly educated man who learned the Trinity Veda at the age of seven. The rich man built a temple for the children of Dhammapala near a big tree on the river bank, which is home to birds. Dhammapala Komar knows the language of all birds and can be a priest performing various blessings for all people.
The children's dhamma teacher asked for a seven-day delay to think of a parable. Six days later, the child monk still did not think and realized that this morning he would be killed by Judge Bill Mahapram for sure. Therefore, it is better to run and hide to die by oneself. Only then did the children go down from the temple and hide under a pair of palm trees. On the palm tree, there is a male eagle nesting.
* New Year Tradition
Day 2: Children give clothes, food, money to the rich, parents, grandparents and so on. Sometimes they give alms to servants or the poor. In the afternoon, they went to the sand dunes again and prayed for the sand dunes, which were supposed to be like the Cholamni stupa, and summoned the monks of the stupa to send blessings to the souls of the dead.
* Khmer New Year celebration
At the appointed time, the angels of the new year come down to bless and bless them so that they can have peace throughout the year. On the second day of the Khmer New Year, which is called the New Year, people go to the pagoda to bring food, cakes and fruits to the monks. In addition, there are also traditional games such as throwing boxes, throwing beads, hiding towels, and singing and dancing traditional songs at pagodas and other areas in Cambodia.
The third day is the end of the New Year, called the New Year. On that day, a ceremony to draw water from the Buddha statues at the pagoda to ask for peace is also held, and it is also the last day of the celebration of the Khmer New Year. Do not let happy days be miserable for your driving! 8 killed, 28 injured in road accidents nationwide
