Business Awareness: Women Entrepreneurs Encourage Increased Production of Domestic Raw Materials Exported to UAE Market After Cambodia-UAE Agreement Implemented
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Keo Mom, owner of Lily Crispy Company, said that the implementation of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates is to open new markets for Cambodian products, therefore she encourages industry owners Increase production quality and quantity to capture new markets.
Ms. Keo Mom pointed out that this is a good opportunity for Cambodian producers as well as Lily Crispy Company to capture this market for future exports, as she wants to show that Lily Crispy Products uses materials. Phkar Romduol rice plant, the number one type of rice in the world.
At the same time, she encouraged other industry owners to strive to produce more goods in order to be more competitive in the market.
"Currently, we see that his local production has the ability to produce products that use Cambodian raw materials are delicious, but his production is still limited, making high costs difficult to compete in the market," she said.
Under the Cambodia-UAE agreement, Cambodia will receive about 97.8% of the total tariff line, or 7,678 tariff lines. The main commodities that Cambodia gets in the market are almost all commodities, including agricultural commodities such as rice, cashews, vegetables, fruits, bananas, mangoes, corn, peppers, durians, rice cakes, fruit desserts and so on.
Industrial goods include: bicycles, electronic components, electric vehicles and textiles, including travel bags, footwear, clothing, except for prohibited goods and specialty goods, which are mostly alcohol and pork.
Cambodia will provide the market with about 91.62% of the total tax line or equal to 10,457 tax lines. The main products that Cambodia offers in the market include: plastics, rubber, some crude oil products, paper, steel and steel, electrical equipment, vehicles for transporting goods, tractors, etc.
