(Siem Reap): Speech by Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the 19th Royal Government and Private Sector Forum on November 13, 2023, which reflects the "Pentagon Strategy" Phase 1, Angle 2 The fourth and fifth points are "Ensuring sustainable social, economic development and building resilience to climate change" by declaring "Phnom Kulen" National Park in Siem Reap as a nature tourism destination.
Separately, Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, on December 28, 2023, instructed the General Department of Local Communities to lead the development of eco-tourism corridor in "Phnom Kulen" National Park through the production of videos and other documents to promote the potential. Natural resources, culture, history and action plan for joint development in "Phnom Kulen" National Park.
In 2004, the Ministry of Environment, Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Siem Reap Provincial Administration updated the border of the National Park, leaving 37,373 hectares of land.
For the ecotourism community development plan, the Minister of Environment has launched a strategic plan to develop green space goals in protected areas in order to serve the interests and improve the sustainable livelihoods of local communities based on the principles The three main ones are as follows:
* First, all development projects in the local community need to serve the interests and improve the livelihood of the community, the development project must be approved by the community, with harmony between the project and the community, at the same time must teach the community to be independent. Own
* Second: All development projects must participate in the protection of protected areas and local communities, in which the project owner must work with the community to prevent the encroachment on state land (protected area land) absolutely, especially to protect. Illegal logging and natural resource crime, as well as the risk of wildfires
And 3: Implement the "clean" greenery in protected areas by maintaining cleanliness in the air, on the ground and in the water, especially the cleanliness that comes from the heart of the community. The base that this beauty will share to the surrounding environment, including tourists visiting the protected area.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth will organize the first Cambodian green recreation destination, which is a Khmer style, a camp (tent) equipped with solar energy (solar lights) in the community of protected areas with tourism potential in the "Phnom Kulen" National Park. Give to the community to charge for tourism services by applying the principle of "cleanliness" at a reasonable price to tourists.
