The children's dhamma teacher asked for a seven-day delay to think of a parable. Six days later, the child monk still did not think and realized that this morning he would be killed by Judge Bill Mahapram for sure. Therefore, it is better to run and hide and die for oneself. Only then did the children go down from the temple and hide under a pair of palm trees. On the palm tree, there is a male eagle nesting.
At the appointed time, the angels of the new year come down to bless and bless them so that they can have peace throughout the year. On the second day of the Khmer New Year, which is called the day of the festival, people go to the pagoda to bring food, cakes and fruits to the monks. In addition, there are also traditional games such as throwing boxes, throwing beads, hiding towels, and singing and dancing traditional songs at pagodas and other areas in Cambodia.
The third day is the end of the New Year, called the New Year. On that day, a ceremony to draw water from the Buddha statues at the pagoda to ask for peace is also held, and it is also the last day of the celebration of the Khmer New Year.
