(Phnom Penh): In the first three months of 2024, there were 3,048 registered enterprises and establishments with a total labor force of 140,524 people. This is according to the message of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia on April 12, 2024, which was sent to the Cambodian people on the occasion of the traditional New Year.
Through this message, His Excellency Hun Manet stated that in the first three months of 2024, the industrial sector had 3,048 registered enterprises and establishments, which absorbed a total of 140,524 workers, while in 2023 there were enterprises. Registration increased to 43,751, employing a total of 1.8 million people nationwide.
According to the President, the minimum wage of textile, garment, footwear and travel and bag manufacturers has been raised to US $ 204, plus other mandatory benefits, as well as continued benefits. Implementation of the Royal Government's social protection policy.
In this message, Samdech Dhipatey also highlighted the progress of the agricultural sector. According to Samdech, in the first three months of 2024, Cambodia exported a total of 4,596,442 tons of agricultural products, including more than 166,000 tons of rice, 1,555,025 tons of rice and 2,874 non-rice agricultural products. 966 tons to destinations in 65 countries.
At the same time, he said that in 2023, the production of wet and dry season rice will reach more than 12.49 million tons, which we estimate has a surplus of nearly 7 million tons of rice, equivalent to 4.5 million tons of rice. Serve for export. Last year, Cambodia exported a total of 8,449,414 tons of agricultural products, of which Angkor produced more than 664 thousand tons, 2,730,825 tons of rice and 5,062,266 tons of non-rice agricultural products to 78 countries.
Ministry of Labor calls on customers and the public to understand and tolerate the provision of services by workers and business owners during the traditional New Year (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on the 12th This April 2024 issued an appeal to customers and the public to understand and tolerate the services provided by workers and business owners during the traditional New Year.
As the traditional New Year approaches, most of the workers, business owners and people from all over the country are traveling to their hometowns to reunite with their families and celebrate various religious and cultural events. Travel to resorts, entertainment centers, restaurants, hotels and guesthouses with fun under the cool shade of peace.
At the same time, some workers who work in resorts, entertainment centers, restaurants, hotels and guesthouses will be doubly busy in providing services to customers and national and international tourists.
In this regard, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training would like to appeal to the people, workers and the public who have taken a break and travel or to receive services at resorts, entertainment centers, restaurants, hotels and guesthouses, please have understanding and tolerance for workers. Employees, service providers and business owners if there are any delays or shortages during this period.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training would like to express its sincere appreciation and appreciation for the professional conscience of all service workers who dedicate their personal time to fulfill their essential and universal duties. Persistently on this occasion.
At the same time, on behalf of the workers, business owners and citizens, the Ministry would like to thank the authorities at all levels, the Armed Forces of all kinds and the private security staff for dedicating their personal time to maintaining social security during the strike. This break is to provide opportunities for workers, business owners and people to enjoy family reunions and travel safely.
