Siem Reap Provincial Authority Holds a Prayer Ceremony for Happiness in Siem Reap Sankranti Event
(Siem Reap): Siem Reap Provincial Authority on April 12, 2024 organized a prayer ceremony for happiness in the event "Siem Reap Sankrant" according to the traditions and religious beliefs of the people of Cambodia before the New Year. This important ceremony took place at the Royal Palace Park in Siem Reap.
The prayer ceremony was also attended by Mr. An Khun, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Prak Sophoan, Provincial Governor, as well as members of the Provincial Council, APSARA Authority, leaders of departments, units, municipal authorities and many government officials.
Religious programs to worship the sacred objects of the world, including the temples of Angkor Wat and ancient temples, the heritage of Khmer ancestral architecture, there are kings, grandmothers, gods, kings, bananas, princes, great kings, the back of the mountain Kulen to ask for happiness Run the "Siem Reap Sankranti 2024" event successfully, the freedom and happiness according to the wishes of the Cambodian people as well as national and international guests.
According to the announcement of the call of the Acharya, who blessed the ceremony on that occasion, the prayer for happiness is a ceremony that is organized in a purely Brahminical way. Through this celebration, the traditional culture of the Cambodian people is deeply embedded in the faith and society.
The prayer ceremony, as well as the Krong Pali ceremony, is a ritual based on the spiritual beliefs of the Cambodian people, who believe that in this world, the powerful who have passed away actually use their souls in care. Preserve the next generation and take responsibility with the power to support the children who do only good deeds and have a patriotic conscience, love to protect the homeland, the ancestral heritage truly.
The celebration also shows the wide hearts of the Cambodian people, who have maintained the traditional beliefs of their nation since the glorious period of the Angkorian Empire, the period of the unification of the mighty Khmer kings. Between Brahmanism and the influx of Buddhism to Cambodia.
The Cambodian people are very proud that through the "Siem Reap Sankranti" event, many religious ceremonies related to Hinduism and other ceremonies, such as the Sand Hill Ceremony, are held in the traditional Buddhist way. And these are proofs that the next generation of Cambodians will continue to respect the culture, traditions, beliefs and religion most firmly.
