Kampong Cham Provincial Court and Prosecutor's Office issued a press release regarding the actions of candlelight party activists on cases of forgery of public documents and use of forged documents in Stung Trang district
(Kampong Cham): The Kampong Cham Provincial Court and Prosecutor's Office have issued a press release regarding the actions of candlelight party activists in cases of forgery of public documents and use of forged documents in Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province.
According to the press release, Heang Soda, a 40-year-old female resident of Samrong village, O'Mlou commune, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province, filed a complaint on the 4th of this month. April 2024 to the Kampong Cham Provincial Police on the activities of San Soeung, male, and his accomplices in connection with the forgery of fingerprints and his name as the ninth reserve candidate of Stung Trang District Council.
After completing the search and investigation, the Judicial Police Officer of Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner arrested (1) San Soeung, male, (2) Srey Mean, male, and (3) Yin Pheap, male, with clues related to Forgery of public documents and use of forged documents from February 17 to March 21, 2024 in Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province.
After questioning the three suspects and examining the relevant documents, including the forensic documents on the fingerprints, the Kampong Cham Provincial Prosecutor's Office decided to charge the three suspects with "fraud." Public documents and use of forged documents ”in accordance with Articles 626, 628 and 629 of the Penal Code and send the case to the Investigating Judge of Kampong Cham Provincial Court for further legal proceedings.
After receiving the case, hearing the accused and examining the evidence, the investigating judge decided to detain the three accused in order to continue the investigation in accordance with the law.
The spokesperson of the Kampong Cham Provincial Court and Prosecutor would also like to emphasize that the above case is a fact of pure criminal offenses as stated in Articles 626, 628 and 629 of the Penal Code.
