(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chhim Chamnan, President of the Cambodian Road Passenger Transport Association, said that currently in Phnom Penh, there are more than 100 companies transporting passengers are not legally registered, and companies are registered legally. Only about 20 companies, the same for companies that do not have the right law, always take the transport service from the people more expensive than legal companies.
Dr. Chhim Chamnan said, "According to the findings of the Ministry, it is confirmed that in Phnom Penh, there are about 100 different passenger transport companies in different locations are not properly registered from there, while companies that are legal and registered. There are only about 20 companies. ”
Dr. stated that legal companies and companies do not have the law, shipping costs are different. For legal companies, the shipping cost from Phnom Penh to Siem Reap is between 45,000 Riel, a little more or less, but for illegal companies, the shipping cost is between 60,000 Riel.
Dr. continued that the high cost of illegal transport companies because they have to share the money sold, these factors make the illegal companies more and can stand for a long time.
Dr. Chhim Chamnan added that most of the people who use illegal transport companies are from the provinces who do not have a clear understanding of transport companies and do not know which companies are legal and which companies are illegal. For others, understanding and using a company with the right rules.
Dr. stated that why use a legal transport company? People pay 45,000 Riel or 50,000 Riel, passengers will get many benefits such as: regular travel, insurance, good service, comfortable car, provide road safety, professional driver Right, do not make any other income by placing plastic chairs on the street.
Dr. added that for companies that are not properly registered, do not provide services or ensure the safety of customers like legal transport companies.
