(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ouk Savuth, Attorney General of the Court of Appeal, decided to appeal to the Court of Appeal to review the decision of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court regarding the case of nearly 800 kilograms of drugs after the release of five Taiwanese nationals.
Please be informed that according to the law, the General Court of Appeal has 3 months to appeal the decision of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court if it finds that this decision is suspicious or there are no irregularities.
Please be informed that on April 1, 2024, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court issued a press release on the sentencing of two Taiwanese nationals to 20 years in prison for trafficking nearly 800 kilograms of drugs, while five Taiwanese nationals Others were released after serving a period of imprisonment on the grounds that they were not involved in the crime.
