Foreign Minister meets with Chinese Ambassador to ASEAN to exchange views on regional and international issues of common interest and concern
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, met with Ms. HOU Yanqi, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to ASEAN on April 1, 2024.
Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chendasophea emphasized the importance of the ASEAN Way - consultations and consensus-based decisions enshrined in the ASEAN Charter, emphasizing the uniqueness of ASEAN and maintaining a neutral and inclusive environment. ASEAN unity in ASEAN relations with its partners. The Deputy Prime Minister thanked China for its strong support for the ASEAN community-building efforts.
The Ambassador praised Cambodia's active role in building the ASEAN Community and acknowledged ASEAN's importance in maintaining peace, security, stability and promoting growth in the region, and reaffirmed China's strong support and respect for ASEAN Centralism and Unity
The Ambassador underscored China's strong commitment to quality cooperation with Cambodia under the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI).
The Deputy Prime Minister and the Ambassador also exchanged views on regional and international issues of common interest and concern, including Mekong-Lanchang cooperation.
