Two Filipino navy pilots killed in helicopter crash
The Philippine Navy said in a statement that a Robinson R22 helicopter carrying two officers on board was forced to make an emergency landing near a market south of Manila. The two pilots were rushed to hospital but died of their injuries. The cause of the crash was not immediately known, but an investigation is under way.
The Philippines has been involved in several helicopter and military plane crashes. In January 2023, for example, two Philippine military pilots were killed when their fighter jet crashed during flight training. In 2021, a military plane crashed, killing 53 people, making it the worst military plane crash in nearly three decades.
