Samdech Thiptey Hun Manet issued a decision to determine the principles of management and exploitation of sand resources by assigning the Ministry of Mines to issue licenses and take full responsibility for all types of sand exploitation.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has issued a decision to determine the principles of management and exploitation of sand resources.
According to this decision, the Royal Government has assigned the Ministry of Mines and Energy to issue the license and be fully responsible for all types of sand business from the time of application to the issuance of the license. All licenses of the Ministry of Mines and Energy must be copied to the relevant ministries and institutions.
In addition, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, in collaboration with the Ministry of Mines and Energy, shall designate three (3) sand resource areas based on the results of the following hydrological and hydrological studies:
The Ministry of Environment must conduct an environmental impact assessment with the participation of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, and the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology. Environmental impact assessments shall be conducted in accordance with technical standards and shall determine the maximum duration of service delivery and appropriate service fees.
The sand mining license shall be valid for a period of 2 (two) years and shall not be allowed to issue a temporary license.
The Ministry of Mines and Energy must set up an information sharing mechanism and an emergency response mechanism for the discovery of illegal dredging at the wrong time and in violation of the licenses. Relevant ministries, sub-national administrations and citizens can report anarchic sand dredging to the Ministry of Mines and Energy at any time.
The Sand Resources Management Committee performs its duties to monitor and monitor the exploitation of sand resources. In case of anarchy or improper sand dredging, the Sand Resources Management Committee recommends in its jurisdiction that the Ministry of Mines and Energy take immediate action.
This morning, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet inaugurated Kiri Sour Dairy Farm
The company has worked closely with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and obtained a 300-hectare land concession in Phnom Tamao, Takeo province to establish a farm and facilitate the import of world-renowned dairy cows from 550 Australians by air to Cambodia
Kiri Sour Farm currently has a total of 928 Holstein dairy cows as of February 2024, including locally bred cows that are already adapted to the Cambodian climate. The farm adheres to modern production principles, including rearing, care, feeding and milking to ensure regular animal health.
Kiri Sour Farm is GMP / HACCP certified in response to a modern, high-security, high-yielding yoghurt and butter production chain with livestock and feed production on a single farm.
Khmer Fresh Mill has selected TSNR as the national distribution agent covering all capitals and provinces to ensure fast and efficient distribution of products to the market. After starting trial production in 2021, the farm has built a reputation in the market to become the largest milk supplier in Cambodia.
The Kiri Sour brand is fully recognized by dairy consumers from all walks of life across the country. The company currently has 127 employees and is headquartered in Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, in addition to a team of farm production experts in Phnom Tamao, Takeo province.
Khmer Fresh Mill has partnered with Israel's most renowned technology and equipment suppliers to successfully complete similar projects across Asia, including projects in China and Bangladesh, especially in Vietnam, which helped TH True Milk become A leading company there.
Currently, the farm has the capacity to produce more than 13,000 liters of fresh milk per day and supply about 15% of the market share in Cambodia.
Kiri Sour has become one of the three most popular brands, using marketing agents with specific strategies and skills to develop effective marketing campaigns. In addition, the company also partners with companies with a successful history to bring products to customers effectively.
Kiri Sour now supplies fresh milk and yoghurt products to more than 100 supermarkets, including Lucky Aeon, Macro Chip, Montreux, Superstars, Supermarkets and Marts, a total of nearly 4,000 cafes nationwide.
At the same time, due to the increase in the number of cattle, farms also need to increase the area to grow grass, corn and other animal feed in order to help supply enough animal feed, as well as reduce the cost of raising cattle.
To supplement the daily feed of the cows, the farm has expanded its fodder crops by contracting with 28 families in Trapeang Kronhung commune, Tram Kak district, on an area of more than 15 hectares to supply feed to dairy cows.
Please note that Cambodia currently has four large dairy farms: Kiri Sour Farm, Mo Mu Farm in Russey Trip National Park and Om Farm. As of March 2024, the four farms have 1,176 dairy cows, producing more than 5 million liters of fresh milk per year, or 17 percent of the domestic demand of more than 30 million liters of fresh milk.
