(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, on April 10, 2024, urged private security service providers and private security enterprises to consider applying for a National Social Security Fund card to agencies. Its not yet intended to gain the support of the Royal Government.
On the occasion of presiding over the representative of General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, at the closing ceremony of the 59th Private Security Agency Training Course of the Private Security Management Department, Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi noted that so far, a number of companies, enterprises and establishments Already requested the ID card for its agent, but some have not been completed.
In this regard, the Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police urged the remaining private security agencies, the owners of all companies, enterprises and establishments to apply to their agents for access to health care from the Royal Government. With this ID card, the private security agent, when receiving health services, does not pay for them, and the state pays for them.
