At the same time, he called on the directors of private security service providers and institutions to continue to support the training by sending private security agents to attend the training, and all participants must apply the knowledge gained from this study and continue to expand their knowledge. Smart, creative and highly responsible in fulfilling their role.
According to the report of Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Department of Private Security Management, there are currently 59 private security agency refresher courses with 10,077 private security agent trainees (218 females) and trainees. 243 members of the National Police (20 females).
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey claimed that the training was aimed at meeting the need to increase the capacity to become a skilled and qualified private security agent for participation in the maintenance and protection of stability. Security, safety, order and life of the people, as well as improve the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
In this regard, we observe that the private security agents who have undergone the training in the past have a clear professionalism, good ethics, good behavior, good cooperation and some legal knowledge make the private security sector very supportive. By quality and sustainability.
Please be informed that the private security agent who has received the training of the private security agent is provided with a certificate of education issued by the General Commission of the National Police and a certificate of private security agency issued by the Department of Private Security Management for management and protection.
