This recommendation was made on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting and the work direction for 2024, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on the afternoon of April 10, 2024.
The nine recommendations made by His Excellency Hun Manet include:
First, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology must continue to strengthen institutional governance by building and promoting human capital through the strengthening of technical capacity, the use of modern technology, the encouragement and strengthening of cooperation with all stakeholders to strengthen resource management. Water in rivers and streams, based on the principles of mixed water resources management.
Second, encourage the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to expedite the preparation of procedures and request the approval of sub-decrees on water licenses, sub-decrees on water quality and other regulations necessary to carry out the duties and responsibilities of the Ministry.
Fourth, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and its subordinates must continue to carry out their roles and responsibilities in close cooperation with relevant ministries and institutions and local authorities in all capitals and provinces in the "one-person system" approach to prevent and Reduce natural disasters such as floods and droughts by building quality water infrastructure and improving flood and weather forecasting efficiency.
Fifth, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology must continue to expand the potential of water supply sources through the construction of dams, reservoirs and water distribution systems with quality and reliability based on scientific studies to ensure water supply. Sufficient for the daily use of clean water and for production in all sectors, as well as to help reduce floods and droughts.
Sixth, the National Mekong Committee of Cambodia must continue to strengthen more effective cooperation with ministries and institutions, as well as with the member countries of the Mekong River Commission, dialogue partners and development partners to achieve sustainable development of water resources and Other relevant resources in the Mekong Basin.
Seventh, encourage the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the feasibility of construction and maintenance of water works and with development partners and aid agencies to raise funds to support Management, conservation and development of water resources in Cambodia.
Eighth: In addition to the infrastructure achievements in building water resources, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology must pay more attention to strengthening soft skills and capacity building in weather forecasting, compilation of meteorological and hydrological data. Serve the various sectors to be more accurate.
This statement was made at the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting and the 2024 work direction of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on the afternoon of April 10, 2024.
"Achievements and progress in the field of water resources and meteorology will not be possible if Cambodia does not have complete peace, political stability and social security," he said.
