From January to March, Cambodia's exports reached more than $ 6.26 billion, up 18%, while re-imports amounted to $ 6.23 billion, up 6.4%, respectively. Cambodia's trade volume and international market reached more than 12.49 billion US dollars, an increase of 11.9%.
Cambodia's top exports were garments and clothing accessories worth more than $ 2 billion, fruits and nuts worth more than $ 407 million, machinery and electrical appliances worth more than $ 448 million. More than $ 483 million in footwear and $ 316 million worth of rubber and rubber products, along with other major commodities.
Pen Sovicheat, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, told Fresh News on April 10 that Cambodia's exports outpaced imports as Cambodia produced the necessary commodities to meet consumer demand. Imported is reduced.
He explained that imports were lower than at the beginning of this year because most of Cambodia imported groceries and consumer goods, which were cheaper compared to high-value goods such as construction materials and electronics. And cars.
He noted that while the global economic situation is not good, Cambodians seem to be more frugal and reduce their spending on luxury goods and electronics. At the same time, due to the decrease in construction activities, the import of goods such as construction materials has also been reduced.
