* President Hun Manet stated that the work of protecting the Tonle Sap Lake conservation land must continue without backing down.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology must continue to expand the potential of water supply sources through the construction of dams, reservoirs and water distribution systems with quality and reliability based on scientific studies to ensure Adequate water supply for daily water use and for production in all sectors, as well as to help reduce floods and droughts.
* Samdech Hun Manet encourages the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the feasibility of funding for the construction and maintenance of water works and with development partners and donors to raise funds to support Management, conservation and development of water resources in Cambodia.
* Samdech Hun Manet requested the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to continue to expand the potential of water supply sources through the construction of dams, reservoirs and water distribution systems with quality and reliability based on scientific studies to ensure Adequate water supply for daily water use and for production in all sectors, as well as to help reduce floods and droughts.
