This afternoon, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet closed the meeting of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Wednesday, April 10, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, will preside over the closing ceremony of the General Assembly. Work in 2023 and raise work direction in 2024.
The water resources sector is an indispensable sector in contributing to improving people's lives, reducing poverty and national economic growth. In this sense, under the high leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia has taken care of and considered the water resources sector as one of the four priority areas: people, water, electricity and roads.
The Royal Government of Cambodia clearly understands the importance of enhancing the management, conservation and development of water resources and meteorology in a highly efficient and sustainable manner. Due to this necessity, the Royal Government of Cambodia in the second mandate decided to establish the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology according to the Royal Kram dated 23 June 1999.
The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has consistently carried out its role and responsibilities in implementing water resources management policies through the rehabilitation, repair and construction of small, medium and large irrigation systems to transform Cambodia into a water security country. Both quantity and quality contribute to improving people's livelihoods, reducing poverty and developing the national economy.
In order to promote the efficiency and quality of work even better, on April 9, 2024, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, together with the National Committee of the Mekong River of Cambodia and the Tonle Sap Authority, held a meeting to review the work in 2023 and set work directions. 2024. The two-day conference aims to review the results of the work achieved and review the challenges to put forward solutions and formulate action plans for implementation in 2024.
The conference was opened and chaired by Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology in the 7th legislature. The conference was also attended by the leadership of civil servants under the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology throughout the capital-province, officials of the National Mekong River Commission of Cambodia and Tonle Sap Authority, representatives of the capital-provincial governors and representatives of relevant ministries.
Through this conference, professional officers made presentations on the achievements of their competencies and also highlighted the challenges encountered.
At the opening ceremony of the conference, Mr. Tho Chetha thanked the leaders and civil servants under the supervision of all ministries for their joint efforts with strong will to perform their duties responsibly until the work should be achieved. Lots of fun in 2023.
At the opening ceremony, the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology also presented many achievements in 2023, especially the construction of irrigation systems.
The following are the achievements of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology achieved in 2023:
+ Results of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology: 1: Accelerate the governance reform to strengthen institutional governance, human resource management and finance to improve the efficiency of the Ministry by achieving 99% of total annual loans.
2. Strengthen policies, strategic plans and legal documents to ensure the sustainable management, conservation and development of water resources and the environment in order to ensure water security for the people of Cambodia.
To date, the Ministry has increased the total irrigation capacity of 1943,992 hectares nationwide, an increase of 32,123 hectares, with a total population of 29,800 families, equivalent to 127 895 people.
4: In order to reduce the threat of floods, the Ministry has repaired 6,820 meters of flood protection dams, dredged canals, protected riverbanks, constructed dams to prevent salt water, and especially the implementation of the drainage and diversion system project. Geography: Phnom Penh and Kandal provinces.
5: In order to prevent and reduce the risk caused by floods and weather, the Ministry monitors and collects data on the water level of the Mekong, Tonle Sap - Tonle Bassac and some major tributaries and forecasts the daily water level at Rainy season and weekly during the dry season, and daily weather forecasts and emergency alerts for short, medium and long term climate change.
7: Continue to pay attention to building gender equality in contributing to the development and management of water resources and set up mechanisms for creating opportunities for women civil servants who are capable of gaining decision-making roles at both the national and national levels. Sub-national.
Along with the results achieved above, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology also faces a number of challenges that require participation. Those challenges include:
1. Annual public investment for water resources management and development and meteorological forecasting, funding for irrigation restoration and construction, and riverbank protection have not yet fully met actual needs. .
2. Climate change has led to increased flooding and frequent droughts, which have affected water infrastructure, hydrological systems, water resources and water demand.
3. Inter-sectoral multi-sectoral water resources management, including river basin management mechanisms, have not been widely and in-depth implementation, which requires more attention and effort.
4. Information management system, information, capacity assessment tools, technical officers and legal standards have not been adequately and comprehensively developed to support decision-making and development planning for resource development and management. Water efficiently and sustainably.
