(Phnom Penh): San Sang, a former member of the Sam Rainsy Party's board of directors, sees the mistakes of Sam Rainsy as having no strategic strategy at all as a major factor leading to the deterioration of the opposition and his political life. Sam Rainsy moves towards extinction.
Speaking of the lack of strategic leadership of Mr. Sam Rainsy, Mr. San Sang also recalled the event of Mr. Sam Rainsy removing the Cambodia-Vietnam border post in 2009, which led to the punishment of fleeing abroad for many years.
Regarding the removal of border markers in Koh Kban village, Samrong commune, Chantrea district, Svay Rieng province, on October 15, 2009, Mr. San Sang reminded that the main purpose of his visit to Svay Rieng province at that time was to hold a Kathin ceremony at a pagoda next to the border. There are no plans to visit the border or remove any border posts.
Suddenly, when he went down to the border pagoda, he removed the border marker. Mr. San Sang said that removing the border post was a mistake, as the president of a political party has no right to remove the border post. But even bigger, after removing and bringing those border posts to the party headquarters.
Starting from the removal of the border marker, the Svay Rieng provincial authorities filed a lawsuit, and Mr. Sam Rainsy fled abroad until July 2013, before returning to the country after making an apology to Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
