During a telephone conversation, Iranian President Raisi expressed frustration with the failure of the international community, especially the United Nations Security Council, to resolve the situation in Gaza effectively.
Raisi stressed the urgent need for joint efforts, especially in the Muslim world, to end the Gaza crisis, citing the conflict as a source of grave concern for Iran, Iraq and the Muslim community as a whole.
He also called for the strengthening of Iran-Iraq relations, citing the common cultural and historical ties between the two countries, and expressed his hope for the strengthening of bilateral cooperation in the coming months. Despite external obstacles.
