The Iraqi president also described the relationship between Baghdad and Tehran as strong and beneficial for both countries, emphasizing the Iraqi government's commitment to strengthening ties regardless of outside critics.
China says Chinese electric car companies do not rely on subsidies to gain competitive advantage
BEIJING: Chinese Commerce Minister Wang Wentao said at a roundtable discussion in Paris on Sunday that Chinese electric car companies do not rely on subsidies to gain competitive advantage. According to Reuters.
Reuters also quoted a statement from the Chinese Ministry of Commerce as saying on Monday that Wang also said that allegations by the United States and Europe about China's "overcapacity" did not exist. No basis.
"China's electric vehicle companies rely on continuous technological innovation, excellent production systems and supply chains, and full market competition for rapid development, without relying on subsidies to achieve," said Wang. "No competitive advantage."
"Allegations by the United States, Europe and other countries about 'overcapacity' are baseless," he added.
KUALA LUMPUR: Malaysia has ordered US tech giant Meta and China's TikTok to unveil a plan to combat malicious content on the Internet after the country reported a sharp rise, Malaysian authorities said on Tuesday. Extremely dangerous content on social media.
While they did not cite any examples of reported cases, authorities said they were particularly concerned about racial, religious and royal messages posted.
The two tech companies attended a meeting chaired by Malaysian Telecommunications Minister Fahmi Fadzil on Monday, and the company was told to step up its censorship efforts, including removing any posts related to scams and scams. Illegal gambling.
"TikTok and Meta are required to provide improvement plans and strategies, along with extensive details as agreed at the meeting," the statement said.
There is no time limit on submitting the plan or there is a penalty if the company does not comply. According to the AFP news agency.
