(Phnom Penh): A spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court said that on April 1, 2024, the specialized forces of the Anti-Drug Department of the National Police General Commission cracked down on drug cases at Tang Houy. KTV Club is located at # 67, Street 103, Village 08, Sangkat Boeung Trabek, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
As a result, the police arrested 12 Chinese, 6 Vietnamese and 1 Cambodian suspects and found 4,765.25 grams of HDNA, 1,663.32 grams of ketamine and dried plants. 162.94 grams and 62.39 grams of ambiguous substances, as well as some evidence of suspicion involved in money laundering.
After completing this operation, the police will build a case and send the suspect to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. As for the parties involved in the above drug case, the authorities have been investigating and sending it to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for action in accordance with the procedure.
After receiving and examining the case, the prosecution decided to charge the suspects and their accomplices with "trafficking, storing, managing, facilitating the use and illegal use of drugs and money laundering" as a criminal offense and shall be punished. According to the provisions of Article 40, Article 42, Article 54, Article 45 and Article 48 of the Law on Drug Control and Article 38 of the Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing.
