General knowledge: How many muscles do we have in the human body?
(Phnom Penh): According to the research of scientists in the human body, we have a total of 639 muscles.
Muscles have many functions, from pumping blood and assisting movement to lifting weights or giving birth. Muscles work by contracting or resting to move. This movement can be voluntary (meaning the movement is made consciously) or done without our understanding (involuntarily).
The glucose from the carbohydrates in our diet stimulates our muscles. To function properly, muscle tissue also needs special minerals, electrolytes, and other nutrients such as calcium, magnesium, potassium, and sodium.
