He added that if we plan according to the memories we remember once or twice a year without a long-term direction, we will be busy and human resources can not guarantee the same. It is important and important to organize the collection and analysis of data clearly.
His Excellency Hun Manet emphasized that the work of the people and development is like a body to the whole people, and in this sense, comprehensive planning is in response to the social needs that require the necessary data. To ensure efficiency as well.
The President's speech was made at the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work in 2023 and raise the direction for 2024 of the Ministry of Planning on the morning of April 9, 2024.
On that occasion, the President said, "Regarding the National School of Planning and Status, I request the Ministry of Planning to discuss with the Ministry of Economy and Finance and relevant ministries to turn the National School of Planning and Statistics into a public administrative institution to strengthen and expand the scope of its role. "And the task to be more progressive and effective in training and training courses for civil servants and subordinates as managers and leaders."
He said that in order to support the quality of education and training, the National School of Planning and Statistics must improve its capacity, both in terms of teachers and institutional capacity, as a basis for education and training.
Hun Manet stated that the National School of Planning and Statistics is an important human resource training center in the field of planning, statistics and demographics in line with the Royal Government's policy on human capital development.
