The Ministry of Planning held a meeting to review the work of 2023 and set the work direction for 2024 on April 8, 2024 under the chairmanship of Mr. Bin Trachhay, Minister of Planning. The conference reviewed the work achieved in 2023 and also raised some challenges to be improved in 2024.
Mr. Bin Trachhay highlighted that in 2023, the Ministry has achieved a lot of work under the leadership of Mr. Chhay Thorn and officials at all levels of the Ministry.
The Minister highlighted that 2023 is the end year of the Royal Government of the sixth mandate and the beginning of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate, which emerged from the July 23, 2023 general election. The Royal Government in the seventh mandate has launched the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy, with the motto of employment growth, equity, efficiency and sustainability, focusing on key priorities: people, roads, water, electricity and digital technology.
The Minister continued that the leaders and civil servants at all levels of the Ministry of Planning have been continuing their efforts to carry out their duties consistently and have achieved many proud achievements. The purpose of the two-day conference is to review the work achievements of 2023, challenges and work direction 2024 of the Ministry of Planning to strengthen the capacity and increase the efficiency of institutions and civil servants at all levels.
The following are the achievements of the Ministry of Planning in 2023:
Global Sustainable Development Goals are localized in the Cambodian context as a framework for the 2016-2030 Cambodia Sustainable Development Goals. This framework is monitored and evaluated for the results achieved through two (two) voluntary national inspection reports in 2019 and 2023.
Population and Development: The General Secretariat of Population and Development is responsible for the implementation of Population and Development, which includes national policy, population, outreach, training, community development, research and development, And cooperation work related to population and development.
1. The General Secretariat of Population and Development shall prepare, disseminate and monitor the implementation of the National Population Policy and update the National Population Policy. The National Population Policy 2016-2030 is a long-term and multi-sectoral policy document that addresses key issues of the population, people-to-people relations and development, and policy measures to address population issues. And is happening.
The national policy focuses on promoting the development of human capital and greater investment in education and health, with a focus on youth.
2: The General Secretariat of Population and Development trains human resources annually to the Internal Secretariat and the officials of the Capital and Provincial Planning Department, especially the Office of Population and Development in order to improve the knowledge and skills in demographics and population policy. .
5: Organizing the World People's Day and other forums related to population and development to reflect the Royal Government's efforts to take into account the living conditions of the people and to consider the rights and People's choice, especially women and girls.
+ Administration and General Affairs: In the context of public administration reform and public financial reform, the Ministry of Planning has implemented and coordinated the following important tasks:
1: Reform and capacity building of institutions and civil servants. 2: Management of the framework and professional development of civil servants. 3: Implementation of the national program for public administration reform. 4. Implementation of public financial management reform program. 5. International cooperation.
Currently, the National School of Planning and Statistics is training a total of 583 students and civil servants (132 females and 451 males), of which 452 are civil servants studying for a bachelor's and master's degree in planning. Development of implementation statistics, demographics and monitoring and evaluation. The National School of Planning and Statistics has also been mobilizing research and development projects.
+ Capital-Provincial Planning, Statistics and Population: The Capital-Provincial Planning Department works on behalf of the Ministry of Planning at the sub-national level and acts as a staff for the Capital-Provincial Board of Governors, actively contributing to the implementation of the Royal Decentralization and Deconcentration Policy. Government at the capital and provincial levels on the following main tasks:
Minister of Health urges all subordinates to perform their duties without delay and responsibility in their duties
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, requested the leaders in the units under the supervision to implement and plan for the development of the health sector based on the principle of not delay, do not procrastinate, do not listen to false rumors and be brave and take responsibility Be in its duty.
The statement was made by the Minister on the occasion of chairing the first leadership meeting in April to review the work progress and work direction.
The Minister also mentioned the continued dissemination of educational messages, health education videos more and more comprehensive and up-to-date, such as continuing to remind the message of low fat, low sugar, low salt for good health, longevity, as well as messages about preventive measures. And protect health in case of global warming, infectious diseases and so on.
The Minister praised the leaders and health officials in the first three months of 2024 for their dedication to work responsibly and achieve many good results. The efforts of the leadership, especially health officials at all levels.
At the same time, the Minister urged the leaders and officials in all health units to continue to work together in solidarity to carry out their work properly, based on the principles of action, problem solving, proactive response and innovation.
Finally, the Minister sent a message to visit all health officials, especially in the capital-province through the director of the capital-provincial health department and wish on the occasion of the Khmer New Year. In the coming 2568, I wish you good health and success in all your work.
It should be noted that the meeting was organized through the Hybrid system, which was directly attended by the Ministry of Health, including the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Advisor to the Director General of the Department, Head of the Central Unit of the Ministry of Health and Director of the Capital-Provincial Health Department. Conference video system. Wat Toul Veng Road in Sangkat Roleap, Pursat City will be built as a DBST paved road in 2024
(Pursat): Residents of Wat Toul Veng Road in Sangkat Roleap, Pursat City, Pursat Province expressed their pride and happiness after receiving the news that this road was provided by the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly. Promote the construction of a two-story DBST paved road in 2024.
This is according to the note of Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development on April 1, 2024 on the progress report on the implementation of the Rural Road Connection Improvement Project (RRCIP) for March 2024.
It should be informed that the people have complained and repeatedly mentioned about this red gravel road, which was promised by the former Governor of Pursat Province, Mr. Mao Thunin, who promised to build it into a 9.7 km DBST rubber road. Meters from the gate of Tuol Veng pagoda in front of the house of Mr. Suy Sem, former Minister of Mines and Energy to the letter T, the rubber road is flat.
This road has been waiting for many years for people to become a rubber road, but only repaired and widened the road in early 2023 and was repeatedly damaged by floods. Broken and due to transport of red soil and stones, no maintenance.
The report also states that the project to improve rural road connections has been implemented in four target provinces, including Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey, for a period of six years from 2023 to 2028 with a total budget. US $ 167,000,000 funded by the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) to upgrade 529.70 km of rural roads to double-deck paved roads (DBST).
The Rural Road Connection Improvement Project has been implemented as planned. Currently, the project is recruiting technical consultants for the study, design and monitoring of project implementation, achieved about 72.00% by March. 2024 and the overall progress will reach 9.02%.
Three communities in Prasat Balang and Kampong Svay districts are benefiting from climate resilience projects such as ponds and wells
(Kampong Thom): The Climate Change Working Group of the Ministry of Rural Development, in collaboration with the Ministry of Environment and development partners, has developed a climate resilience project for rural water supply infrastructure in Cambodia, with financial support as a grant from the Alliance Program. Cambodia Climate Change Phase III (CCCA3) in Kampong Svay and Prasat Balang districts, Kampong Thom province.
Through this project, thousands of people in the communities of Prasat Balang and Kampong Svay districts in Kampong Thom province have benefited directly from the community's use of daily livelihoods as well as the irrigation of crops.
Mr. Kim Chhay Na, Greenhouse Gas Fiscal Officer of the Cambodian Climate Change Alliance Program of the Ministry of Environment, Phase 3, confirmed the project on building climate resilience for rural water supply infrastructure in Cambodia started on October 1, 2020 and Completed the construction of rural water supply physical infrastructure by March 31, 2024.
According to the project official, the project has built rural water supply physical infrastructure, has formed six water user groups with 680 members (50% women) to manage and maintain the water supply infrastructure.
The main achievements under the implementation of the project are: drilling wells equipped with automatic pump motor using solar and water tank capacity of 3 liters, 48 meters deep in Sre village, Sala Visay commune, Prasat Balong district, 50 meters deep in Chamnar village, Sala Visay commune, Prasat Balong district, a well with a depth of 47 meters in Dang Antak village, Sala Visay commune, Prasat Balong district.
For community ponds, there are 3 pumps and filtration systems with ponds 100 meters long, 50 meters wide and 4 meters deep (pond size 20,000 cubic meters) in Andas village, Sala Visay commune, Prasat Balong district. The pond is 100 meters long, 50 meters wide and 4 meters deep (15,000 cubic meters in Sleng Khpos village, Sankor commune, Kampong Svay district. The pond is 50 meters long, 35 meters wide and 4 meters deep in Lvea Chom village, Trapeang Russey commune, district). Kampong Svay.
For Mr. Theng Them, chief of Andas village, Sala Visay commune, said that the changing weather has caused the water source to disappear from day to day, making it difficult for people to use water. The digging of ponds under this project has made it easier for the people in the community to get water for the dry and rainy seasons.
The climate resilience project was implemented 100 percent successfully, including digging ponds and wells for people in three communities in Prasat Balong and Kampong Svay districts, Kampong Thom province. The project provides water sources for people to use in the community for their daily lives as well as irrigating their agricultural crops.
