(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, on April 9, 2024, donated Techo Sen Russey Fresh Milk to orphans and the disabled at the National Infant and Child Center of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation. The traditional Khmer New Year is coming soon.
Borey Infant and Child National is raising and caring for orphans and the disabled, all of whom are more than 100 people with autism. Established in 1980, the National Baby and Child Borey is now under the control of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, and it operates with the help of the Royal Government of Cambodia and philanthropists.
During the distribution of fresh milk, Dr. Sok Touch was shocked to see the situation of orphans and disabled people, but he also claimed that he was happy when he celebrated and saw a beautiful smile. From their hearts, expressing gratitude, though unable to speak out.
"I brought 200 liters of Techo Sen Russey Trip fresh milk to 177 children at the orphanage, some of them orphans and some of them with disabilities," he said. Others are born with the loss of a parent or being abandoned at an early age. "I was shocked to see the situation of the children, but also happy to see the smiles of the children."
