Battambang Provincial Administration Delivers Donations to Forces Standing along the Cambodian-Thai Border in Battambang Province
(Battambang): The Battambang Provincial Administration led by Mr. Uy Ry, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Sok Lou, Provincial Governor, as well as Provincial Councilors, Deputy Provincial Governors, Administrative Directors, Chairmen and Deputy Heads of Departments around Units and Civil Servants on April 8. In 2024, he visited the troops stationed along the Cambodian-Thai border in 4 districts in Battambang province on the occasion of the traditional New Year.
Mr. Sok Loo said that during the visit, he visited the forces stationed along the Cambodian-Thai border in four districts, including:
The first venue was at the 52nd Infantry Brigade Command, Plou Meas Village, Rattanak Mondul District. 502 Samlot District * Land Border Police Battalion No. 823, Samlot District
The second location is at the 53rd Infantry Brigade Command in Kamprang Village, Kamrieng District, Battambang Province, with the participation of: * 53rd Infantry Brigade, Kamrieng District * 819th Border Police Battalion, Kamrieng District * Police Battalion Land Border Protection No. 817, Sampov Loun District
