According to the district governor, Preah Ream Rainsy pagoda has a long history, starting from 1910, and many pagodas were involved in the construction of each stage until 1975-1979. The Khmer Rouge cleared, destroyed, decapitated monks, and brutally tortured them.
The pagoda here was rebuilt after January 7, 1979 under the leadership of the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia and the Cambodian People's Party. At that time, the people cleaned the pagoda together and the Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda participated in the festival to restore and rebuild the achievements in the pagoda.
It was not until 2009 that construction of the new church began. The temple in Wat Preah Ream Rainsy was formed due to the cooperation and support of local authorities at all levels and the Buddhists have come together as a driving force to make the pagoda grow as it is today. According to the report, the construction of the church cost about $ 220,686.
