Prime Minister Hun Manet's Cabinet Reveals Results of Meeting between Samdech and the Australian Ambassador
Justin Kevin White has resigned as Ambassador to Cambodia, and this afternoon's meeting with the President is a farewell.
During the farewell meeting, Mr. Justin Kevin White thanked Mr. Hun Manet for taking the time to allow him and his colleagues to pay a courtesy call and say goodbye. The outgoing Ambassador praised the good relations between Australia and Cambodia and expressed his gratitude for the support and cooperation of the Cambodian Ministries and Institutions in strengthening ties and cooperation between the two countries. A while ago.
The Ambassador also briefed the President on the progress of cooperation that the Prime Minister and the Prime Minister of Australia recently discussed in Australia. At the same time, the Ambassador informed the President about the continued support for cooperation in the field of education by continuing to provide additional scholarships to Cambodian students and the linkages and cooperation between Australian universities and Cambodian universities. .
He also reaffirmed the two countries' commitment to continuing cooperation in a number of priority areas, including agriculture, investment, trade, infrastructure, green energy and defense and security.
The Prime Minister praised the diplomatic mission of Justin Kevin White and expressed satisfaction over the progress of cooperation that he and the Prime Minister of Australia have discussed in the past.
He thanked Australia for its support for priority areas and for cooperation. Regarding investment and trade, the President announced efforts to promote the connection between the private sector and the private sector, and was confident that the relationship between the two countries would be better for the mutual benefit of the people.
Regarding the infrastructure and green energy sector, Samdech Dhipaty highlighted the Royal Government's efforts to promote the construction of infrastructure and the development of green energy by promoting the participation of the private sector in the development and investment in these sectors.
Within the framework of the defense and security sector, Samdech Dipdey reaffirmed the continuation of the Cambodia-Australia cooperation in the field of defense and security through the promotion of training and capacity building.
The Prime Minister and the Ambassador also exchanged views on cooperation between the two countries in contributing to the maintenance of regional and international peace and prosperity in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks. Samdech Techo Hun Sen sends a message of thanks to the Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference for congratulating him on his election as President of the Senate.
