Phnom Penh Capital Hall Disseminates the Results of the Workshop on "Information and Public Opinion"
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of April 8, 2024, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration held a meeting to disseminate the results of the workshop on "Information and Public Opinion" for the Phnom Penh Capital Administration on the morning of April 8, 2024.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor, and Mr. Khuong Sreng, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, with the participation of Phnom Penh Municipal Administration, Phnom Penh Police, Khan officials and departments around the Capital Hall.
Mr. Keut Chhe said that in the context of globalization and digital evolution, the use of social media and social media is important because it is an effective means of communication between citizens and the authorities, and that people can raise their requests. Blessings and challenges in daily life for the authorities to take action.
In addition to the easy access to information from the people, the sub-national administration in general and the Phnom Penh Capital Administration and the relevant units face challenges due to the fact that some information is not well-founded and some information is not. False information that makes it difficult for information officers to review and report to management for review and resolution.
According to Mr. Keut Chhe, starting from all the above issues, it is required that the information officers of the Capital, Khan, Sangkat and Departments and Units are competent enough to analyze, analyze and verify that information with their sources and networks. To ensure that the information is accurate, avoid information that causes social unrest, political incitement, which wastes time studying and researching information sources.
"Information is important because we all need to know that the information around us is what we need," says Keut Chhe. He said that as information technology becomes more sophisticated, anti-corruption groups use social media to spread false and fake information to attack or demean the government, contrary to reality.
Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor, instructed the Information Officer to prevent fake news, attack and disseminate what we have developed, which we have done, and set up a group channel to easily monitor and manage the information in a timely manner and respond quickly.
"If we do not lead the public opinion, we will only follow their advice, we will only interpret and respond," he said. "As a journalist, you have to be both pre-reaction and response, including bragging, to control public opinion."
