According to Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), the weather in the dry season of 2024 is in the El Nino phenomenon, which since the beginning of April, the temperature has risen sharply, causing the consumption of electricity from the supply system of EDC by about 30 % Compared to last year.
To meet this rapidly increasing demand for electricity, Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) needs to generate electricity from high-cost fuel plants. Therefore, in order to help save money and reduce the cost of using high-cost electricity in the short term, leave this budget to serve something useful, EDC asks all electricity users to participate as follows:
1: Inspect and maintain all electrical equipment in accordance with the technical specifications, including the cooling equipment to clean and control the gas system, etc.
2: Turn off / disconnect electrical equipment, especially reduce the use of air conditioning as much as possible in case of unnecessary
3: Reduce the door often open for a long time to the room or refrigerator that cool the air.
4: Choose equipment that is highly efficient, uses less electricity.
Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) stated that "saving your electricity in the above way not only reduces the cost of paying for your own electricity, but also contributes to reducing EDC's production costs." "High cost energy, in particular, avoids a lack of supply sources in the event of a large-scale power outage that could eventually occur in such hot and humid conditions."
