Ministry of Health introduces 14 points to people to protect and maintain health during hot weather
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health said that the situation of climate change is causing hot weather in Cambodia as well as many countries that can make everyone sick from heat, especially people at risk. High are the elderly, infants, children, pregnant women, outdoor workers, athletes, people with weakened immune systems and people with chronic diseases.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Health, obtained by Fresh News on April 7, 2024, said that when the weather is hot, it can cause some symptoms such as abnormal sweating, fatigue, cramps. Headache, nausea, vomiting, dizziness, fainting, fast and weak pulse and stroke.
Therefore, the Ministry of Health calls on all people to pay attention to health care and advise to jointly implement 14 rules to prevent serious accidents during hot weather, including:
1: Drink plenty of water and often more than 2 liters per day, even if not thirsty.
2. Prevent diarrhea and other diseases that cause dehydration by maintaining good hygiene, food hygiene and drinking boiled or distilled water.
3. Avoid alcohol, coffee, tea, beverages that contain caffeine, sugar, salt because it causes dehydration.
4: Wear clothing that protects against heat and sunburn, such as loose-fitting, light-colored clothing, wear a hat with large brims, or use an umbrella as a sunscreen and change clothing if it is too wet.
5: Avoid dressing your baby or toddler with too thick clothing or wrapping them in a blanket that heats up further.
6: Avoid being in direct sunlight for too long by seeking shade or using sunscreen.
8: If you go out, schedule an activity for the morning if possible or in the evening when the temperature drops. Avoid activities at noon or when the sun is hot. Gradually adapt to hot weather conditions.
9. Use a damp towel to wipe your face in the shade or place it around your neck if it feels too hot. Take cold showers or plain water often, but avoid making drastic temperature changes. Avoid taking a cold shower immediately after returning from a hot spot, which can cause a sudden drop in temperature and May be especially dangerous for the elderly or children.
10: Know your limits and your own ability to work safely in the heat that can withstand and work slowly, do not rush.
11. Take time to relax and take shelter in a cool, shady place or stay indoors as much as possible, unless you are sure that your body can withstand a certain amount of heat.
12: Limit the use of stoves and ovens because it will make you and your home warmer.
13. Family members should be diligent in monitoring and monitoring the vulnerable to hot weather, including the elderly over 60 years old, the sick, children under 2 years old, the chronically ill and the sick. Mind because they may need help at least twice a day during hot weather. Do not leave them unattended.
14: If you have symptoms such as dizziness, nausea or vomiting, headache, muscle cramps (cramps), which are the first signs of the effects of heat, move to a cool place and rest for a few minutes and drink cold drinks slowly, do not continue. Because it can lead to high risk. Absolutely avoid crowds around people with health problems. Seek immediate medical attention at a health center or hospital near your home if you do not feel better.
