On the other hand, to claim that if Cambodians use the word "sangkran" as a means of helping to spread Songkran in Thailand, it does not seem reasonable at all. Because researchers, whether national or foreign, often delve into the very roots of the culture of each nation. Therefore, the idea of wanting to get rid of this Sanskrit word is not equal to the rejection of the cultural heritage of its ancestors that has existed for thousands of years or something?
The word "sangkran" in Sanskrit speaks astronomically, the orbit of the sun for one round of the earth or one cycle of the universe is one year. Because in order to count the time, they are divided into zodiac signs according to the journey of the sun into 12 flat zodiac signs or flat planets equal to 1 year. And the sun revolves around 12 flats for one round, the old year is over, the new year is called the new "sangkant".
Among them are Sanskrit, then Pali, an ancient language and a language that exalts the ancient nobility from Indian civilization, not English, French, which is a newly developed language, becoming the language of our modern civilization. . Because culture is something that has been around for a long time.
Therefore, according to tradition, before the New Year, they decorate their houses, clean the courtyards of pagodas, roads, shrines, resorts, build temples, and prepare new clothes for their parents, grandparents, and elders to pay tribute to their ancestors. Because it is believed that it is an opportunity to clear up the evils of the old year in order to accept the good things that are good with the New Year angels in happiness and bliss in peace.
During the three days of the traditional Khmer New Year, people, young and old, young and old, gather to play various popular games, including throwing games, throwing games, hiding towels, dancing and popular Khmer traditional games. Many more full of fun and unity.
Senior official of the Ministry of Culture: Bokator is performed in "Hun Sen High School, Kampong Tralach Sankrant"
(Phnom Penh): Bokator martial arts, which was registered as a UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity at the end of 2022, was performed at "Hun Sen High School, Kampong Tralach Sankranti" or Sankrant program at Hun Sen High School, Kampong Tralach.
The Sankranti program at Hun Sen High School in Kampong Tralach was officially opened on Saturday afternoon, April 6, 2024, under the chairmanship of Dr. He Virak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Kampong Tralach District. From the team, teachers, students.
According to a senior official of the Ministry of Culture, "Hun Sen High School, Kampong Tralach Sankranti" also has a popular game of throwing, throwing leaves, hiding towels and traditional dances.
This Sankranti program went smoothly with a happy Khmer folk game with a fresh smile and a traditional Khmer dance competition, which is to maintain, promote and promote the will of the younger generation to know and understand. The priceless heritage of Khmer ancestors.
According to the elder Krama Meas San Kim Sean, to learn bokator for the Khmer ancestors from the beginning, learn both "Human Martial Arts" and "Divine Martial Arts". He added that Jayavarman VII, when he went to war, he used a great strategy, he used both martial arts and martial arts. Tactics refer to Balikatha. Martial arts refers to fighting with weapons. Art refers to tricks, temptations, and attacks.
Bokator is a traditional Khmer martial art that has been deeply rooted in Cambodian society for centuries and continues to survive in Cambodian society to this day. The carvings on the walls of Angkorian temples are clear evidence of this martial art practice. The training of bokator from generation to generation is to strengthen the wisdom and ability to defend themselves from wild animals and enemies, as well as to protect the society and the motherland.
According to the book "San Kimsan Bokator", bokator is divided into 12 gates, the first to the eighth gate uses physical fitness, and the ninth to twelfth gate uses weapons, including dangerous and non-dangerous weapons. Dangerous weapons include knives, swords, spears, arrows and knives. Non-hazardous weapons include rice husks, short sticks, long sticks, shields and shower sticks.
In addition, bokator can also use the krama as a weapon. In general, this position is flexible, can defend itself against attacks from all eight directions, and everything around it can be used as a weapon.
Father and son were electrocuted and died in O'Kanthor Sangkat, Stung Sen City
(Kampong Thom): On the morning of April 7, 2024, an electric shock caused the death of two people, a father and a son, at 7:00 am in O'Kanthor Cheung village, Sangkat O'Kanthor, Stung Sen city, Kampong Thom province.
According to Mr. Chiv Kim Un, Chief of O'Kanthor Commune, the case of electric shock was named Yun Yat, male, 75 years old, father and Yat Yorn, male, 41 years old, son. The family cooperated with the monks to give birth to the seven relatives, which took place every year. Unfortunately, the father and son inadvertently changed the position of the microphone, took the microphone cable, raised the microphone and touched the power cord, causing the electric shock to die on the spot.
After the authorities performed the merits of the two bodies, the father and son actually died due to the electric shock, and the authorities handed over the two bodies to the relatives for a Buddhist ceremony.
At the same time, Mr. O'Kanthor Sangkat Chief called on people to be careful like this case and be careful of fire as well.
