(Phnom Penh): In addition to the traditional gatherings of the Royal Government, as well as the authorities at all levels for the people and foreign tourists, the New Year is also an opportunity that we see the attention of the Royal Government to the people, civil servants and the armed forces of all kinds.
First, hundreds of public buses have been set up to transport people from Phnom Penh to their hometowns and from their hometowns to Phnom Penh for free. In addition to providing a lot of benefits to citizens and workers, they do not have to pay for travel, the bus also provides comfortable travel and can reduce road accidents.
Second, on the occasion of the New Year, the Royal Government has donated 50,000 Riels to all types of civil servants and the Armed Forces, as well as sub-national officials to retirees and people with disabilities. This support confirms the Royal Government's concern for those who work hard to serve the nation and dedicate themselves to the cause of the nation, the motherland and the people.
Fourth, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, Head of the Royal Government, has just issued a sub-decree on the increase of salaries for civil servants, the Armed Forces and the monthly allowance for sub-national authorities. This is a regular effort of the Royal Government to improve the lives of all those who work for the nation.
Fifth, the six priority policy programs announced at the end of August 2023 by the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly focus on improving the lives of people, especially poor and vulnerable families. . This is a policy to help people to have a more prosperous life.
Sixth, in the Pentagon Strategy, the most important goal of the Royal Government led by Samdech Hun Sen is to achieve the vision of Cambodia 2050 to become a high-income country, a country with a strong economy, high prestige, people have a prosperous life. Good knowledge and morals, live in a green environment, a good environment, pure and receive all the protection from society.
All in all, civil servants and the armed forces, as well as the general population, are warm, hopeful and proud under the leadership of the Royal Government of the Cambodian People's Party.
More than 1 million saplings were planted in nursery schools in the capitals and provinces for distribution to people to plant in the rainy season
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has planted more than 1 million saplings in the nursery grounds of the provincial and municipal Departments of Environment, and one part was a generous gift from Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, for a campaign to plant at least one tree. Millions of trees every year from the rainy season of 2024 onwards. This was confirmed by Mr. Khvay Atiya, a spokesman for the Ministry of Environment.
In fact, as of April 5, 2024, the Ministry of Environment has planted a total of 642310 saplings and distributed 20,028 saplings to people to plant at home, school, pagoda, community. At the same time, Dr. Eang Sophalleth donated more than 300,000 palm seedlings in this campaign.
Through the October 10, 2023 campaign, the Minister of Environment urged people to plant trees, rehabilitate forests and protect forests and the natural environment to increase forest cover and sell carbon to increase income in the community. .
Dr. Eang Sophalleth stated that Cambodia's green strategy is designed in accordance with the Environmental Chart Strategy set out in accordance with the Pentagon Strategy Phase 1 of the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature under the wise leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Towards achieving the vision of increasing forest cover by 60% by 2050.
