Phnom Penh Municipal Police spokesman Sam Vichheka confirmed that the arrest of Kim Hong, the second deputy chief of Orussey IV commune, was carried out on a warrant issued by the prosecutor's office for "requesting documents." By dishonesty ”(Registration on the list of reserve candidates for Khan 7 Makara Council for the Khmer Will Party without the permission of the person concerned) took place in Phnom Penh on March 13, 2024.
Authorities are currently building a case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action.
Negotiators are expected to meet again in Cairo as the Israeli-Hamas war draws to a close.
(Gaza) - US and Israeli negotiators are expected to be present in Cairo, Egypt, this weekend to try to push for a new ceasefire in exchange for the release of hostages in the Israeli-Israeli war. Hamas in the Gaza Strip, which has lasted for almost half a year. This was released by the AFP news agency on Saturday, April 6, 2024.
Ahead of the meeting, US President Joe Biden sent a letter to the leaders of Egypt and Qatar urging them to put pressure on Hamas to accept a ceasefire. The United States, Qatar and Egypt have been seeking a ceasefire and the release of hostages for months, but have not achieved much since a week-long ceasefire in November 2023.
Israel and Hamas have blamed and blamed each other for the lack of progress in the talks, with Hamas still calling on Israel to withdraw its troops from Gaza.
