(Phnom Penh): A person named Keut Saray was arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police on April 6, 2024 after this person had bad intentions to incite people in Preah Vihear province for fear of profiteering. Politics creates the misconception that the authorities are oppressing the people.
In addition to malicious intent to disrupt the peace, this individual and his party also fabricated false information and gave interviews to foreign media in an attempt to incite unrest in connection with a land case in Preah Vihear province. Therefore, in order to prevent riots on the occasion of the Khmer New Year, the court decided to issue an arrest warrant for this person in order to prevent instability and disturb the people and the authorities.
Speaking to Fresh News, Colonel Sam Vichheka, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, said that the arrest of Keut Saray was made on a warrant issued by Deputy Prosecutor Seng Heang of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. Phnom Penh on "incitement to cause serious chaos to social security."
According to the spokesman, the man had already been arrested and jailed for "inciting serious social unrest." But this person is not consistent.
Recently, a person named Keut Saray fabricated false information related to land disputes in Preah Vihear province to give interviews to foreign media in order to incite resentment and anger the Royal Government. Especially to the international stage.
Colonel Sam Vichheka stated, "We can conclude that the name Keut Saray was really intended to incite people to anger the government, and that person even provided information to the rebel media, including VOD and RFA." "Disseminate false information and fabricate information to show abroad and punish Cambodia."
Please be informed that after the arrest, the suspect was sent to the Phnom Penh Police for further action.
