Royal Government of Cambodia paves the way for SCA to act as operator of Techo International Airport when launched
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has given the green light to SCA, which is currently operating Phnom Penh International Airport, to act as an operator of Techo International Airport at the time of its launch after the closure of Phnom Penh International Airport.
The delegation comes after the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation signed an agreement with Societe Consulate de la Europe (SCA) on the principles for restoring the financial balance of the concession agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and Societe Consulate General. La Europe on April 5, 2024.
Speaking at the signing ceremony, Dr. Mao Havannal, Minister in charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, said that after the signing of this agreement, the Royal Government will entrust SCA to act as the operator of Techo International Airport at the start of operation. At the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia will extend the time for SCA to develop and strengthen the capacity of Sihanoukville International Airport.
Please be informed that in 1995, the Royal Government of Cambodia provided investment to SCA to develop, build and manage the operation of Phnom Penh International Airport, and in 2006, the Royal Government provided investment to this French company to develop, build and manage the operation of Sihanoukville International Airport. Class 4E on an area of 682 hectares.
