Lt. Gen. Seak Socheat Meets Cambodian Workers Returning Home on New Year's Day and Facilitates Travel at Osmach International Gate
(Oddar Meanchey): On the morning of April 5, 2024, at the Osmach International Gate, Lt. Gen. Seak Socheat, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense, Chairman of the Second Group of the Commission on Government Affairs, led the members of the Commission on Affairs and related institutions to meet with Thai immigration officials. And meet and greet Cambodian workers who return home during the traditional New Year.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Seak Socheat also facilitated the entry and exit of Cambodian workers during the upcoming Khmer New Year to pay attention to coordinating and cooperating to organize order at the entrance checkpoint. Leaving the country well to avoid congestion and health problems of workers and passengers in general to them.
On that occasion, General Seak Socheat instructed Mr. Hor Chinvirayuth, Deputy Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province and other relevant institutions at the border gate to prepare a package of pure water and set up an office for the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Health Department at the Osmach International Gate to be ready for emergency treatment and facilitation. Travel in and out of the country for Cambodian workers during the upcoming National New Year.
Mr. Seak Socheat advised that in order to facilitate the entry and exit of Cambodian workers through the border gates, the governors of the three provincial governors, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey and Preah Vihear, are members of the commission to lead and implement in the spirit of Decision No. 99 USA dated 13 September 2023 of the Royal Government to effectively carry out the following tasks:
* First, the relevant authorities and institutions at all border crossings must provide services to facilitate the entry and exit of Cambodian citizens and workers during their return to Cambodia to celebrate. Celebrate the upcoming Khmer New Year.
* Second, urge the authorities at checkpoints and checkpoints to strengthen border control measures thoroughly, facilitate the entry and exit of traders and workers holding legal passports quickly. At the same time, measures must be taken to prevent entry and exit using irregular passports.
* Third: Instruct the competent authorities to stand at all border gates, to immediately stop the issuance of irregular passports, not to take unofficial fees from workers when they pass through the border gates. .
* Fourth, to close all illegal corridors within its jurisdiction, and to take strict legal action to crack down on air activities and accomplices who lure people to cross the border illegally in all forms. .
* Fifth: Collect information related to the migration of workers through the border gates, manage the flow of workers in and out of the border and try to solve the challenges that arise for them.
* 6: Instruct the municipal administration to conduct regular and widespread dissemination to the people in its jurisdiction about providing border card services to them without discrimination and without informal fees, and to disseminate to them He understands the procedures for crossing the border when traveling in and out of the border must have legal documents.
* Seventh: To set up a leadership mechanism to monitor the implementation of the measures set out and to have officials in charge of monitoring the work clearly. There must be a practical inspection program to carry out the duties and responsibilities of border gate officials to remind, encourage, improve and resolve irregularities that occur according to the work method, mirroring, bathing, scrubbing, treatment and surgery.
* 8th: To make monthly, quarterly, semi-annual and annual reports on the situation and resolving the problem of entry and exit of Cambodian workers at the border to the second working group, the Commission on Affairs and must report immediately to have timely guidance and guidance in Necessary cases. Lt. Gen. Chhuon Thavorin visits and talks with troops stationed at Kampong Chhnang Air Force Base before the New Year.
