(Phnom Penh): Railways are a means of transporting both passengers and valuable goods in the transportation system. Cambodia also has ambitions to improve its railway system, especially high-speed rail.
Regarding the railway development project in Cambodia, Mr. Peng Po, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that Cambodia has already studied and prepared a plan. The railway development plan in Cambodia is divided into two phases: medium phase from 2023 to 2027 and long term from 2028 to 2033.
According to Mr. Peng Po Na, in the medium term, Cambodia has three railway development projects, including: Transforming the current two lines (Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville, Phnom Penh-Poipet) into high-speed rail. More than now, the second and third projects are to build a railway connecting Phnom Penh to Techo International Airport and connecting Siem Reap International Airport to Siem Reap City.
In particular, for the long term from 2028 to 2033, Cambodia has five railway development projects, including: the construction of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville and Phnom Penh-Poipet high-speed railways, the construction of the Phnom Penh-Bavet expressway to the Vietnamese border, Phnom Penh to Poipet via Kampong Thom and Siem Reap.
In addition to the four high-speed rail projects to Cambodia, the project will also build a railway system in Phnom Penh to facilitate the growing traffic of the people.
