(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Seak Socheat, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense, Chairman of the Second Working Group of the Commission on Addressing the Migration of Cambodian Workers at the Cambodian Border, held a meeting on the morning of April 4, 2024 to facilitate the transit of People on the occasion of the upcoming New Year.
The meeting was held at the Poipet International Gate, which was composed of the Deputy Chairman of the Working Group on Border Governance in Banteay Meanchey Province and relevant authorities.
Mr. Seak Socheat set out measures for the Deputy Chairman and members of the Second Working Group to remind the competent authorities to increase the sense of responsibility in managing and facilitating Cambodian workers who cross the border into Cambodia during the festival. In the coming New Year, we will prepare the medical staff at the gate to provide emergency assistance to the people if necessary.
* Third: Instruct the competent authorities to stand at all border gates to immediately stop issuing irregular passports and not to take unofficial fees from workers when they pass through the border gates. .
* 8th: To make monthly, quarterly, semi-annual and annual reports on the situation and resolving the problem of entry and exit of Cambodian workers through the border to the second working group, the Commission on Affairs and must report immediately to have timely guidance and guidance in If necessary.
The President of the National Assembly of Laos sends a congratulatory letter to Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of being elected President of the Senate for the 5th term
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Say Mony Phok Vihan, President of the National Assembly of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, sent a congratulatory message to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of his election as President of the Senate for the 5th term in the first session. The 5th Senate on April 3, 2024 under the highest presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In a message, the Speaker of the National Assembly of the Lao People's Democratic Republic stated:
On behalf of the National Assembly of the Lao People's Democratic Republic and on my own behalf, I would like to extend my sincere congratulations and congratulations to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party of the Kingdom of Cambodia for the election. President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia in the first session of the Senate of the 5th legislature on April 3, 2024.
I would like to commend Samdech, who was elected President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia, for his rich experience in leading the country. Samdech's skillful ability and the high trust of the Party, State and the Cambodian people as a whole.
I look forward to working closely with you and the senior leadership of the Cambodian Senate for further strengthening the good traditional friendship and long-term cooperation and comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership between the two parties. Both people, especially between our two legislatures.
Please take this precious opportunity to wish Samdech and the Senators of the Kingdom of Cambodia good health, prosperity and great success in all their noble duties.
With respect. ”
