(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Thailand, Mr. Srettha Thavisin, sent a congratulatory message to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of his election as the President of the Senate for the fifth term in the first session of the Senate for the fifth term on April 3, 2024 under the highest presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In a message, the Thai Prime Minister stated:
I have the honor to sincerely congratulate Samdech Techo on his election as President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Samdech's election by the Cambodian Senate reflects his confidence in his leadership and wisdom in promoting peace, stability and prosperity of the nation.
I would like to reaffirm Thailand's readiness to work closely with Samdech in his new position. Under the leadership of Samdech, as President of the Senate, I am very confident that the bilateral ties between Thailand and Cambodia will continue to grow and develop.
On behalf of the people of the Kingdom of Thailand, I would like to extend my best wishes to Samdech Techo, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany and the people of the Kingdom of Cambodia, wishing them happiness, prosperity and good health forever.
