Nearly 200 Cambodian-Thai hybrid products on display for 3 days at Koh Pich Gallery, Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): High quality international goods of Cambodia and Thailand 2024 will be brought to the exhibition for 3 days from 05 to 7 April 2024 at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center, Phnom Penh, a trade fair event. The annual large-scale international event aims to promote trade and investment activities in Cambodia, especially to promote trade ties between Cambodia and Thailand.
Cambodia and Thailand Trade and Consumer Fair, which will be open to the public free of charge every day from 9am to 9pm. While there are 160 booths of used products in the exhibition, 80 booths of Cambodian products and 80 booths of Thai products.
The booths exhibited by Cambodian enterprises participating in the IBB are from: Food & Beverage Companies, Franchise Companies, Distributors of Agricultural Products, Hotels and Resorts, Telecommunications and Internet Service Providers, Banks and Microfinance Institutions, Insurance Companies Food and payment companies, car dealers, real estate developers.
According to the organizers of the exhibition, the exhibition is mostly goods that help small and medium enterprises (SMEs) also have Khmer and Thai cuisine for visitors to taste the work. Both ends are also ethnic.
As planned, the 2024 International High-Quality Commodity Fair of Cambodia and Thailand will be held twice a year, with the aim of inviting manufacturers from other countries to exhibit their products in Events as well.
Visitors to the fair will be able to purchase a variety of products with special discounts for Khmer New Year, as well as concerts, art performances, and raffle prizes.
