Official inauguration of the delta dam, ring road, Preah Vihear city and some artistic structures! Senior official of the Ministry of Economy: Preah Vihear province is highly developed, not inferior to other provinces
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Im Sethyra, Representative of the Royal Government, Representative of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, said that Preah Vihear Province has undergone significant changes and development, not inferior to other provinces and cities, but only for a few years under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen Former Prime Minister of Cambodia and will grow even more under the leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Mr. M. Setthira said that the inauguration of the Preah Vihear Delta Dam now confirms the development of the progress and progress of the Kingdom of Cambodia in general and in particular for Preah Vihear province, which is the work of the province. Construction of delta dam and ring road of Preah Vihear city.
The delta dam will not only prevent the flooding of houses in Preah Vihear city during the rainy season, but it will become a ring road with the subsequent construction of infrastructure such as concrete, corrugated iron, drainage, and door construction. Water. He said that the dam was built to serve the people of Preah Vihear, especially to avoid flooding in the city of about 280 hectares with many houses.
Mr. Kim Rithy expressed his deep gratitude to Mr. Im Sethyra and the Ministry's leadership for allocating funds for the construction of this important Delta Dam project. He also commended the local authorities, specialized departments, provincial departments of public works and transportation, who worked hard to build a project, prepare a technical plan, address the impact and implement the project according to plan until it is successful, timely and quality.
(Kampong Chhnang): Teachers and students in Preah Bat Suramarit High School in Kampong Chhnang this morning, April 5, 2024, held an exhibition of student work and New Year Sankranta under the chairmanship of Mr. Yin Saven, Deputy Governor. Kampong Chhnang Province, with the cooperation of Kampong Chhnang Municipal Administration, Kampong Chhnang Municipal Office of Education, Youth and Sports and the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, together with Preah Bat Suramarit High School.
Mr. Yin Saven, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, said that the exhibition of students' work in Preah Bat Suramarit High School now shows the knowledge and skills of students, which is a measure of life skills for future students who are the successors of bamboo. Develop a national society from our elders.
At the same time, the Deputy Governor also confirmed that the word Sankrant in Sanskrit language, which is the traditional culture of Khmer ancestors, has existed since ancient times, especially with clear images on the inscriptions on the walls of Angkor Wat. This Sankranti is used in four countries: Cambodia, Thailand, Laos, and Burma, with separate cultural traditions of each nation.
Therefore, as students who are the youth, the pillars of the nation and the successors of bamboo, we must unite to preserve Sankranti, which is the tradition of our Khmer ancestors, by educating our brothers and sisters and not copying Sankranti culture. They do not play water spray and do not play powder in the Khmer New Year Sankranti. This is the additional confirmation of the Deputy Governor.
