(Phnom Penh): Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that all people should stop blaming each other regarding traditional arts and culture, but we must participate in promoting what is the value of traditional culture, art, Khmer folk games. To cultivate the spirit of young people to know and love what belongs to Cambodia.
Dr. Yong Pov's statement came after the recent singing and gesturing in a number of songs to celebrate the traditional Khmer New Year, leaving behind cultural and artistic values. Khmer, which led to a lot of debate on social media.
Dr. Yong Pov said that for the Sankranti ceremony at the Royal Academy of Cambodia to celebrate the traditional Khmer New Year, the year of Rong Chhasak. 2567 also features performances by Chinese artists to strengthen Cambodian-Chinese ties to the level of people and peoples, as announced by the two governments recently.
