(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) of Korea has decided to provide health assistance to the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to help build a Dangkor Referral Hospital to improve public health services for Cambodians, especially in Dangkor district.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that the decision to build a Dangkor Referral Hospital under the auspices of KOICA is a testament to the commitment of the Korean government and people to contribute to the development of Cambodia. Demonstrates the strengthening of solidarity ties between the two countries.
Mr. Khuong Sreng continued that the decision to choose Dangkor district to build this referral hospital was because the Phnom Penh Capital Administration saw that this location was good, there were many factories, enterprises, workers and people gathered here in 2025. A new airport near the site will also be opened, leaving the area densely populated, while Dangkor district has only one national hospital for cancer treatment.
