This activity is highly appreciated by the followers of social events, who not only followed the instructions of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, but also raised the value of Khmer culture.
This is an encouragement to the day and night efforts of the management team, teachers and students who have joined forces to maintain, preserve, develop and promote the traditions of the Khmer ancestors in the cause of good behavior. Model students and good youth in society, avoid drugs and other vices.
In addition to the art exhibition, the students also exhibited handicrafts, art objects, palm products, food stalls and souvenirs showing Cambodian art. On the important occasion of the above program, the leaders and students also organized a fundraiser for the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia to contribute to the sustainability of the hospital's operations, as well as to provide a smile to Cambodian children.
Dr. Heng Sophady stated, "We know that the Royal University of Fine Arts is a university focused on the study of arts and culture, which is the national identity, we do everything in keeping with the traditions not to leave."
According to the Rector, the event was not just for fun, but for the students to show off their work and talents that they have studied here. He added that this is also to promote the national art and culture to the public.
At the same time, Dr. Kin Phea, a social event monitor, said that for him personally, he really supported the organization of the New Year in this form. Dr. praised and highly valued the Royal University of Fine Arts, especially the Minister of Foreign Affairs, who initiated such a meaningful event.
The President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia considered that this event has really contributed significantly to the preservation, preservation, development and promotion of our Khmer traditions from our ancestors, especially as a model for our Cambodian youth.
"As we all know, the current trend of celebrating the New Year, our national tradition seems to be a bit far from the original form, which is a beautiful tradition of our Khmer ancestors left behind," he said. Come to this generation and the next. We see that the trend of celebrating singing, dancing, drinking, throwing water, flour, etc., is not a traditional form of our Khmer tradition.
