(Phnom Penh): The ASEAN-Cambodia Business Summit 2024, which ended on April 2, marked a milestone in regional economic cooperation that has brought significant progress in building resilience. New partners and strategic economic initiatives.
Organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce in collaboration with partners of the International Chamber of Commerce and International Trade Associations in Cambodia, this summit is a testament to the spirit of cooperation to promote ASEAN's economic future.
The opening ceremony of the summit began on April 2, 2024 under the high presidency of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Senior dignitaries include: Deputy Prime Minister, Ministers, Senior Government Officials and Ambassadors, as well as more than 500 business leaders from ASEAN and around the world, including CEOs of major international corporations operating in Cambodia. Attend this summit.
In his keynote address, the Prime Minister praised the remarkable development of ASEAN, which has become a dynamic economic zone since its establishment in 1967. The Prime Minister emphasized Cambodia's role as an active and close partner in the ASEAN family and reaffirmed Cambodia's commitment to contributing to the ASEAN Economic Community, which is resilient, environmentally friendly and competitive. .
The summit will also host a Cocktails Party on April 1, 2024, chaired by Cambodian Minister of Commerce Cham Nimmol, to build valuable relationships across business, government and investment.
She stressed the focus of the meeting on ASEAN economic advancement and the potential for increased regional connectivity, pushing for a commitment to sustainable and inclusive growth as Cambodia prepares to be An important gateway to the ASEAN market.
The summit explored three pillars of evolution, including:
1. Unleashing the Power of Connectivity: This section underscores the importance of promoting cross-border partnerships and joint initiatives that are important in achieving ASEAN common economic potential.
2. Cambodia is a gateway to ASEAN: The discussions shed light on Cambodia's strategic position and its growing potential as a hub for trade, investment and cooperation in ASEAN, which promotes deeper integration in the region.
3. Utilizing Technology and Digital Innovation for Environmental Growth: The Summit discussed how digital evolution and emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence (AI) can lead to business transformation, fill the digital gap, and drive entrepreneurial development. By sustainability.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN-Cambodia Business Advisory Council, highlighted the importance of the summit as Cambodia continues to participate in ASEAN economic integration.
Nararya S. Soeprapto, Deputy Secretary-General of ASEAN for Community and Corporate Affairs, summed up the outcome of the Summit with an optimistic outlook, emphasizing the spirit of cooperation that leads to discussions and potential opportunities to take advantage of the agreement. Free trade, digital transformation and a thriving green economy.
The event ended with a dinner hosted by Mr. Say Sam Al, which provided an opportunity to network further for the delegation and strengthen the common focus on strong economic cooperation in ASEAN. Open training course to share knowledge on understanding Artificial Intelligence (AI) system
