In the first quarter of this year, Cambodia approved 106 investment projects totaling 2.2 billion USD
(Phnom Penh): 106 investment projects with a total investment capital of 2.2 billion US dollars approved by the Council for the Development of Cambodia in the first quarter of 2024 can create more than 107 thousand jobs. This is according to the press release of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on January 5, 2024.
Notably, there are 73 investment projects located outside the special economic zone, including 3 production expansion projects, while 33 investment projects located outside the special economic zone, including production expansion projects. 3 projects.
Overall, in the first quarter of 2024, the approval of investment projects increased by 67 projects, while investment capital increased significantly by nearly 2 billion US dollars, equivalent to about 649% compared to the same period in 2023.
The sharp increase is due to the presence of new projects in infrastructure, industry, tourism and industrial expansion in special economic zones.
