Senate Holds the First Session of the 5th Legislature to Approve Local Regulations and Elect Members of Commissions
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of April 5, 2024, the Senate held its first session for the fifth legislature to decide on two agendas.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Prak Sokhon, Acting President of the Senate, while Samdech Techo Hun Sen was acting Acting Head of State during the King's visit to Japan.
The agenda of this morning's session is as follows: First, the approval of the rules of procedure of the Senate, and second, the election of members of the committees of the Senate.
The Senate for the fifth term has 62 members, two of whom are nominated by the King, two are nominated by the National Assembly and 58 are elected by popular vote.
