Sri Lanka sees no need for talks with India over islands entrusted to it for years
(Sri Lanka) - Sri Lanka does not see the need to open talks on a disputed island that India handed over to it 50 years ago, the Sri Lankan foreign minister has said. This is according to the release by Reuters on Thursday, April 4, 2024.
India ceded an island of the Palk Strait to Sri Lanka in 1974 and reached a convention on fishermen in 1976, but dissatisfaction with the surrender, coupled with a decline in fishery rights, prompted Controversy in the courts that has not been resolved in the last 20 years.
