Banteay Meanchey Military sends 3 suspects to court in connection with motorcycle and drug theft
* First name: Leng Saka (aka Sak), 17 years old, currently living in Kordathan village, Sangkat O'Ambel, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province * Sam Piseth, 16 years old, current residence: Khla Kon Chas village, Sangkat Kampong Chas, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province, while another member escaped.
Brigadier General Sok Leng, Commander of the Municipal Gendarmerie, said that at the time of the incident, the victim was riding a black Honda Dream motorcycle made in 2020 with license plate Banteay Meanchey 1V-2472, a taxi from the market and He left the motorcycle in front of the rented room where he was staying.
Then he ate with his wife and children and fell asleep. At 3:00 the same day, when he left the room, he suddenly lost his motorbike and came to file a complaint at the Serei Sophorn City Police Base.
After being arrested and interrogated, the suspects confessed that they were involved in a motorcycle theft and illegal drug use. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the local force of the Municipal Gendarmerie has built a case and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Lt. Col. Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of crime investigation and crackdown, said that the crackdown was also authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander and coordinated. Proceedings from Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
The three suspects have now been sent to the Provincial Court by the Criminal Office of the Provincial Gendarmerie on Thursday afternoon, April 4, 2024 to follow the procedure.
